{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T04:50:15.947Z","ordinal":37855,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-866f6614-f6b7-490f-a7ef-2eb14b13af4b","process_id":"18421","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n '60|rate|limit|per caller|per-caller|identity' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md | head -55; cat /private/tmp/dev75-rate-design-notes.md | tail -50; cat packages/calculators/src/index.ts | head -95; rg -n 'CalculatorServiceError|CapacityExceeded|TimedOut' packages/calculators/src/schemas.ts | head -22; gh run view 37414462610 --json status,conclusion,headSha,jobs"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n '60|rate|limit|per caller|per-caller|identity' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md | head -55; cat /private/tmp/dev75-rate-design-notes.md | tail -50; cat packages/calculators/src/index.ts | head -95; rg -n 'CalculatorServiceError|CapacityExceeded|TimedOut' packages/calculators/src/schemas.ts | head -22; gh run view 37414462610 --json status,conclusion,headSha,jobs"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"18:publication or provider apply. Final provider-plan approval remains separate.\n31:results while replacing the public interface deliberately.\n33:The architectural trade-off is recorded in [ADR 0001](../adr/0001-separate-website-and-api.md).\n39:- a separate website and backend API;\n60:target 2025–26. The rebuild makes these limits visible and adds no new tax tables.\n85:  -> Website HTML with browser-safe generated presentation components\n87:generated sitemap/robots/agent indexes/static Markdown/OG -> accepted catalogue assets\n91:  -> existing shared Axiom logs/metrics/traces, filtered by TaxKit identity\n98:Generated clients remain private. Preview uses its own backend. Runtime secrets\n100:application secrets retain separate ownership.\n103:need separate checks; a registered tool name does not prove that an agent can\n131:private generated client Layers. The domain/calculator/content owners keep\n134:request limits and safe measurement. No transport duplicates tax policy,\n141:native generated client private. The Website has no live rule engine, authored\n147:Context. Its explicit build/ingress route uses the native generated function\n183:uses an identity encoder and can reflect its supplied tag. Qualify a supported\n204:| Public API and remote MCP access | Agreed in Q2: anonymous access with request limits | Keep access simple and bound expensive requests | Request limits, privacy and abuse handling |\n210:| Measurement | Agreed in Q8 and expanded by Cooper's latest message | PostHog visits and calculator names; Axiom logs, traces and metrics in the existing shared datasets; no calculation details or consent dialog | Event ownership, privacy checks, identity filters and retained provider resources |\n234:operations. It does not add tax years, rates, accounts, payments or saved\n244:Add a separate MCP adapter only where its public protocol needs an owner; it\n262:| CSF-003 | Separate native backend and standard frontend | Native Alchemy API handlers keep request work and cleanup; no backend ManagedRuntime. The Website uses one server runner and one React-owned browser Atom graph. Native RPC clients use a same-stage server binding and checked public browser URL, implementing checked named operations with a complete-response deadline, revision agreement and caller cancellation. |\n264:| CSF-005 | Serve anonymous API, remote MCP and browser tools | HTTP/OpenAPI and native Effect MCP reuse checked named operations. Bound bodies, work, concurrency and request rates; return checked rate-limit/error responses. WebMCP can find, read, fill, calculate and read results through visible page commands. Feature detection keeps normal browser use working. |\n265:| CSF-006 | Publish one useful content and discovery catalogue | Review existing pages, record exact acceptance for finished content and navigation, and keep unfinished drafts out of public search. Derive SEO/AEO metadata, canonicals, sitemap, robots, structured data, search, agent indexes, processed Markdown and page OG images from the same accepted catalogue. Markdown covers public pages/reference content only; no personal report download. Website owns HTML and browser-safe compiled presentation exports; dynamic source/search/Markdown/image services belong to the backend. Generated static assets need no extra server. No raw MDX or alternate calculations. |\n267:| CSF-008 | Measure only traffic and chosen calculator usage in PostHog | Explicit pageview and successful calculator-use events pass a closed Schema allowlist after SDK enrichment. No figures, facts, result details, free text, user profiles, session recordings or automatic click capture. No consent dialog. Respect Do Not Track; proposed browser identity is memory-only. |\n268:| CSF-009 | Send useful, safe telemetry to the three shared Axiom datasets | Reference site-prod-logs/site-prod-traces/site-prod-metrics without changing their owner or retention. One owner per signal, checked TaxKit identity fields, bounded event cleanup, safe fields, correct endpoint/encoding/header and independent filtered readback. No second competing trace exporter. |\n280:Initial anonymous calculation/MCP policy is 60 work requests per minute per\n281:trusted, non-logged client rate key; 64 KiB request bodies; at most eight active\n287:use HTTP 503/504 and RPC revision 3. The five-second limit on all nine service operations includes\n291:native rate limiter must be documented. Metadata/content responses are bounded\n295:unbounded would retain the same memory risk. Exact-limit valid native replies\n297:policy does not apply to future framed MCP streams without separate proof.\n301:limits, and record a justified adjustment in the SPEC rather than adding an\n302:unlimited fallback. Rate identity is not an analytics visitor ID and must not\n312:keep one-use mapping and error logic beside the operation. Separate contracts,\n319:work stays in the caller's span unless it owns a separate external operation.\n371:permit nearby mutation, loops, SDK leakage or a nested runtime. Generated,\n392:adapters get only their necessary exception; generated/vendor exclusions are\n418:search alone does not establish their identity. Each correction must reject\n455:rejection, header agreement, origins, rate limits, stream cancellation and\n466:| `$pageview` | Initial accepted public page and each completed client navigation | Checked page identity/path and bounded source classification; strip URL query/fragment and referrer details. |\n469:Add only operational identity needed to filter project, app, stage and schema\n474:browser opt-out to that application boundary without passing browser identity.\n475:It never grants authentication or a request-limit bypass. API and MCP events\n476:use request-scoped random identity rather than a stored user profile. Use one\n477:UUID for an event and preserve it within any deliberately qualified delivery\n497:after SDK enrichment rejects unknown events/fields. Anonymous event identity\n503:or identity migration to copy into the fresh application.\n506:analytics exception to separate machine routes. Fix its regional upstream,\n523:Define one TaxKit resource identity: `project=taxkit`,\n527:ref, revision and request identity on logs/traces only. Dashboards and proof\n531:to the query identity. Avoid request/revision/visitor values as metric labels,\n549:| Calculation log | `taxkit.calculation`: calculator ID, checked outcome and duration | One API application operation, separate from product analytics. Do not log facts, values or report contents. |\n556:relevant. Describe native CPU/startup/I/O separately if exposed. A native root\n558:Browser pageviews remain PostHog's separate measurement. Qualify observable\n562:Use a closed safe application field set: route identity, status/outcome, duration,\nRate slice preparation; implementation not yet accepted.\n\nInstalled Alchemy RateLimit is a Worker binding with no backing cloud resource. Its namespace is a desired positive integer/string configuration; it must be unique for the account/stage before an authorised apply. A declared local namespace is not provider readback or reservation. Native client returns raw {success} and unsafe vendor RateLimitError cause, so the TaxKit owner must immediately decode success and replace any vendor failure with a fixed safe tagged failure.\n\nThe accepted requirement says trusted, non-logged client key; it does not require a new secret or persistent browser ID. A checked connection key can remain private to request context and the native rate binding, with no telemetry/header/error projection. Decide whether raw trusted edge identity meets the owning privacy contract before implementation; do not introduce a salt/provider secret merely from preference.\n\nPossible binding-only dispatch capability: Website captures its original trusted edge identity before creating form/backend requests; a named native Worker RPC method accepts a transferable Request plus the encoded checked key. Public API fetch captures its own edge identity. Both methods call one application Effect with request Context, preserve native request lifetime and apply the same calculation-owned admission method. Caller-supplied forwarded headers are not authority. Need native built proof and the installed WorkerBridge method semantics before accepting this design.\n\nEach calculation, including each batch member, takes one rate unit. Metadata takes none. Approximate per-location native limiter scope must be explicit. Direct local engine/SDK policy remains unchanged. Native same-zone Worker identity assumptions need account/zone inventory before Production acceptance; no provider facts are invented here. Unknown identity fails safely rather than guessing a key.\n\nInstalled Effect 4 RpcServer handlerContext merges entry context with the actual request fibre context. Outside real router proof uses distinct Context.Reference values for two public HTTP calculations and two three-member native JSON RPC batches. All eight calculate calls retain their originating value. This establishes context propagation in the installed HTTP/RPC code, not the Worker binding or native rate counter. The prototype uses the actual source routes/calculator live Layer and checked native wire request fields; no tracked source changes or provider calls.\n\nNative WorkerBridge supports named binding-only methods returned by the Worker shape and processes each event through the native runtime Context. Cloudflare transfer uses web Request/Response, not an Effect HttpServerResponse. A candidate private method should restrict itself to the closed JSON calculator RPC path, convert the native request at ingress and return the native Response at egress, and prove body/lifetime preservation in a built local Worker. Raw HTTP headers cannot authorise that method. No generic client callback or public HTTP key header is needed.\n\nFurther review: catalog program is optional despite all three entries supplying it and no reader consuming it. Core CalculationError still has optional unknown cause; all current rule producers omit it, while the public service union exposes it. Decide a checked privacy/compatibility owner after actual cause-form baselines and usage review; do not remove or transform it during the frozen request candidate.\n\nNative local Miniflare 5 preparation now proves transferable Request/Response through a named private WorkerEntrypoint method, with exact body retention. A single native rate binding counts 12 direct fetches plus 50 private binding calls under one fixture key: 60 allowed, two rejected; a second fixture key succeeds. This is the raw local platform, not the Alchemy bridge or TaxKit application. No real edge trust, global rate guarantee, namespace reservation or provider operation is established. Miniflare 5 native config uses env type rate-limit with namespace; older constructor fields and namespaceId are rejected before startup and retained as failed preparation.\n\nBefore changing the private Website transport, qualify cancellation and lifetime using the actual Alchemy bridge, not only raw native Request/Response transfer. A named RPC method has a distinct event path from fetch; do not assume a transferred Request preserves the previous binding-fetch abort behaviour or a Response stream keeps scope alive. Restrict proposed dispatch to closed JSON RPC, retain existing ten-second reply and five-second service budgets, and run the owning built cancellation/body/cleanup tests. Configuration capability validation must preserve the original binding and method receiver; derive method/encoded-key Types from a shared narrow owner instead of mirroring a generic client.\n\nActual installed Alchemy bridge preparation now passes transferable Request/Response and native RateLimitBinding through a separately built outside Worker: 12 public fetch + 50 private calls produce 60 allowed and two rejected; another fixture key succeeds; 63 event-scope finalizers are observed. This still does not run TaxKit application code or qualify edge trust. Crucially, after the caller aborts, the transferred Request signal remains live in this local private-method observation. Do not claim remote cancellation from that path. Any eventual application change must retain the five-second work/cleanup budget and separately prove its actual caller cancellation; return buffered closed JSON rather than assume a native Response stream transfers Effect scope. The first preparation failed because its manifest named worker.js while the builder emitted entry.js; fixed before Worker startup.\n\nCurrent primary Cloudflare documentation was read 6 October 2026: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/bindings/rate-limit/ describes per-location, eventually consistent permissive counters and warns that IPs can be shared by valid users. https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/http-headers/ distinguishes edge client IP, same-zone x-real-ip changes and a shared cross-zone Worker address. https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/bindings/service-bindings/rpc/ describes binding-only methods. These do not establish TaxKit provider configuration; retain network-key/shared-network and local-approximation limits rather than claiming individual/global precise accounting. A private method can carry the original checked Website connection key without trusting an HTTP forwarded-key header.\nexport {\n  CalculatorCatalog,\n  getCalculatorCatalogEntry,\n  listCalculatorCatalogEntries,\n  type CalculatorCatalogEntry,\n} from \"./catalog.js\";\nexport { toCalculatorInputDecodeError } from \"./errors.js\";\nexport {\n  CalculatorCatalogItems,\n  CalculatorCatalogResponseValue,\n  JurisdictionsResponseValue,\n  TaxYearsResponseValue,\n  filterCalculatorEntries,\n  toCalculatorCatalogItem,\n  toCalculatorGraphResponse,\n  toCalculatorSchemaResponse,\n  toFactsResponse,\n  toRulesResponse,\n} from \"./metadata.js\";\nexport {\n  PublicCalculatorService,\n  type PublicCalculatorServiceContract,\n} from \"./service.js\";\nexport { PublicCalculatorServiceLive } from \"./live.layer.js\";\nexport {\n  CalculatorCapacityExceeded,\n  CalculatorOperationTimedOut,\n  CalculatorRequestError,\n  CalculatorMetadataError,\n  CalculatorCatalogItem,\n  CalculatorCatalogResponse,\n  CalculatorCatalogResponseData,\n  CalculatorContext,\n  CalculatorContextQuery,\n  CalculatorGraphResponse,\n  CalculatorId,\n  CalculatorInputDecodeError,\n  CalculatorInputHelp,\n  CalculatorInputIssue,\n  CalculatorJurisdiction,\n  CalculatorRunFacts,\n  CalculatorRunReport,\n  CalculatorRunRequest,\n  CalculatorRunResponse,\n  CalculatorRunResponseData,\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\n  CalculatorSchemaResponse,\n  CalculatorServiceError,\n  CalculatorTaxYear,\n  CalculationQuery,\n  DescriptorFilterQuery,\n  FactDescriptorMetadata,\n  FactsResponse,\n  GetCalculatorGraphRequest,\n  GetCalculatorRequest,\n  HelpMode,\n  HelpQuery,\n  Jurisdiction,\n  JurisdictionsResponse,\n  MetadataQuery,\n  ParameterDescriptorMetadata,\n  PublicApiError,\n  type PublicCalculatorError,\n  PublicCalculationFacts,\n  PublicCalculationReport,\n  PublicCalculationRequest,\n  PublicCalculationResponse,\n  PublicCalculationResponseData,\n  PublicCalculationServiceRequest,\n  RuleDescriptorMetadata,\n  RuleGraphEdge,\n  RulesResponse,\n  TaxYear,\n  TaxYearsResponse,\n  UnsupportedCalculatorContextError,\n  UnsupportedCalculatorError,\n} from \"./schemas.js\";\n169:export class CalculatorCapacityExceeded extends Schema.TaggedError<CalculatorCapacityExceeded>()(\n170:  \"CalculatorCapacityExceeded\",\n180:export class CalculatorOperationTimedOut extends Schema.TaggedError<CalculatorOperationTimedOut>()(\n181:  \"CalculatorOperationTimedOut\",\n202:  CalculatorOperationTimedOut,\n207:export const CalculatorServiceError = Schema.Union([\n209:  CalculatorCapacityExceeded,\n210:  CalculatorOperationTimedOut,\n213:export type CalculatorServiceError = typeof CalculatorServiceError.Type;\n216: * @deprecated Transitional API-era alias. Use `CalculatorServiceError`.\n218:export const PublicApiError = CalculatorServiceError.annotate({\n223: * @deprecated Transitional API-era alias. Use `CalculatorServiceError`.\n225:export type PublicApiError = CalculatorServiceError;\n228: * @deprecated Transitional API-era alias. Use `CalculatorServiceError`.\n230:export type PublicCalculatorError = CalculatorServiceError;\n{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"headSha\":\"1b85440f844858a96a91172014a10afb87aa452c\",\"jobs\":[{\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"databaseId\":112109888774,\"name\":\"quality\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-06T04:35:54Z\",\"status\":\"in_