vering from a hacked site L99:     * cite63†Scan for PCI compliance L100:     * cite64†Secure your website ↗︎ L101:     * cite65†Under a DDoS attack? L102: \nL103:   * Cloudflare's API\nL104: \nL105:     * Get started\nL106:       * cite66†Create API token L107:       * cite67†Get Global API key (legacy) L108:       * cite68†Get Origin CA keysDeprecated L109:       * cite69†Token formats L110:       * cite70†Account API tokens L111: \nL112:     * How to\nL113: \nL114:       * cite71†Make API calls L115:       * cite72†Create tokens via API L116:       * cite73†Control API Access L117:       * cite74†Restrict tokens L118:       * cite75†Roll tokens L119:       * cite76†API token template URLs L120: \nL121:     * Reference\nL122:       * cite77†REST API ↗︎API L123:       * cite78†GraphQL API ↗︎ L124:       * cite79†Wrangler API ↗︎ L125:       * cite80†API token permissions L126:       * cite81†API deprecations L127:       * cite82†API token templates L128:       * cite83†Rate limits L129:       * cite84†SDKs L130: \nL131:     * cite85†Troubleshooting L132: \nL133:   * OAuth Applications on Cloudflare\nL134: \nL135:     * cite86†Overview L136:     * cite87†Create your OAuth client L137:     * cite88†Integrate your OAuth client with Cloudflare L138:     * cite89†Authorizing an application L139: \nL140:   * Reference\nL141: \nL142:     * Migration guides\nL143: \nL144:       * cite90†SCIM migration L145:     * Policies\nL146: \nL147:       * cite91†Cloudflare Cookies L148:       * cite92†Compliance documentation L149:       * cite93†Content Security Policies (CSPs) L150:       * cite94†Delivering Videos with Cloudflare L151:       * cite95†Licenses L152:       * cite96†Project Cybersafe Schools L153: \nL154:     * Abuse\nL155:       * cite97†Overview L156:       * cite98†Review abuse policies†www.cloudflare.com L157:       * cite99†Complaint types L158:       * cite100†Providing specific URLs L159:       * cite101†Customer abuse report obligations L160:       * cite102†View and submit reports L161:       * cite103†Blocked Content L162:     * cite104†SDK ecosystem support policy L163:     * cite105†Troubleshooting L164:     * cite106†/cdn-cgi/ endpoint L165:     * cite107†Account and domain management best practices L166:     * cite108†Cloudflare and Google Analytics L167:     * cite109†Cloudflare crawlers L168:     * cite110†Cloudflare HTTP headers L169:     * cite111†Cloudflare Ray ID L170:     * cite112†Cloudy AI agentBeta L171:     * cite113†Connection limits L172:     * cite114†Cryptographic Attestation of Personhood L173:     * cite115†Error responses L174:     * cite116†Glossary L175:     * cite117†Markdown for AgentsBeta L176:     * cite118†Network Layers L177:     * cite119†Network ports L178:     * cite120†Partners L179:     * cite121†Redirects L180:     * cite122†Scans and penetration testing policy L181:     * cite123†TCP connections L182:     * cite124†Under Attack mode L183:   * RSS Feeds\nL184: \nL185:     * cite125†Available RSS Feeds L186:     * cite126†Consuming RSS Feeds L187: \nL188:   * Agent resources\nL189: \nL190:     * cite127†Agent setup ↗︎ L191:     * cite128†Cloudflare Skills ↗︎†github.com L192:     * cite129†Code Mode MCP Server ↗︎†github.com L193:     * cite130†Domain-specific MCP Servers ↗︎MCP†github.com L194:     * cite131†Cloudflare Fundamentals llms.txt ↗︎ L195:     * cite132†Cloudflare Fundamentals llms-full.txt ↗︎ L196:     * cite133†Cloudflare Docs llms.txt ↗︎ L197:     * cite134†Cloudflare Docs llms-full.txt ↗︎ L198:   1. cite135†Home L199:   2. /cite1†Cloudflare Fundamentals L200:   3. /Reference\nL201:   4. /Cloudflare HTTP headers\nL202: # Cloudflare HTTP headers\nL203: \nL204: Last updated May 5, 2026|Copy as Markdown|cite136†View as Markdown |cite127†Agent setup L205: \nL206: [Select]\nL207: \nL208: ## Request headers\nL209: \nL210: Cloudflare passes all HTTP request headers to your origin web server and adds additional headers as specified below.\nL211: \nL212: Note\nL213: \nL214: Cloudflare may remove HTTP request headers with names considered invalid cite137†according to NGINX ↗︎†nginx.org — for example, header names containing a `.` (dot) character.\nL215: ### Accept-Encoding\nL216: \nL217: For incoming requests, the value of this header will always be set to `accept-encoding: br, gzip`. If the client set a different value, such as `accept-encoding: deflate`, it will be overwritten and the original value will be available in `request.cf.clientAcceptEncoding`.\nL218: ### CF-Connecting-IP\nL219: \nL220: `CF-Connecting-IP` provides the client IP address connecting to Cloudflare to the origin web server. This header will only be sent on the traffic from Cloudflare's edge to your origin web server.\nL221: \nL222: For guidance on logging your visitor's original IP address, refer to cite138†Restoring original visitor IPs .\nL223: Alternatively, if you do not wish to receive the `CF-Connecting-IP` header or any HTTP header that may contain the visitor's IP address, cite139†enable the Remove visitor IP headers Managed Transform .\nL224: #### CF-Connecting-IP in Worker subrequests\nL225: \nL226: In same-zone Worker subrequests, the value of `CF-Connecting-IP` reflects the value of `x-real-ip` (the client's IP). `x-real-ip` can be altered by the user in their Worker script.\nL227: \nL228: In cross-zone subrequests from one Cloudflare zone to another Cloudflare zone, the `CF-Connecting-IP` value will be set to the Worker client IP address `'2a06:98c0:3600::103'` for security reasons.\nL229: For Worker subrequests destined for a non-Cloudflare customer zone, the `CF-Connecting-IP` and `x-real-ip` headers will both reflect the client's IP address, with only the `x-real-ip` header able to be altered.\nL230: \nL231: When no Worker subrequest is triggered, `cf-connecting-ip` reflects the client's IP address and the `x-real-ip` header is stripped.\nL232: ### CF-Connecting-IPv6\nL233: \nL234: Cloudflare provides cite140†free IPv6 support to all domains without requiring additional configuration or hardware. To support migrating to IPv6, Cloudflare's cite141†Pseudo IPv4 provides an IPv6 to IPv4 translation service for all Cloudflare domains.\nL235: \nL236: If Pseudo IPv4 is set to `Overwrite Headers` - Cloudflare overwrites the existing `Cf-Connecting-IP` and `X-Forwarded-For` headers with a pseudo IPv4 address while preserving the real IPv6 address in `CF-Connecting-IPv6` header.\nL237: ### CF-EW-Via\nL238: \nL239: This header is used for loop detection, similar to the `CDN-Loop` cite142†header ↗︎†blog.cloudflare.com .\nL240: \nL241: ### CF-Pseudo-IPv4\nL242: \nL243: If cite141†Pseudo IPv4 is set to `Add Header` - Cloudflare automatically adds the `CF-Pseudo-IPv4` header with a Class E IPv4 address hashed from the original IPv6 address.\nL244: ### True-Client-IP (Enterprise plan only)\nL245: \nL246: `True-Client-IP` provides the original client IP address to the origin web server. `True-Client-IP` is only available on an Enterprise plan. In the example below, `203.0.113.1` is the original visitor IP address. For example: `True-Client-IP: 203.0.113.1`\nL247: There is no difference between the `True-Client-IP` and `CF-Connecting-IP` headers besides the name of the header. Some Enterprise customers with legacy devices need `True-Client-IP` to avoid updating firewalls or load-balancers to read a custom header name.\nL248: \nL249: To add a `True-Client-IP` HTTP header to requests, cite139†enable the Add \"True-Client-IP\" header Managed Transform .\nL250: Alternatively, if you do not wish to receive the `True-Client-IP` header or any HTTP header that may contain the visitor's IP address, cite139†enable the Remove visitor IP headers Managed Transform .\nL251: \nL252: Caution\nL253: \nL254: If you are using Cloudflare in a stacked CDN and authenticating HTTP requests based on the IP address value in the `True-Client-IP` header, you must add a `True-Client-IP` header to your requests. If you do not add this header, its value can be spoofed to any value.\nL255: ### X-Forwarded-For\nL256: \nL257: `X-Forwarded-For` maintains proxy server and original visitor IP addresses. If there was no existing `X-Forwarded-For`header in the request sent to Cloudflare, `X-Forwarded-For` has an identical value to the `CF-Connecting-IP` header.\nL258: \nL259: For example, if the original visitor IP address is `203.0.113.1` and the request sent to Cloudflare does not contain an `X-Forwarded-For` header, then Cloudflare will send `X-Forwarded-For: 203.0.113.1` to the origin.\nL260: If, on the other hand, an `X-Forwarded-For` header was already present in the request to Cloudflare, Cloudflare will append the IP address of the HTTP proxy connecting to Cloudflare to the header.\nL261: For example, if the original visitor IP address is `203.0.113.1` and a request is proxied through two proxies: proxy A with an IP address of `198.51.100.101` and proxy B with an IP address of `198.51.100.102` before being proxied to Cloudflare, then Cloudflare will send `X-Forwarded-For: 203.0.113.1,198.51.100.101,198.51.100.102` to the origin.\nL262: Proxy A will append the original visitor's IP address (`203.0.113.1`) to `X-Forwarded-For` before proxying the request to proxy B which, in turn, will append Proxy A's IP address (`198.51.100.101`) to `X-Forwarded-For` before proxying the request to Cloudflare. And finally, Cloudflare will append proxy B's IP address (`198.51.100.102`) to `X-Forwarded-For` before proxying the request to the origin.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRequest · Cloudflare Workers docs (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/request/)\nciteturn22view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/request/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1072\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","create_time":1791262248.689072}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
