{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T05:04:12.098Z","ordinal":38146,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac4814015b487d0bfdc8a4e515e21c6","status":"completed","call_id":"call_8qh7T3VUHvAACsELIdQnGdTC","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport subprocess,json\\nhead=subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD']).decode().strip();assert head=='0d83692f5f3a81e3b4a776a4b82d990892685e9b'\\nbody='''Optional calculator context, help, filters and metadata now use canonical nested Option types and constructor defaults while preserving the original missing, undefined, present and explicit-false representations. The SDK constructs context/help through those owners; the selected calculator still owns fact decoding and safe input guidance. Calculator service/work tests now join their owning compiler.\\n\\nTyped callers, public examples and real native fixtures use the same owners. The website native fixture reads the identical request payload Schema through its declared RPC dependency, fixing Linux TS2307 without adding a package dependency. Four major package Changesets and a docs content patch cover the request interface changes.\\n\\nValidation: the original request candidate passed all nine local CI-mode stages in 660.13 seconds, including genuine installed declarations/runtime and built browser/Worker journeys. The corrective fixture commit passes the website compiler, lint, docs, runbooks and formatting; direct checks prove the same Schema object and exact fixture bytes. The original Linux run failed on the undeclared import; fresh corrected-head hosted checks and combined domain qualification remain pending.\\n\\n'''+f'[Dated proof and corrective record](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/{head}/docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-request-absence.json). This draft follows #150. T004 remains active for domain review and trusted rate identity/limits. No merge, publication, deployment, provider mutation or Medicare correction is included.\\\\n'\\nPath('/private/tmp/dev75-request-151-corrected-pr-body.md').write_text(body)\\nsubprocess.run(['gh','pr','edit','151','--body-file','/private/tmp/dev75-request-151-corrected-pr-body.md'],check=True)\\nr=json.loads(subprocess.check_output(['gh','pr','view','151','--json','headRefOid,baseRefName,isDraft,state,body,statusCheckRollup']));assert r['headRefOid']==head and r['isDraft'] and r['state']=='OPEN' and r['baseRefName']=='codex/dev-75-domain-absence-owners' and r['body']==body;Path('/private/tmp/dev75-request-151-corrected-readback.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\\\n');print(json.dumps({k:r[k] for k in ['headRefOid','baseRefName','isDraft','state','statusCheckRollup']}))\\nsubprocess.run(['git','switch','codex/dev-75-domain-contract-closeout'],check=True)\\nsubprocess.run(['git','rebase','codex/dev-75-request-absence-owners'],check=True)\\nassert not subprocess.check_output(['git','status','--porcelain']);print(subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD']).decode().strip())\\nPY\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1600}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","create_time":1791263038.482163}}}
