{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T05:16:08.295Z","ordinal":38399,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10fa3-fee7-73d3-a94b-e471dea9ad7e","call_id":"call_0bCxBh0DaoZ97Ojx3BOoZ7NM","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"d54067\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008834,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2195,\"output\":\"17:- when the user asked “Audit and tell me your proposed changes ELI5 with images” -> give a visual, plain-language, proposal-first audit with concrete examples before editing. [Task 1]\\n19:- treat the confirmed logo/lockup as authoritative before making dependent changes. [Task 1]\\n33:scope: connect Linear product updates to Changesets-owned engineering changelogs, publish plugin releases, and independently verify claim-matched completion.\\n36:## Task 1: Improve Linear changelog and release guidance, completed\\n40:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-02T10-05-16-R7K2-release_linear_changelog_guidance_0_6_1.md (cwd=/Users/cooper/Projects/calico, rollout_path=/Users/cooper/.codex/archived_sessions/rollout-2026-10-02T20-05-16-01a0fc13-458c-7740-b459-14e8375c457a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T10:55:30+00:00, thread_id=01a0fc13-458c-7740-b459-14e8375c457a, executed in /private/tmp/commonplace-linear-skill)\\n44:- Linear, Changesets, changelog, project-update, release, duplicate-safe, Development Workflows, `0.6.1`, PR #23, `changeset status --since=origin/main`, `EPERM`\\n50:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-02T10-05-16-R7K2-release_linear_changelog_guidance_0_6_1.md (cwd=/Users/cooper/Projects/calico, rollout_path=/Users/cooper/.codex/archived_sessions/rollout-2026-10-02T20-05-16-01a0fc13-458c-7740-b459-14e8375c457a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T10:55:30+00:00, thread_id=01a0fc13-458c-7740-b459-14e8375c457a, release, cache and Linear completion independently verified)\\n58:- when publishing product updates, lead with user impact, availability and required action while linking engineering evidence rather than duplicating changelog detail. [Task 1]\\n64:- Changesets owns generated `CHANGELOG.md` entries; do not hand-edit generated release history. Product updates should link the exact immutable changelog and release, while a package release remains distinct from website deployment or browser-journey verification. [Task 1]\\n65:- Fixture testing covered published plugin, saved release update after timeout, unmerged version PR and published code with unverified website rollout; all four passed. Repository tests reported 3 files/12 tests passed and full verification passed. [Task 1]\\n71:- Symptom: `changeset status --since=origin/main` fails after adding a Changeset. Cause: the Changeset is outside that comparison range. Fix: use plain `bun run changeset status`. [Task 1]\\n72:- Do not announce publication until the release workflow, refs, rendered changelog anchor, manifests, installed files and Linear records are independently read back. [Task 2]\\n100:- when planning the rebuild, the user confirmed code/repository restructuring while preserving existing content, visual design and personal-site purpose -> do not change those assets unless explicitly asked. [Task 1]\\n113:- Symptom: a Linear description write does not match on readback. Fix: re-read the exact issue, make a targeted correction and verify the changed field; likewise, do not claim a push until remote SHA readback matches. [Task 2]\\n152:- when the user later said “Approve the changes you need to make” -> treat provider, repository, folder and saved-connection changes as approved only after that review, then use narrow approvals and final readback. [Task 1][Task 3]\\n158:- Current public endpoints are `https://withcommonpractice.com` and `https://api.withcommonpractice.com`; old Website paths/queries redirect while old API aliases remain for POST/RPC/MCP clients. Use native Alchemy for provider changes. `bun run verification` is the canonical local check. [Task 2]\\nimport { defaultServerConditions } from \\\"vite\\\";\\nimport { defineConfig } from \\\"vitest/config\\\";\\n\\nexport default defineConfig({\\n  resolve: { conditions: [\\\"source\\\", ...defaultServerConditions] },\\n  // Vite's server loader resolves workspace exports separately from browser resolution.\\n  // Fresh tool tests need the source export before any package build exists.\\n  ssr: { resolve: { conditions: [\\\"source\\\", ...defaultServerConditions] } },\\n  test: {\\n    // These are source inputs for the actual CLI fixtures, not test suites.\\n    exclude: [\\\"tools/oxlint/fixtures/**\\\"],\\n    fileParallelism: false,\\n    include: [\\\"tools/**/*.test.ts\\\"],\\n    passWithNoTests: false,\\n    pool: \\\"forks\\\",\\n  },\\n});\\nimport { describe, expect, it as test } from \\\"@effect/vitest\\\";\\nimport { Array as EffectArray, Effect, Option, Result, Schema } from \\\"effect\\\";\\n\\nimport automationJson from \\\"./automation-register.json\\\";\\nimport controlsJson from \\\"./controls.json\\\";\\nimport {\\n  decodeQualityWorkflow,\\n  inspectGovernanceRegisters,\\n  inspectQualityWorkflow,\\n  inspectReleaseRuntime,\\n} from \\\"./policy.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  AutomationRegister,\\n  ControlRegister,\\n  QualityWorkflowInputError,\\n} from \\\"./schemas.js\\\";\\n\\nconst acceptedWorkflow = `name: Quality\\non:\\n  pull_request:\\n  push:\\n    branches:\\n      - main\\npermissions:\\n  contents: read\\nenv:\\n  TAXKIT_ACTION_PIN_UPDATE_OWNER: taxkit-ci-release-maintainer\\nconcurrency:\\n  group: quality-${\\\"${{\\\"} github.workflow }}-${\\\"${{\\\"} github.ref }}\\n  cancel-in-progress: true\\njobs:\\n  quality:\\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n    timeout-minutes: 30\\n    steps:\\n      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1\\n        with:\\n          fetch-depth: 0\\n      - run: git show-ref --verify --quiet refs/heads/main || git branch --track main origin/main\\n      - uses: oven-sh/setup-bun@0c5077e51419868618aeaa5fe8019c62421857d6\\n        with:\\n          bun-version-file: .bun-version\\n      - id: bun-cache-path\\n        run: echo \\\"path=$(bun pm cache)\\\" >> \\\"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\\\"\\n      - id: bun-cache-restore\\n        uses: actions/cache/restore@55cc8345863c7cc4c66a329aec7e433d2d1c52a9\\n        continue-on-error: true\\n        with:\\n          path: ${\\\"${{\\\"} steps.bun-cache-path.outputs.path }}\\n          key: bun-packages-${\\\"${{\\\"} runner.os }}-${\\\"${{\\\"} runner.arch }}-${\\\"${{\\\"} hashFiles('.bun-version') }}-${\\\"${{\\\"} hashFiles('bun.lock') }}\\n      - run: bun install --frozen-lockfile\\n      - uses: actions/cache/save@55cc8345863c7cc4c66a329aec7e433d2d1c52a9\\n        if: steps.bun-cache-restore.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\\n        continue-on-error: true\\n        with:\\n          path: ${\\\"${{\\\"} steps.bun-cache-path.outputs.path }}\\n          key: ${\\\"${{\\\"} steps.bun-cache-restore.outputs.cache-primary-key }}\\n      - run: echo \\\"PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=$RUNNER_TEMP/ms-playwright\\\" >> \\\"$GITHUB_ENV\\\"\\n      - id: playwright-identity\\n        run: echo \\\"version=$(apps/docs/node_modules/.bin/playwright --version | cut -d' ' -f2)\\\" >> \\\"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\\\"\\n      - id: playwright-cache-restore\\n        uses: actions/cache/restore@55cc8345863c7cc4c66a329aec7e433d2d1c52a9\\n        continue-on-error: true\\n        with:\\n          path: ${\\\"${{\\\"} env.PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH }}\\n          key: playwright-chromium-${\\\"${{\\\"} runner.os }}-${\\\"${{\\\"} runner.arch }}-${\\\"${{\\\"} steps.playwright-identity.outputs.version }}-${\\\"${{\\\"} hashFiles('bun.lock') }}\\n      - run: apps/docs/node_modules/.bin/playwright install --with-deps chromium\\n      - uses: actions/cache/save@55cc8345863c7cc4c66a329aec7e433d2d1c52a9\\n        if: steps.playwright-cache-restore.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\\n        continue-on-error: true\\n        with:\\n          path: ${\\\"${{\\\"} env.PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH }}\\n          key: ${\\\"${{\\\"} steps.playwright-cache-restore.outputs.cache-primary-key }}\\n      - run: bun run check:quality-workflow\\n      - name: Fetch trusted CI configuration\\n        id: doppler-ci\\n        if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository\\n        uses: dopplerhq/secrets-fetch-action@451892f16195f9ac360e1a5bcbf0b5fd0e957534\\n        with:\\n          doppler-token: ${\\\"${{\\\"} secrets.DOPPLER_CI_TOKEN }}\\n      - name: Check trusted CI configuration identity\\n        if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository\\n        env:\\n          DOPPLER_CONFIG: ${\\\"${{\\\"} steps.doppler-ci.outputs.DOPPLER_CONFIG }}\\n          DOPPLER_PROJECT: ${\\\"${{\\\"} steps.doppler-ci.outputs.DOPPLER_PROJECT }}\\n        run: test \\\"$DOPPLER_PROJECT\\\" = \\\"taxkit\\\" && test \\\"$DOPPLER_CONFIG\\\" = \\\"ci\\\"\\n      - name: Run trusted Quality with remote cache\\n        if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository\\n        env:\\n          TURBO_CACHE: local:rw,remote:rw\\n          TURBO_TEAM: ${\\\"${{\\\"} steps.doppler-ci.outputs.TURBO_TEAM }}\\n          TURBO_TOKEN: ${\\\"${{\\\"} steps.doppler-ci.outputs.TURBO_TOKEN }}\\n        run: bun run release:check -- --ci\\n      - name: Run fork Quality without credentials\\n        if: github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name != github.repository\\n        env:\\n          TURBO_CACHE: local:rw\\n        run: bun run release:check -- --ci\\n`;\\n\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"current_time\":\"2026-10-06 05:16:08 UTC\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","create_time":1791263768.295202}},"metadata":{"client_authored":fal