{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T05:49:00.342Z","ordinal":38982,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d895ba05-e7d1-4d71-9083-7a9497ed90ef","process_id":"93394","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short | head -n 45; cat packages/docs-content/content/api/authentication-and-deployment-assumptions.mdx"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short | head -n 45; cat packages/docs-content/content/api/authentication-and-deployment-assumptions.mdx"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":" M alchemy.apps.local.run.ts\n M apps/api/src/worker.application.ts\n M apps/api/src/worker.ts\n M apps/api/test/worker.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/calculation-failure.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/calculator.boundary.browser.test.tsx\n M apps/web/src/lib/config.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/live.server.layer.ts\n M apps/web/src/server.ts\n M apps/web/test/native-cancellation.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/test/native-pair.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/test/native-rpc-failures.boundary.test.ts\n M docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md\n M packages/api/http/src/groups/calculators.ts\n M packages/api/http/src/handlers/calculators.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/package.json\n M packages/api/rpc/src/client-response.boundary.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/src/errors.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/src/handlers.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/src/schemas.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/test/handlers.test.ts\n M packages/calculators/package.json\n M packages/calculators/src/index.ts\n M packages/calculators/src/schemas.ts\n M packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.test.ts\n M packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.ts\n?? apps/api/src/worker-admission.layer.ts\n?? apps/api/test/rate-admission.boundary.test.ts\n?? apps/web/test/native-rate.fixture.ts\n?? packages/api/rpc/src/rate-identity.boundary.ts\n?? packages/calculators/__tests__/calculation-admission.test.ts\n?? packages/calculators/src/admission.layer.ts\n?? packages/calculators/src/admission.schemas.ts\n?? packages/calculators/src/admission.service.ts\n---\ntitle: \"Authentication and deployment assumptions\"\ndescription: \"Understand the current HTTP API deployment boundary before you call it.\"\nstatus: \"draft\"\n---\n\n# Authentication and deployment assumptions\n\nUse this page before wiring a public client to the HTTP API. It records the\ncurrent deployment assumptions without turning them into a field-level endpoint\nreference.\n\n## Current assumptions\n\nThe current API runtime is `apps/api`. It serves the reusable HTTP contract\nfrom `@taxkit/api-http` and exposes local defaults on `127.0.0.1:4000`.\n\nThere is no public authentication contract in this documentation slice. Treat\nauthentication, tenant routing and public hosting as application-owned until a\nfuture API deployment spec defines them.\n\n## Local routes\n\nLocal development uses the API app or the portless route described in\n`apps/api/README.md`:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api start\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/health\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/docs/openapi.json\n```\n\nIf you run through portless, use:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api dev\ncurl https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/health\n```\n\n## Caller responsibilities\n\n- Send `content-type: application/json` for calculate requests.\n- Pass canonical calculator facts in the request body.\n- Keep application authentication outside the calculator payload.\n- Read endpoint fields from the generated [OpenAPI reference](./openapi-reference.mdx).\n- Handle `CalculatorApiErrorEnvelope` for expected calculator service errors.\n\n## Related pages\n\n- [API overview](./overview.mdx)\n- [Endpoints](./endpoints.mdx)\n- [Errors](./errors.mdx)\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":" M alchemy.apps.local.run.ts\n M apps/api/src/worker.application.ts\n M apps/api/src/worker.ts\n M apps/api/test/worker.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/calculation-failure.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/calculator.boundary.browser.test.tsx\n M apps/web/src/lib/config.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/live.server.layer.ts\n M apps/web/src/server.ts\n M apps/web/test/native-cancellation.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/test/native-pair.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/test/native-rpc-failures.boundary.test.ts\n M docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md\n M packages/api/http/src/groups/calculators.ts\n M packages/api/http/src/handlers/calculators.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/package.json\n M packages/api/rpc/src/client-response.boundary.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/src/errors.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/src/handlers.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/src/schemas.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/test/handlers.test.ts\n M packages/calculators/package.json\n M packages/calculators/src/index.ts\n M packages/calculators/src/schemas.ts\n M packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.test.ts\n M packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.ts\n?? apps/api/src/worker-admission.layer.ts\n?? apps/api/test/rate-admission.boundary.test.ts\n?? apps/web/test/native-rate.fixture.ts\n?? packages/api/rpc/src/rate-identity.boundary.ts\n?? packages/calculators/__tests__/calculation-admission.test.ts\n?? packages/calculators/src/admission.layer.ts\n?? packages/calculators/src/admission.schemas.ts\n?? packages/calculators/src/admission.service.ts\n---\ntitle: \"Authentication and deployment assumptions\"\ndescription: \"Understand the current HTTP API deployment boundary before you call it.\"\nstatus: \"draft\"\n---\n\n# Authentication and deployment assumptions\n\nUse this page before wiring a public client to the HTTP API. It records the\ncurrent deployment assumptions without turning them into a field-level endpoint\nreference.\n\n## Current assumptions\n\nThe current API runtime is `apps/api`. It serves the reusable HTTP contract\nfrom `@taxkit/api-http` and exposes local defaults on `127.0.0.1:4000`.\n\nThere is no public authentication contract in this documentation slice. Treat\nauthentication, tenant routing and public hosting as application-owned until a\nfuture API deployment spec defines them.\n\n## Local routes\n\nLocal development uses the API app or the portless route described in\n`apps/api/README.md`:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api start\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/health\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/docs/openapi.json\n```\n\nIf you run through portless, use:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api dev\ncurl https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/health\n```\n\n## Caller responsibilities\n\n- Send `content-type: application/json` for calculate requests.\n- Pass canonical calculator facts in the request body.\n- Keep application authentication outside the calculator payload.\n- Read endpoint fields from the generated [OpenAPI reference](./openapi-reference.mdx).\n- Handle `CalculatorApiErrorEnvelope` for expected calculator service errors.\n\n## Related pages\n\n- [API overview](./overview.mdx)\n- [Endpoints](./endpoints.mdx)\n- [Errors](./errors.mdx)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6333},"formatted_output":" M alchemy.apps.local.run.ts\n M apps/api/src/worker.application.ts\n M apps/api/src/worker.ts\n M apps/api/test/worker.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/calculation-failure.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/calculator.boundary.browser.test.tsx\n M apps/web/src/lib/config.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/live.server.layer.ts\n M apps/web/src/server.ts\n M apps/web/test/native-cancellation.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/test/native-pair.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/test/native-rpc-failures.boundary.test.ts\n M docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md\n M packages/api/http/src/groups/calculators.ts\n M packages/api/http/src/handlers/calculators.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/package.json\n M packages/api/rpc/src/client-response.boundary.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/src/errors.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/src/handlers.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/src/schemas.ts\n M packages/api/rpc/test/handlers.test.ts\n M packages/calculators/package.json\n M packages/calculators/src/index.ts\n M packages/calculators/src/schemas.ts\n M packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.test.ts\n M packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.ts\n?? apps/api/src/worker-admission.layer.ts\n?? apps/api/test/rate-admission.boundary.test.ts\n?? apps/web/test/native-rate.fixture.ts\n?? packages/api/rpc/src/rate-identity.boundary.ts\n?? packages/calculators/__tests__/calculation-admission.test.ts\n?? packages/calculators/src/admission.layer.ts\n?? packages/calculators/src/admission.schemas.ts\n?? packages/calculators/src/admission.service.ts\n---\ntitle: \"Authentication and deployment assumptions\"\ndescription: \"Understand the current HTTP API deployment boundary before you call it.\"\nstatus: \"draft\"\n---\n\n# Authentication and deployment assumptions\n\nUse this page before wiring a public client to the HTTP API. It records the\ncurrent deployment assumptions without turning them into a field-level endpoint\nreference.\n\n## Current assumptions\n\nThe current API runtime is `apps/api`. It serves the reusable HTTP contract\nfrom `@taxkit/api-http` and exposes local defaults on `127.0.0.1:4000`.\n\nThere is no public authentication contract in this documentation slice. Treat\nauthentication, tenant routing and public hosting as application-owned until a\nfuture API deployment spec defines them.\n\n## Local routes\n\nLocal development uses the API app or the portless route described in\n`apps/api/README.md`:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api start\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/health\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/docs/openapi.json\n```\n\nIf you run through portless, use:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api dev\ncurl https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/health\n```\n\n## Caller responsibilities\n\n- Send `content-type: application/json` for calculate requests.\n- Pass canonical calculator facts in the request body.\n- Keep application authentication outside the calculator payload.\n- Read endpoint fields from the generated [OpenAPI reference](./openapi-reference.mdx).\n- Handle `CalculatorApiErrorEnvelope` for expected calculator service errors.\n\n## Related pages\n\n- [API overview](./overview.mdx)\n- [Endpoints](./endpoints.mdx)\n- [Errors](./errors.mdx)\n"},"started_at_ms":1791265740342,"completed_at_ms":1791265740342}}
