l:microfrontends: Guide for building (file: r10/microfrontends/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:ncc: Expert guidance  (file: r10/ncc/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:next-cache-components: Next.js 16 Cache (file: r10/next-cache-components/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:next-forge: next-forge expert  (file: r10/next-forge/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:next-upgrade: Upgrade Next.js to (file: r10/next-upgrade/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:nextjs: Next.js App Router (file: r10/nextjs/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:observability: Vercel Observabi (file: r10/observability/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:payments: Stripe payments in (file: r10/payments/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:react-best-practices: React best-practic (file: r10/react-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:routing-middleware: Vercel Routing Mid (file: r10/routing-middleware/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:runtime-cache: Vercel Runtime C (file: r10/runtime-cache/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:satori: Expert guidance fo (file: r10/satori/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:shadcn: shadcn/ui expert g (file: r10/shadcn/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:sign-in-with-vercel: Sign in with Ver (file: r10/sign-in-with-vercel/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:swr: SWR data-fetchin (file: r10/swr/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:turbopack: Turbopack expert (file: r10/turbopack/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:turborepo: Turborepo expert (file: r10/turborepo/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:v0-dev: v0 by Vercel exper (file: r10/v0-dev/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-agent: Vercel Agent guida (file: r10/vercel-agent/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-api: Vercel app and RES (file: r10/vercel-api/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-cli: Vercel CLI expert  (file: r10/vercel-cli/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-connect: Vercel Connect exp (file: r10/vercel-connect/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-firewall: Vercel Firewall  (file: r10/vercel-firewall/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-flags: Vercel Flags guida (file: r10/vercel-flags/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-functions: Vercel Functions e (file: r10/vercel-functions/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-queues: Vercel Queues gu (file: r10/vercel-queues/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-sandbox: Vercel Sandbox gui (file: r10/vercel-sandbox/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-services: Vercel Services  (file: r10/vercel-services/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-storage: Vercel storage exp (file: r10/vercel-storage/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:verification: Full-story verific (file: r10/verification/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:workflow: Vercel Workflow De (file: r10/workflow/SKILL.md)\n- visualize:visualize: Create visualizati (file: r5/visualize/1.0.46/skills/visualize/SKILL.md)\n- work-email-assistant: MS365/Outlook inbo (file: r1/work-email-assistant/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:create-pet: Create, repair, val (file: r11/create-pet/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:pets: List, inspect, sele (file: r11/pets/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:update-pet: Inspect, validate,  (file: r11/update-pet/SKILL.md)\n- writing-skills: How to write skil (file: r1/ai-for-ui-skills/writing-skills/SKILL.md)\n\u003c/skills_instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cpermissions instructions\u003e\nFilesystem sandboxing defines which files can be read or written. `sandbox_mode` is `danger-full-access`: No filesystem sandboxing - all commands are permitted. Network access is enabled.\nApproval policy is currently never. Do not provide the `sandbox_permissions` for any reason, commands will be rejected.\n\u003c/permissions instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e# Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e...\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only for optional questions where the answer would materially improve the quality of the work.\n\nIf `request_user_input` returns no answers, continue with best judgment instead of asking again or treating the turn as blocked.\n\nNever use the `request_user_input` tool for permission requests or permission-related escalations.\n\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003crecommended_plugins\u003e\nHere is a list of plugins that are available but not installed.\n\n- Dropbox (app-69b31dc2110c8191b8b47dc98fe5a052@openai-curated-remote)\n- Box (box@openai-curated-remote)\n- Codex Security (codex-security@openai-curated-remote)\n- Figma (figma@openai-curated-remote)\n- Gmail (gmail@openai-curated-remote)\n- Google Calendar (google-calendar@openai-curated-remote)\n- Google Drive (google-drive@openai-curated-remote)\n- Linear (linear@openai-curated-remote)\n- OpenAI Developers (openai-developers@openai-curated-remote)\n- Outlook Calendar (outlook-calendar@openai-curated-remote)\n- SharePoint (sharepoint@openai-curated-remote)\n- Slack (slack@openai-curated-remote)\n\u003c/recommended_plugins\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a10fcb-fb22-7a01-867f-c76aaae6045c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["generic.developer_instructions","memories.instructions","host_skills.instructions","permissions.instructions","collaboration_mode.instructions","plugins.recommendations"],"turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_role\u003eYou are `/root`, the primary agent in a team of agents collaborating to fulfill the user's goals.\n\nAt the start of your turn, you are the active agent.\nYou can spawn sub-agents to handle subtasks, and those sub-agents can spawn their own sub-agents.\nAll agents in the team, including the agents that you can assign tasks to, are equally intelligent and capable, and have access to the same set of tools.\n\nYou can use `spawn_agent` to create a new agent, `followup_task` to give an existing agent a new task and trigger a turn, and `send_message` to pass a message to a running agent without triggering a turn.\n`send_message` calls may be read by a human, so ensure they are legible. Always put proper spaces between words and/or numbers.\nChild agents can also spawn their own sub-agents.\nYou can decide how much context you want to propagate to your sub-agents with the `fork_turns` parameter.\n\nYou will receive messages in the analysis channel in the form:\n```\nMessage Type: MESSAGE | FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: \u003crecipient\u003e\nSender: \u003cauthor\u003e\nPayload:\n\u003cpayload text\u003e\n```\nThey may be addressed as to=/root\n\nNote that collaboration tools cannot be called from inside `functions.exec`. Call `spawn_agent`, `send_message`, `followup_task`, `wait_agent`, `interrupt_agent`, and `list_agents` only as direct tool calls using the recipient shown in their tool definitions, such as `to=functions.collaboration.spawn_agent`, since they are intentionally absent from the `functions.exec` `tools.*` namespace. Available tools in `functions.exec` are explicitly described with a `tools` namespace in the developer message.\n\nAll agents share the same directory. In detail:\n- All agents have access to the same container and filesystem as you.\n- All agents use the same current working directory.\n- As a result, edits made by one agent are immediately visible to all other agents.\n\nWhen calling `wait_agent`, prefer longer waits (minutes) to avoid busy polling.\n\nThere are 4 available concurrency slots, meaning that up to 4 agents can be active at once, including you.\n\nFull-history forks (`fork_turns` omitted or `\"all\"`) inherit the parent model and reasoning effort and do not accept overrides. Only set `model` or `reasoning_effort` when explicitly requested by the user, applicable `AGENTS.md` instructions, or skill instructions; when doing so, set `fork_turns` to `\"none\"` or a positive integer string.\u003c/multi_agent_role\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a10fcb-fb22-7a01-867f-c77fc358447c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.role_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_mode\u003eAny earlier instruction enabling proactive multi-agent delegation no longer applies. Do not spawn sub-agents unless the user or applicable AGENTS.md/skill instructions explicitly ask for sub-agents, delegation, or parallel agent work.\u003c/multi_agent_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a10fcb-fb22-7a01-867f-c78d1b46a19d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.mode_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"# AGENTS.md instructions for /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit\n\n\u003cINSTRUCTIONS\u003e\n## Strict communication requirement\n\nAlways respond in plain, simple Australian English. Use an ELI5 style and avoid jargon, buzzwords, and unexplained technical terms.\n\nThis rule applies especially when discussing codebases or software engineering. Explain those topics in simple English for a beginner unless the user asks for more detail. Use concrete words and examples. Avoid specialist shorthand and vague terms such as “seams” and “gates” unless the user asks for them or the term is essential and clearly explained.\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n---\ndocument_type: agent-router\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: repository-maintainers\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\n---\n\n# TaxKit repository guide\n\nTaxKit is the public monorepo for the open-source tax engine, API, SDK, and\ndocumentation site. Start with [`docs/README.md`](docs/README.md), the sole\nmaintainer-document lifecycle and truth-layer router. `CLAUDE.md` points to this\nfile; edit `AGENTS.md` only.\n\n## Operating loop\n\n1. Read `docs/README.md`, then only the semantic owner for the task.\n2. Confirm the claim against code, configuration, Schemas, exports, generated\n   owners, or external readback at the boundary it describes.\n3. Put current implementation intent in a SPEC/task and active execution plan;\n   never reopen completed work as policy.\n4. Update the earliest durable owner and required pointers in the same slice.\n5. Run `bun run check:docs`, `bun run check:runbooks` when operations changed,\n   focused checks, and `bun run verification`;\n   package-facing changes also need an appropriate Changeset.\n6. Retain artifact identity, authority, postconditions, limitations,\n   non-claims, and rollback.\n\nFor any material calculator/rule/schema, SDK/export/example, HTTP/OpenAPI,\npublic MDX/navigation/runtime, package/app, command/CI/versioning/release-proof,\nlifecycle, SPEC, plan, runbook, or skill change, invoke the repository-local\n`$docs-maintainer` route before accepting the slice. Record `Change required`,\n`Preserve`, or evidenced `N/A` for its documentation impact. Scheduled or\nbackground freshness work is report-only candidate output unless a separately\nattached implementation authority names the reviewer and publisher.\n\n## Task routes\n\n- Repository and package topology:\n  [`docs/architecture/README.md`](docs/architecture/README.md), then\n  [`docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`](docs/architecture/package-ownership.md).\n- Effect services and boundaries:\n  [`docs/architecture/effect-services.md`](docs/architecture/effect-services.md)\n  and the applicable package README.\n- API/SDK: [`docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`](docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md),\n  [`apps/api/README.md`](apps/api/README.md), and\n  [`packages/sdk/typescript/README.md`](packages/sdk/typescript/README.md).\n- Calculators/rules/facts: the focused owner under `docs/architecture/` and the\n  owning package README.\n- Frontend/public docs:\n  [`docs/architecture/frontend.md`](docs/architecture/frontend.md),\n  [`docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md`](docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md),\n  and [`apps/docs/README.md`](apps/docs/README.md).\n- Current work: [`docs/product-specs/index.md`](docs/product-specs/index.md) and\n  [`docs/exec-plans/active/README.md`](docs/exec-plans/active/README.md).\n- Standards, tests, and release checks:\n  [`docs/standards/README.md`](docs/standards/README.md) and\n  [`docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md`](docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md).\n- Repeatable release, versioning, packed-consumer and recovery operations:\n  [`docs/runbooks/README.md`](docs/runbooks/README.md) and\n  [`docs/operations/authority-model.md`](docs/operations/authority-model.md).\n- References and audits: [`docs/references/README.md`](docs/references/README.md)\n  and [`docs/documentation-audit/README.md`](docs/documentation-audit/README.md).\n\nUse the repository-owned [Linear skill](.agents/skills/linear/SKILL.md) when\nwork is tracked in Linear. The [strict Effect skill](.agents/skills/strict-effect-ts/SKILL.md)\nand [Alchemy skill](.agents/skills/alchemy-iac/SKILL.md) supply methods; local\nprofiles and the installed dependency graph own TaxKit compatibility. Skill\ninstallation does not imply that the clean-slate enforcement migration is complete.\n\n## Engineering guardrails\n\n- Use Effect-native Schema, branded identities, Config, services, Layers,\n  tagged errors, collections, Command, and runtime primitives when they own the\n  semantics. Decode unknown/representation ingress once and encode egress at\n  explicit boundaries.\n- Reuse owning Schemas and schema-derived types. Do not mirror raw `id: string`,\n  DTOs, provider types, primitive semantic config, or unchecked SDK output.\n- Keep primary Effects flat, sequential, and pipe-first where that clarifies\n  data flow. Keep one-use mapping/decoding/error logic inline; reject\n  helper/common/utils sprawl and generic SDK callback wrappers.\n- Keep service contracts, live Layers, test Layers, and executable composition\n  separate. Do not run Effects or build live Layers inside domain logic.\n- Provider clients expose named Effect operations, `Config.schema` with\n  redacted secrets, immediate Schema decoding, safe tagged errors without\n  `instanceof`, and live/mock Layers.\n- React composition flows route → policy-owning container → focused leaf.\n  Routes own transport restoration/outcome matching, containers own commands\n  and coordination, and leaves render readonly values/local interaction state.\n- Admit an abstraction only with semantic weight, an owner, a real reuse or\n  substitution point, a simpler call graph, and focused proof.\n\n## Authority and proof\n\nTool access is capability, not authority. Provider, registry, publication,\nrelease, deployment, credential, and destructive operations require a named\nprincipal, operation, resource, environment, approval boundary, receipt,\nrollback/revocation, and readback. Local gates do not prove publication,\nproduction, or external consumer behavior.\n\nUse `bun run check:repository-paths` for checkout portability and\n`bun run verification` for repository closeout. Use `bun run release:check`\nonly for its documented local release-evidence graph; it does not authorize or\nprove publication.\n\n\u003c/INSTRUCTIONS\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cenvironment_context\u003e\n  \u003ccwd\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit\u003c/cwd\u003e\n  \u003cshell\u003ezsh\u003c/shell\u003e\n  \u003ccurrent_date\u003e2026-10-06\u003c/current_date\u003e\n  \u003ctimezone\u003eAustralia/Melbourne\u003c/timezone\u003e\n  \u003cfilesystem\u003e\u003cworkspace_roots\u003e\u003croot\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit\u003c/root\u003e\u003c/workspace_roots\u003e\u003cpermission_profile type=\"disabled\"\u003e\u003cfile_system type=\"unrestricted\" /\u003e\u003c/permission_profile\u003e\u003c/filesystem\u003e\n\u003c/environment_context\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a10fcb-fb22-7a01-867f-c79c78c08e67","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["agents_md.instructions","environments.environment_context"],"turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_1bVTWMcCf1Qh4ZCVQoDmUT9n\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"The Linear connector requires a fresh confirmation to post the prepared progress comment to DEV-75. It links draft #146 and its passing checks, and says rate limiting and domain work remain unfinished. Approve this comment?\",\"answer\":\"Approve the DEV-75 comment\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a10eaa-f994-7390-bfc4-e0aa97ccc7c9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791247448.468928,"turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f"},"role":"user","type":"message"}],"replacement_history_metadata":[{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1055e-500d-7de0-b833-96db813b1de3","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},"revision":"retained_01a1055e-500d-7de0-b833-96f424cd39df"},"user_input_order":0},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_issue"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.list_comments"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_workspace"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_status_updates"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_project"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.save_comment"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","plugin_id":"codex-app-tools@openai-bundled","server_name":"codex_app","tool_name":"attach_artifact"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.save_status_update"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a106da-6a9d-7e63-a676-d613ca83284b","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},"revision":"retained_01a106da-6a9d-7e63-a676-d63d307e199e"},"user_input_order":162},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_issue"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.list_comments"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_workspace"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_status_updates"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_project"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.save_comment"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","plugin_id":"codex-app-tools@openai-bundled","server_name":"codex_app","tool_name":"attach_artifact"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.save_status_update"},{"first_turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","server_name":"executor-personal","tool_name":"skills"},{"first_turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","server_name":"executor-personal","tool_name":"execute"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a10eaa-f994-7390-bfc4-e0aa97ccc7c9","role":"user","turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f"},"revision":"retained_01a10eaa-f994-7390-bfc4-e0c71863ea13"},"user_input_order":644},{"client_authored":false,"compaction_model_hash":"3000","mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_issue"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.list_comments"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_workspace"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_status_updates"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_project"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.save_comment"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","plugin_id":"codex-app-tools@openai-bundled","server_name":"codex_app","tool_name":"attach_artifact"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.save_status_update"},{"first_turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","server_name":"executor-personal","tool_name":"skills"},{"first_turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","server_name":"executor-personal","tool_name":"execute"},{"first_turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","server_name":"executor-personal","tool_name":"resume"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","realtime_active":false}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac487325af087d08c8cb7e2bc5224d8","order":808,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10fb0-1f17-76d2-8338-ea05d9d09dc9","text":"I’ll check whether the approved DEV-75 comment has already been posted, then continue the shared rate limit work.\n","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac4873f146487d08bc003b6b0bf0b26","order":809,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10fb0-53bc-7b33-96f5-50a520d78e17","text":"The corrected draft #151 has passed GitHub’s checks. Draft #152 is still being checked.\n\nI’m using the repository’s documentation, Effect and Alchemy skills for the shared rate limit change. The API and website will use the same calculation allowance; reading calculator information will not use it.\n","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac48766b6ec87d08601f33ff88b14a7","order":810,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10fb0-ef2f-7ac1-b162-fa17fe4faff1","text":"The approved comment is already saved on DEV-75, so there’s no duplicate to post. I’ve started the rate limit change from draft #152.\n\nCalculation requests with missing or invalid client details will return a safe error. Metadata requests will still work.\n","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac487e55f5c87d0b1b226a5df03bd95","order":811,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10fb2-dd29-7330-9324-f65afbf68dc2","text":"The shared calculation allowance and safe error types are taking shape. Client details will stay out of calculator results and error messages.\n\nNext I’m connecting the native host. The tests need to show that public calls, website calls and batched calls all count towards the same allowance.\n","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac48a10103887d0ad8017f0cd79869f","order":812,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10fbb-55a1-78a1-876e-14ff330b4830","text":"The HTTP and website paths now use the same rate-limit error and retry guidance. The compiler caught two places that needed updating: an HTTP error case and the type used for the private binding.\n\nI’m adding tests that confirm rejected requests do no calculation work and metadata uses no rate allowance.\n","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac48b1ad22487d0a7cb69e4bae153a7","order":813,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10fbf-67a0-7262-9659-fe48ea1e6ed4","text":"The source tests pass. They show that HTTP and private calls share the 60-calculation allowance, each batch member uses a unit, and metadata uses none. The generated HTTP client also receives the checked 429 error with `Retry-After: 60`.\n\nThe built-host tests are next. Those will check the actual native binding and website forwarding.\n","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac48b99b95487d0b04131aa1558b026","order":814,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10fc1-569e-7851-86ed-5a01e296da87","text":"Draft #152 has now passed GitHub’s checks too.\n\nThe rate-limit tests found a useful distinction: adding the native binding changes the deployment plan. I’m updating the local test’s saved “unchanged” state to include that binding, then checking that the planner still makes no provider changes.\n","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac48d80f95087d08b892f87e6833b9e","order":815,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10fc8-c62f-7e13-b9c0-8f74aafe8fdf","text":"The built-host tests caught a local-development problem: local emulation does not supply Cloudflare’s client header. I’m adding an explicit mode for the disposable local stack, with one limited allowance shared by that emulator. Hosted requests will still need valid client details.\n\nThe failing tests are retained while I check this change and the deployment-plan result.\n","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":816,"user_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a1055e-500d-7de0-b833-96db813b1de3","order":0,"revision":"retained_01a1055e-500d-7de0-b833-96f424cd39df","text":"\n# Files pasted by the user:\n\n## \"--- document_type: execution-plan lifecycle: current authority: supporting owne…\": /Users/cooper/.codex/attachments/f82088a9-b579-462a-9bee-4d3685805660/Pasted text.txt\n\nPasted text contains the user's request.\n\n## My request:\n\n","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a106da-6a9d-7e63-a676-d613ca83284b","order":162,"revision":"retained_01a106da-6a9d-7e63-a676-d63d307e199e","text":"Continue","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10eaa-f994-7390-bfc4-e0aa97ccc7c9","order":644,"revision":"retained_01a10eaa-f994-7390-bfc4-e0c71863ea13","text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_1bVTWMcCf1Qh4ZCVQoDmUT9n\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"The Linear connector requires a fresh confirmation to post the prepared progress comment to DEV-75. It links draft #146 and its passing checks, and says rate limiting and domain work remain unfinished. Approve this comment?\",\"answer\":\"Approve the DEV-75 comment\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e","turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f"}],"user_messages_incomplete":false,"verified_answers":[]},"window_id":"01a10fcb-fb1f-7912-8da3-0d8de91c8576","window_number":51}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T05:59:48.771Z","ordinal":39133,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{"directory":"/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","text":"## Strict communication requirement\n\nAlways respond in plain, simple Australian English. Use an ELI5 style and avoid jargon, buzzwords, and unexplained technical terms.\n\nThis rule applies especially when discussing codebases or software engineering. Explain those topics in simple English for a beginner unless the user asks for more detail. Use concrete words and examples. Avoid specialist shorthand and vague terms such as “seams” and “gates” unless the user asks for them or the term is essential and clearly explained.\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n---\ndocument_type: agent-router\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: repository-maintainers\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\n---\n\n# TaxKit repository guide\n\nTaxKit is the public monorepo for the open-source tax engine, API, SDK, and\ndocumentation site. Start with [`docs/README.md`](docs/README.md), the sole\nmaintainer-document lifecycle and truth-layer router. `CLAUDE.md` points to this\nfile; edit `AGENTS.md` only.\n\n## Operating loop\n\n1. Read `docs/README.md`, then only the semantic owner for the task.\n2. Confirm the claim against code, configuration, Schemas, exports, generated\n   owners, or external readback at the boundary it describes.\n3. Put current implementation intent in a SPEC/task and active execution plan;\n   never reopen completed work as policy.\n4. Update the earliest durable owner and required pointers in the same slice.\n5. Run `bun run check:docs`, `bun run check:runbooks` when operations changed,\n   focused checks, and `bun run verification`;\n   package-facing changes also need an appropriate Changeset.\n6. Retain artifact identity, authority, postconditions, limitations,\n   non-claims, and rollback.\n\nFor any material calculator/rule/schema, SDK/export/example, HTTP/OpenAPI,\npublic MDX/navigation/runtime, package/app, command/CI/versioning/release-proof,\nlifecycle, SPEC, plan, runbook, or skill change, invoke the repository-local\n`$docs-maintainer` route before accepting the slice. Record `Change required`,\n`Preserve`, or evidenced `N/A` for its documentation impact. Scheduled or\nbackground freshness work is report-only candidate output unless a separately\nattached implementation authority names the reviewer and publisher.\n\n## Task routes\n\n- Repository and package topology:\n  [`docs/architecture/README.md`](docs/architecture/README.md), then\n  [`docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`](docs/architecture/package-ownership.md).\n- Effect services and boundaries:\n  [`docs/architecture/effect-services.md`](docs/architecture/effect-services.md)\n  and the applicable package README.\n- API/SDK: [`docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`](docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md),\n  [`apps/api/README.md`](apps/api/README.md), and\n  [`packages/sdk/typescript/README.md`](packages/sdk/typescript/README.md).\n- Calculators/rules/facts: the focused owner under `docs/architecture/` and the\n  owning package README.\n- Frontend/public docs:\n  [`docs/architecture/frontend.md`](docs/architecture/frontend.md),\n  [`docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md`](docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md),\n  and [`apps/docs/README.md`](apps/docs/README.md).\n- Current work: [`docs/product-specs/index.md`](docs/product-specs/index.md) and\n  [`docs/exec-plans/active/README.md`](docs/exec-plans/active/README.md).\n- Standards, tests, and release checks:\n  [`docs/standards/README.md`](docs/standards/README.md) and\n  [`docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md`](docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md).\n- Repeatable release, versioning, packed-consumer and recovery operations:\n  [`docs/runbooks/README.md`](docs/runbooks/README.md) and\n  [`docs/operations/authority-model.md`](docs/operations/authority-model.md).\n- References and audits: [`docs/references/README.md`](docs/references/README.md)\n  and [`docs/documentation-audit/README.md`](docs/documentation-audit/README.md).\n\nUse the repository-owned [Linear skill](.agents/skills/linear/SKILL.md) when\nwork is tracked in Linear. The [strict Effect skill](.agents/skills/strict-effect-ts/SKILL.md)\nand [Alchemy skill](.agents/skills/alchemy-iac/SKILL.md) supply methods; local\nprofiles and the installed dependency graph own TaxKit compatibility. Skill\ninstallation does not imply that the clean-slate enforcement migration is complete.\n\n## Engineering guardrails\n\n- Use Effect-native Schema, branded identities, Config, services, Layers,\n  tagged errors, collections, Command, and runtime primitives when they own the\n  semantics. Decode unknown/representation ingress once and encode egress at\n  explicit boundaries.\n- Reuse owning Schemas and schema-derived types. Do not mirror raw `id: string`,\n  DTOs, provider types, primitive semantic config, or unchecked SDK output.\n- Keep primary Effects flat, sequential, and pipe-first where that clarifies\n  data flow. Keep one-use mapping/decoding/error logic inline; reject\n  helper/common/utils sprawl and generic SDK callback wrappers.\n- Keep service contracts, live Layers, test Layers, and executable composition\n  separate. Do not run Effects or build live Layers inside domain logic.\n- Provider clients expose named Effect operations, `Config.schema` with\n  redacted secrets, immediate Schema decoding, safe tagged errors without\n  `instanceof`, and live/mock Layers.\n- React composition flows route → policy-owning container → focused leaf.\n  Routes own transport restoration/outcome matching, containers own commands\n  and coordination, and leaves render readonly values/local interaction state.\n- Admit an abstraction only with semantic weight, an owner, a real reuse or\n  substitution point, a simpler call graph, and focused proof.\n\n## Authority and proof\n\nTool access is capability, not authority. Provider, registry, publication,\nrelease, deployment, credential, and destructive operations require a named\nprincipal, operation, resource, environment, approval boundary, receipt,\nrollback/revocation, and readback. Local gates do not prove publication,\nproduction, or external consumer behavior.\n\nUse `bun run check:repository-paths` for checkout portability and\n`bun run verification` for repository closeout. Use `bun run release:check`\nonly for its documented local release-evidence graph; it does not authorize or\nprove publication.\n"},"apps_instructions":false,"collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","instructions":"0a11049b0421e1e86f1e129af8d547a89548a0c3"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","status":"available","shell":"zsh"}},"current_date":"2026-10-06","timezone":"Australia/Melbourne","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></filesystem>"},"environments_instructions":false,"git_attribution":false,"host_skills":{"body":"\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/skills`\n- `r1` = `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills`\n- `r2` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r3` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/plugins/cache/commonplace/development-workflows/0.6.2/skills`\n- `r4` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/plugins/cache/commonplace/foundations/0.5.1/skills`\n- `r5` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r6` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/bits-and-bolts-remote/1.0.23/skills`\n- `r7` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/plugins/cach