{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:09:33.142Z","ordinal":39524,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","item":{"type":"Extension","kind":"web.search","id":"exec-d12f1c6d-17a8-4023-a92f-77f0007ad6c5","query":"site.cloudflare.com \"AbortSignal\" \"serialization\" Workers","action":{"type":"search","query":"site.cloudflare.com \"AbortSignal\" \"serialization\" Workers","queries":null},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.cloudflare.com","ref_id":"turn27search0","snippet":"When `enhanced_error_serialization` is enabled, errors serialized using `structuredClone()` or V8 serialization support more error types and include own properties on the error object. ... When","title":"Compatibility flags · Cloudflare Workers docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/compatibility-flags/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn27search1","snippet":"* `AbortSignal` — not serializable without the `AbortSignal serialization` compat flag. ... The abort loopback could expose a `poll()` method the sub-agent checks periodically, sidestepping","title":"agents/design/loopback.md at main · cloudflare/agents · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/agents/blob/main/design/loopback.md"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn27search2","snippet":"== \"automatic\") { init.encodeResponseBody = cfReq.encodeResponseBody; } // TODO: Support request.signal. ... So for now, since we don't support AbortSignal yet, all we can do","title":"capnweb/src/serialize.ts at main · cloudflare/capnweb · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/capnweb/blob/main/src/serialize.ts"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn27search3","snippet":"The signal is linked to Think's per-turn `AbortController`; when it aborts: ... `AbortSignal` cannot be passed as an RPC argument across Durable Object boundaries —","title":"agents/docs/think/sub-agents.md at main · cloudflare/agents · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/agents/blob/main/docs/think/sub-agents.md"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"9a51ac8b.previews.developers.cloudflare.com","ref_id":"turn27search4","snippet":"When `enhanced_error_serialization` is enabled, errors serialized using `structuredClone()` or V8 serialization support more error types and include own properties on the error object.","title":"Compatibility flags · Cloudflare Workers docs","url":"https://9a51ac8b.previews.developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/compatibility-flags/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn27search5","snippet":"# WebAssembly based projects often rely on this API for wasm memory cleanup requestSignalPassthrough @85 :Bool $compatEnableFlag(\"request_signal_passthrough\") $compatDisableFlag(\"no_request_signal_pas","title":"workerd/src/workerd/io/compatibility-date.capnp at main · cloudflare/workerd · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/workerd/blob/main/src/workerd/io/compatibility-date.capnp"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"kbaqcfpccwnulvbfjm4ethla4hnq.qer011.online","ref_id":"turn27search6","snippet":"You cannot perform any I/O within them, including emitting events to a tail Worker. ::: ... When the `request_signal_passthrough` flag set, the `AbortSignal` of an","title":"Compatibility flags · Cloudflare Workers docs","url":"https://kbaqcfpccwnulvbfjm4ethla4hnq.qer011.online/workers/configuration/compatibility-flags/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"app.unpkg.com","ref_id":"turn27search7","snippet":"* The **`throwIfAborted()`** method throws the signal's abort AbortSignal.reason if the signal has been aborted; otherwise it does nothing. ... * The **`ExtendableEvent`** interface extends","title":"UNPKG","url":"https://app.unpkg.com/%40cloudflare/workers-types%405.20260810.1/files/index.d.ts"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"fossies.org","ref_id":"turn27search8","snippet":"export function assertSqliteIntegrityInWorker( | | export function assertSqliteIntegrityInWorker( ... signal: AbortSignal, | | callerSignal: AbortSignal, ... serialization: \"advanced\", | | serializati","title":"openclaw: sqlite-integrity-worker.ts - 2026.9.4 vs. 2026.9.5 changes | Fossies Diffs","url":"https://fossies.org/diffs/openclaw/2026.9.4_vs_2026.9.5/src/infra/sqlite-integrity-worker.ts-diff.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"blog.gitcode.com","ref_id":"turn27search9","snippet":"读完本文,你将理解 Cloudflare Workers 中哪些对象无法跨越 RPC 边界、为什么 `WorkerEntrypoint` 可序列化 props 加\"调用时解析\"的组合能够绕开这些限制,并看到该模式在 `@cloudflare/think` 包中 `HostBridgeLoopback` 的真实源码实现、接线方式与测试覆盖。 ... `AbortSignal`——在没有 `Abort","title":"Cloudflare Agents SDK 中的 Loopback 模式:让 RPC 在隔离边界之后仍可序列化与持久化 - AtomGit | GitCode博客","url":"https://blog.gitcode.com/97ac5ff6c00b5655a26daa1d1248d3db.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"cfdata.lol","ref_id":"turn27search10","snippet":"When the `allow_eval_during_startup` flag is set, Workers can use `eval()` and `new Function(text)` during the startup phase of a Worker script. ... When the `request_signal_passthrough`","title":"workerd - Cloudflare Datamining","url":"https://cfdata.lol/workerd/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.npmjs.com","ref_id":"turn27search11","snippet":"import {ThreadWebWorker, ThreadAbortSignal} from '@quilted/threads'; ... signal: ThreadAbortSignalSerialization;","title":"@quilted/threads - npm","url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/%40quilted/threads"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"sydr-fuzz.github.io","ref_id":"turn27search12","snippet":"[2022-11-13 14:00:39] [INFO] casr-san: NOT_EXPLOITABLE: SourceAvNearNull: /xlnt/source/detail/serialization/xlsx_consumer.cpp:2044:22 ... [2022-11-13 14:00:39] [INFO] casr-gdb: NOT_EXPLOITABLE: AbortS","title":"Презентация PowerPoint","url":"https://sydr-fuzz.github.io/papers/vishnyakov-sydr-offzone2023.pdf"}]},"started_at_ms":1791266970540,"completed_at_ms":1791266973142}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:09:33.202Z","ordinal":39525,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10fd4-e612-7f80-9917-3d00e61a9daa","call_id":"call_0TM6aPWsoBbQkt73Jy6oA5J5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"4040be\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005667,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Compatibility flags · Cloudflare Workers docs (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/compatibility-flags/)\nciteturn27search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; When `enhanced_error_serialization` is enabled, errors serialized using `structuredClone()` or V8 serialization support more error types and include own properties on the error object. ... When the `disallow_importable_env` flag is enabled, Workers will not allow importing the environment variables via the `cloudflare:workers` module and will not populate the environment variables in the global `process.env` object when Node.js compatibility is enabled. ... When the `request_signal_passthrough` flag set, the `AbortSignal` of an incoming request will be passed through to subrequests when the request is forwarded to a subrequest using the `fetch()` API. ... Meanwhile, if the Worker passes the response through to the client, Cloudflare's HTTP proxy will opportunistically gzip the response body on that side of the Workers runtime instead.\n          // With this flag: error.message === \"custom error message\"\n        });\n      }\n    }`\n\nWith the `workflows_preserve_non_retryable_error_message` flag enabled, the original error message and name are preserved, making it easier to debug and handle specific error cases in your Workflow code.\n\n### Enhanced error serialization\n\nDefault as of  | 2026-04-21\nFlag to enable  | `enhanced_error_serialization`\nFlag to disable  | `legacy_error_serialization`\n\nWhen `enhanced_error_serialization` is enabled, errors serialized using `structuredClone()` or V8 serialization support more error types and include own properties on the error object.\n\nNote that when enabled, deserialization of errors will not preserve the original stack trace by default.\n\nPreviously, only basic `Error` types were serialized, and own properties added to error objects were lost during serialization.\n\n### Use an isolated PID namespace for containers\n\nDefault as of  | 2026-04-01\nFlag to enable  | `containers_pid_namespace`\nFlag to disable  | `no_containers_pid_namespace`\nThese callbacks do not have an associated async context. You cannot perform any I/O within them, including emitting events to a tail Worker. :::\n\n:::caution These APIs are fundamentally non-deterministic. The timing and execution of garbage collection are unpredictable, and you should not rely on them for essential program logic. Additionally, cleanup callbacks registered with `FinalizationRegistry` may never be executed, including but not limited to cases where garbage collection is not triggered, or your Worker gets evicted. :::\n\n### Passthrough AbortSignal of incoming request to subrequests\n\nFlag to enable  | `request_signal_passthrough`\nFlag to disable  | `no_request_signal_passthrough`\n\nWhen the `request_signal_passthrough` flag set, the `AbortSignal` of an incoming request will be passed through to subrequests when the request is forwarded to a subrequest using the `fetch()` API.\n\nThe the `no_request_signal_passthrough` flag is set, the `AbortSignal` of the incoming request will not be passed through.\n\n### Spec-compliant URLPattern implementation\n\nDefault as of  | 2025-05-01\nFlag to enable  | `urlpattern_standard`\nFlag to disable  | `urlpattern_original`\n\nThe original `URLPattern` implementation was not fully compliant with the WHATWG URLPattern Standard ↗︎, leading to a number of issues reported by users.\n\nWith `urlpattern_standard` enabled, Workers uses a spec-compliant URLPattern implementation. This is a breaking change from the original behavior, so it is gated behind a compatibility flag.\n\nIf you are using `URLPattern` and encounter unexpected behavior changes after updating your compatibility date, you can set `urlpattern_original` to revert to the previous implementation.\n\nThis broke subclassing at the JavaScript layer, preventing a subclass from correctly overriding the superclass getters/setters. This flag controls the breaking change made to set those getters/setters on the prototype template instead.\n\nThis changes applies to:\n\n  * `AbortSignal`\n  * `AbortController`\n  * `Blob`\n  * `Body`\n  * `DigestStream`\n  * `Event`\n  * `File`\n  * `Request`\n  * `ReadableStream`\n  * `ReadableStreamDefaultReader`\n  * `ReadableStreamBYOBReader`\n  * `Response`\n  * `TextDecoder`\n  * `TextEncoder`\n  * `TransformStream`\n  * `URL`\n  * `WebSocket`\n  * `WritableStream`\n  * `WritableStreamDefaultWriter`\n\n### Durable Object `stub.fetch()` requires a full URL\n\nDefault as of  | 2021-11-10\nFlag to enable  | `durable_object_fetch_requires_full_url`\nFlag to disable  | `durable_object_fetch_allows_relative_url`\n\nOriginally, when making a request to a Durable Object by calling `stub.fetch(url)`, a relative URL was accepted as an input. The URL would be interpreted relative to the placeholder URL `http://fake-host`, and the resulting absolute URL was delivered to the destination object's `fetch()` handler. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nagents/design/loopback.md at main · cloudflare/agents · GitHub (https://github.com/cloudflare/agents/blob/main/design/loopback.md)\nciteturn27search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago;   * `AbortSignal` — not serializable without the `AbortSignal serialization` compat flag. ... The abort loopback could expose a `poll()` method the sub-agent checks periodically, sidestepping the AbortSignal serialization issue entirely. ...   * Runtime workarounds — several `getOwnPropertyDescriptor` and `getPrototypeOf` overrides exist to work around workerd bugs.\n\n## Breadcrumbs\n\n  1. agents\n  2. /design\n\n/\n\n# loopback.md\n\n# Loopback Pattern\n\nCross-boundary RPC for sub-agents and dynamic isolates.\n\n## The problem\n\nSub-agents (facets) run as colocated child Durable Objects with their own isolated SQLite. The parent calls them via typed RPC stubs. But several things cannot cross the RPC boundary:\n\n  * `AbortSignal` — not serializable without the `AbortSignal serialization` compat flag. Passing one from parent to sub-agent throws `DataCloneError`.\n  * Closures and live objects — an `RpcTarget` can cross the boundary, but it ties the child's execution to a live reference held by the parent. If the parent hibernates, the reference dies.\n  * Dynamic worker bindings — dynamic isolates loaded via `env.LOADER` can only receive `Fetcher`/`ServiceStub` in their `env`, not `RpcStub`. You cannot hand them an RPC handle to a Durable Object.\n  * Persistable references — a stub to a dynamic worker entrypoint cannot be persisted, because the system doesn't know how to restart the dynamic worker without help from whatever loaded it.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ncapnweb/src/serialize.ts at main · cloudflare/capnweb · GitHub (https://github.com/cloudflare/capnweb/blob/main/src/serialize.ts)\nciteturn27search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; == \"automatic\") { init.encodeResponseBody = cfReq.encodeResponseBody; } // TODO: Support request.signal. ... So for now, since we don't support AbortSignal yet, all we can do is ignore // it; we can't throw an error if it's present. return [\"request\", req.url, init]; } case \"response\": { let resp = <Response>value; let body = this.devaluateImpl(resp.body, resp, depth + 1); let init: Record<string, unknown> = {}; if (resp.status ! ... <Iterable<[string, string]>><any>resp.headers]; if (headers.length > 0) { // Note that we don't need to serialize this as [\"headers\", headers] because we are only // trying to create a valid ResponseInit object. init.headers = headers; } // These properties are specific to Cloudflare Workers.\n Cast the request to `any` to // silence type errors on other platforms. let cfReq = req as any; if (cfReq.cf) init.cf = cfReq.cf; if (cfReq.encodeResponseBody && cfReq.encodeResponseBody !== \"automatic\") { init.encodeResponseBody = cfReq.encodeResponseBody; } // TODO: Support request.signal. Annoyingly, all `Request`s have a `signal` property even // if none was passed to the constructor, and there's no way to tell if it's a real // signal. So for now, since we don't support AbortSignal yet, all we can do is ignore // it; we can't throw an error if it's present. return [\"request\", req.url, init]; } case \"response\": { let resp = <Response>value; let body = this.devaluateImpl(resp.body, resp, depth + 1); let init: Record<string, unknown> = {}; if (resp.status !== 200) init.status = resp.status; if (resp.statusText) init.statusText = resp.statusText; let headers = [...<Iterable<[string, string]>><any>resp.headers]; if (headers.length > 0) { // Note that we don't need to serialize this as [\"headers\", headers] because we are only // trying to create a valid ResponseInit object. init.headers = headers; } // These properties are specific to Cloudflare Workers. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nagents/docs/think/sub-agents.md at main · cloudflare/agents · GitHub (https://github.com/cloudflare/agents/blob/main/docs/think/sub-agents.md)\nciteturn27search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; The signal is linked to Think's per-turn `AbortController`; when it aborts: ... `AbortSignal` cannot be passed as an RPC argument across Durable Object boundaries — workerd's JSRPC layer rejects it at serialization time.\n        setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 30_000);\n    \n        const { status } = await this.saveMessages(\n          [\n            {\n              id: crypto.randomUUID(),\n              role: \"user\",\n              parts: [{ type: \"text\", text }]\n            }\n          ],\n          { signal: controller.signal }\n        );\n    \n        if (status === \"aborted\") {\n          console.log(\"Turn cancelled by external signal\");\n        }\n      }\n    }\n\n#### Crossing DO boundaries\n\n`AbortSignal` cannot be passed as an RPC argument across Durable Object boundaries — workerd's JSRPC layer rejects it at serialization time. Construct the controller inside the DO that calls `saveMessages` and bridge the parent's intent through a serializable mechanism.\n\nFor agent orchestration, prefer Agent Tools. `runAgentTool()` and `agentTool()` handle the parent abort signal, child-local `saveMessages({ signal })`, event forwarding, replay, and cleanup for Think and `AIChatAgent` child agents.\n\nFor lower-level custom RPC patterns, return a `ReadableStream` from the child and let the parent cancel its reader. workerd propagates that cancellation back to the source stream's `cancel` callback, where the child can abort its local controller.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCompatibility flags · Cloudflare Workers docs (https://9a51ac8b.previews.developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/compatibility-flags/)\nciteturn27search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; When `enhanced_error_serialization` is enabled, errors serialized using `structuredClone()` or V8 serialization support more error types and include own properties on the error object.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nworkerd/src/workerd/io/compatibility-date.capnp at main · cloudflare/workerd · GitHub (https://github.com/cloudflare/workerd/blob/main/src/workerd/io/compatibility-date.capnp)\nciteturn27search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week;  # WebAssembly based projects often rely on this API for wasm memory cleanup requestSignalPassthrough @85 :Bool $compatEnableFlag(\"request_signal_passthrough\") $compatDisableFlag(\"no_request_signal_passthrough\"); # When enabled, the AbortSignal of the incoming request is not passed through to subrequests. ... # WARNING: This API is still in development and may change or be removed in the future. abortSignalRpc @88 :Bool $compatEnableFlag(\"enable_abortsignal_rpc\") $experimental; # Enables experimental support for passing AbortSignal over RPC. allowEvalDuringStartup @89 :Bool $compatEnableFlag(\"allow_eval_during_startup\") $compatEnableDate(\"2025-06-01\") $compatDisableFlag(\"disallow_eval_during_startup\"); # Enables eval() and new Function() during startup. enableRequestSignal @90 :Bool $compatEnableFlag(\"enable_request_signal\") $compatDisableFlag(\"disable_request_signal\"); # Enables Request.signal for incoming requests.# This feature is still experimental and the compat flag has no default enable date. connectPassThrough @91 :Bool $compatEnableFlag(\"connect_pass_through\") $experimental; # Causes the Worker to handle incoming connect events by simply passing them through to the # Worker's globalOutbound (typically, the internet).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCompatibility flags · Cloudflare Workers docs (https://kbaqcfpccwnulvbfjm4ethla4hnq.qer011.online/workers/configuration/compatibility-flags/)\nciteturn27search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; You cannot perform any I/O within them, including emitting events to a tail Worker. ::: ... When the `request_signal_passthrough` flag set, the `AbortSignal` of an incoming request will be passed through to subrequests when the request is forwarded to a subrequest using the `fetch()` API.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUNPKG (https://app.unpkg.com/%40cloudflare/workers-types%405.20260810.1/files/index.d.ts)\nciteturn27search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago;        * The **`throwIfAborted()`** method throws the signal's abort AbortSignal.reason if the signal has been aborted; otherwise it does nothing. ...      * The **`ExtendableEvent`** interface extends the lifetime of the `install` and `activate` events dispatched on the global scope as part of the service worker lifecycle.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nopenclaw: sqlite-integrity-worker.ts - 2026.9.4 vs. 2026.9.5 changes | Fossies Diffs (https://fossies.org/diffs/openclaw/2026.9.4_vs_2026.9.5/src/infra/sqlite-integrity-worker.ts-diff.html)\nciteturn27search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; export function assertSqliteIntegrityInWorker(  |  | export function assertSqliteIntegrityInWorker( ... signal: AbortSignal,  |  | callerSignal: AbortSignal, ... serialization: \"advanced\",  |  | serialization: \"advanced\",\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCloudflare Agents SDK 中的 Loopback 模式:让 RPC 在隔离边界之后仍可序列化与持久化 - AtomGit | GitCode博客 (https://blog.gitcode.com/97ac5ff6c00b5655a26daa1d1248d3db.html)\nciteturn27search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; 读完本文,你将理解 Cloudflare Workers 中哪些对象无法跨越 RPC 边界、为什么 `WorkerEntrypoint` 可序列化 props 加\"调用时解析\"的组合能够绕开这些限制,并看到该模式在 `@cloudflare/think` 包中 `HostBridgeLoopback` 的真实源码实现、接线方式与测试覆盖。 ... `AbortSignal`——在没有 `AbortSignal serialization` compat flag 的情况下不可序列化。\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nworkerd - Cloudflare Datamining (https://cfdata.lol/workerd/)\nciteturn27search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; When the `allow_eval_during_startup` flag is set, Workers can use `eval()` and `new Function(text)` during the startup phase of a Worker script. ... When the `request_signal_passthrough` flag set, the `AbortSignal` of an incoming request will be passed through to subrequests when the request is forwarded to a subrequest using the `fetch()` API.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@quilted/threads - npm (https://www.npmjs.com/package/%40quilted/threads)\nciteturn27search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago;     import {ThreadWebWorker, ThreadAbortSignal} from '@quilted/threads'; ...       signal: ThreadAbortSignalSerialization;\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nПрезентация PowerPoint (https://sydr-fuzz.github.io/papers/vishnyakov-sydr-offzone2023.pdf)\nciteturn27search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.1 years ago; Crawled: 3.1 years ago; [2022-11-13 14:00:39] [INFO] casr-san: NOT_EXPLOITABLE: SourceAvNearNull: /xlnt/source/detail/serialization/xlsx_consumer.cpp:2044:22 ... [2022-11-13 14:00:39] [INFO] casr-gdb: NOT_EXPLOITABLE: AbortSignal: /xlnt/third-party/utfcpp/utf8/checked.h:216\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","create_time":1791266973.202959}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
