d task artifacts in the same slice;\n   - **audit or curator:** for scheduled/background freshness work, or when\n     mutation authority is absent, produce an isolated report-only candidate\n     with provenance and a proposed patch. Publication requires a separately\n     named responsible owner and publisher identity.\n\nNever let a curator publish its own uncorroborated findings or treat its prior\noutput as independent feedback. Pin any published context projection to an\nimmutable repository revision; refresh it only at a recorded phase boundary.\n\nKeep these truth layers distinct and apply the strongest applicable precedence:\nexternal system for current external state; shared store for shared source\nmaterial; immutable context projection for a recorded phase; repository code,\nconfig, and Schemas for desired state; durable docs for explanation and routing;\ndated evidence for observations; active SPEC/tasks for current intent and\nexecution. Link across layers instead of copying claims between them.\n\nFor a repository-wide documentation audit, substantial PRD, or cross-cutting\nharness change, read\n[repository-harness-contract.md](references/repository-harness-contract.md).\nIt routes to the complete local method and requires no external source lookup.\nLoad the applicable structured modules directly:\n\n- [contract map](references/harness/contract-map.md) for mode and lifecycle;\n- [invariant register](references/harness/invariant-register.md) for stable IDs;\npackages/calculators/README.md:36:  calculator input schemas for generated API docs and typed clients\npackages/calculators/README.md:88:- Keep service contracts separate from layer wiring. Do not export `Live`,\npackages/calculators/README.md:127:The [transport architecture](../../docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md) and active clean-slate plan own application use and proof limits.\npackages/calculators/README.md:129:## Shared calculation work limits\npackages/calculators/README.md:133:active calculations; each calculation in an RPC batch takes a separate place.\npackages/calculators/README.md:156:inside the operation budget. Per-client rate identity, rate limiting and future\napps/web/README.md:7:review_trigger: website rendering, settings, transport, form, generated types or build change\napps/web/README.md:14:in the separate API app. The current public docs app remains `apps/docs`.\napps/web/README.md:56:## Settings and generated owners\napps/web/README.md:61:reads semantic strings; Schema checks the native binding object separately.\napps/web/README.md:67:owns `src/worker-runtime.generated.d.ts`; regenerate it rather than editing it.\napps/web/README.md:73:bun run --filter=web generate:worker-types\napps/web/README.md:96:The public API and private binding use separate local isolates built from the\napps/web/README.md:126:matching native API binding; the separate Bun HTTP process cannot supply that\napps/web/README.md:143:qualification and safe exported telemetry remain separate unfinished tasks.\napps/web/README.md:149:ingress. The native function's generated URL is the exact admitted address;\napps/web/README.md:170:bounded batches, plus procedure decoding, version disagreement and expected\napps/web/README.md:181:the rest of that same reply for twelve seconds. The generated client must reach\napps/web/README.md:201:It separates the first visible page edit from exact source restoration by\napps/web/README.md:229:zero minimum is shown separately. Annual pages visibly state that retained\napps/web/README.md:251:request size and rate-limit errors before reading an error body. The calculator\napps/web/README.md:257:The [shared work policy](../../packages/calculators/README.md#shared-calculation-work-limits) gives the API instance one eight-calculation pool\napps/web/README.md:261:manual retry only. This is separate from the body-read and ten-second client\napps/web/README.md:266:control returns. Rate identity, per-client rate limits, MCP and full T004\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:15:packages. Both native app candidates now consume it. T003's bounded local\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:23:- `./errors`: bounded expected, unavailable, invalid-response and deadline errors.\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:43:its unknown request envelopes before native dispatch. Only bounded request IDs,\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:44:the declared procedure, a bounded batch and correctly shaped headers pass.\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:73:wider design and proof limits. Reusable content operations remain with T005;\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:89:The Website's local pair receipt separately records its native built artifacts\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:93:through the Website binding and Chromium form. Separate removal checks disable\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:96:trace-export proof. The native cancellation test separately qualifies the complete\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:100:is a separate unresolved decision. The canonical render receipt records its\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:107:version, body/batch limits, safe error/defect encoding, operation-scoped native\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:121:budget; metadata uses no calculation place. Per-client rate limits and later MCP\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:126:408, 413 and 429 become distinct checked errors with fixed safe codes, literal\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:128:unavailable. The request is scoped through headers and bounded body reading,\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:140:The [shared work policy](../../../packages/calculators/README.md#shared-calculation-work-limits) gives the API instance one eight-calculation pool\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:144:manual retry only. This is separate from the body-read and ten-second client\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:149:control returns. Rate identity, per-client rate limits, MCP and full T004\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:163:Schemas. One private concrete Effect transformation owns each generated native\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:176:Remaining body/work/rate and whole T004 requirements are separate; this slice\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:177:adds no rate identity, metadata operation budget, MCP or provider operation.\npackages/api/http/README.md:13:calculation endpoints, generated docs and API server route wiring.\npackages/api/http/README.md:17:`@taxkit/api-http` owns the current HTTP API contract, generated OpenAPI\npackages/api/http/README.md:85:generated OpenAPI exposes concrete supported fact shapes under `facts.anyOf`\npackages/api/http/README.md:192:`src/openapi.ts` is the single source for generated OpenAPI. The live\npackages/api/http/README.md:224:   schema references and generated calculator fact shapes.\npackages/api/http/README.md:272:2. Refresh the OpenAPI snapshot when generated route, status or schema\npackages/api/http/README.md:323:- Add OpenAPI annotations with new API groups so docs stay generated from the\npackages/api/http/README.md:348:the separate native app composition task; it is not native Worker lifetime proof.\npackages/api/http/README.md:350:The [shared work policy](../../../packages/calculators/README.md#shared-calculation-work-limits) gives the API instance one eight-calculation pool\npackages/api/http/README.md:354:manual retry only. This is separate from the body-read and ten-second client\npackages/api/http/README.md:359:control returns. Rate identity, per-client rate limits, MCP and full T004\napps/api/README.md:19:schemas, generated OpenAPI and docs routes stay in `packages/api/http`.\napps/api/README.md:47:discarded before console output. This is bounded containment; T009 still owns\napps/api/README.md:113:generated OpenAPI request body shows supported fact shapes under `facts.anyOf`;\napps/api/README.md:138:The retained standalone public API can be run separately:\napps/api/README.md:161:take-home-pay calculation and checks the generated OpenAPI document. It then\napps/api/README.md:191:coverage; failures report their bounded reason and available exit code.\napps/api/README.md:193:consumer deliberately uses ordinary JavaScript `fetch` and JSON to check a\napps/api/README.md:261:records the bounded observations.\napps/api/README.md:271:The [shared work policy](../../packages/calculators/README.md#shared-calculation-work-limits) gives the API instance one eight-calculation pool\napps/api/README.md:275:manual retry only. This is separate from the body-read and ten-second client\napps/api/README.md:280:control returns. Rate identity, per-client rate limits, MCP and full T004\n"},"started_at_ms":1791267005707,"completed_at_ms":1791267005707}}
