d-consumer-operation-owner` |\n| `recovery` | `docs/runbooks/recovery.md` | `taxkit-recovery-operation-owner` |\n| `docs-deployment` | `docs/runbooks/docs-deployment.md` | `taxkit-docs-deployment-operation-owner` |\n\nThese are exactly the five canonical TaxKit runbooks. Before any consequential\noperation, apply the [authority model](../operations/authority-model.md). Run\n`bun run check:runbooks` to inspect their structural and semantic contract. The\nvalidator executes no documented command and writes only the ignored bounded\nreceipt `tmp/runbook-validation-report.json`.\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:45:The active Doppler configuration governance SPEC authorises repository\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:49:config, service token or secret, or a GitHub or Cloudflare credential.\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:53:bridge, config or provider mutation must still name Cooper or another approved\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:54:TaxKit operator, the exact config and environment, least privilege, expiry,\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:55:rollback, revocation owner and names-only readback. Preview and Production are\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:59:shape only; it does not prove a Doppler config, bridge, hosted run or provider\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:66:direct Cloudflare pair from the Preview and Production GitHub environments,\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:73:same config, update only its matching bridge, read back metadata and then\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:102:configuration, hosted verification and cache-only rollback needed by TCC-001\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:146:TCC-004 applies that cache-only authority to the reviewed docs Preview,\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:150:Chromium caches. This does not add Cloudflare, Alchemy, mutation, artifact,\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:175:### 2026-08-20 — automatic Preview teardown admission\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:178:manual-recovery environment. The repository change may bind Preview deploy and\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:192:The accepted GitHub mutation read back zero Preview protection rules and the\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:196:Rollback restores the Preview reviewer rule and the former teardown environment\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:200:repository environment-list readback proved its absence. Preview retained its\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:204:### 2026-08-24 — Alchemy structure correction authority\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:209:is narrower: it permits only the existing docs Preview plan/bootstrap/state and\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:215:The Preview and Production workflow principals may expose\ndocs/operations/authority-model.md:218:non-cancellable `prod` group; Preview and teardown retain their exact `pr-N`\n---\ndocument_type: execution-plan\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: supporting\nowner: taxkit-implementation-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\nreview_trigger: local continuation, PR reconciliation, approval or dependency revision changes\n---\n\n# TaxKit local continuation prompt\n\nPaste the following into the local thread with this repository selected.\n\n## Task and authority\n\nContinue the approved TaxKit clean-slate improvements tracked in Linear DEV-72\nthrough DEV-81. Work only in `crcorbett/taxkit`. Cooper authorised implementation,\nreviewable commits, pushes, draft PRs and routine Linear tracking. The cloud task\nstopped at Cooper's explicit request to hand off locally; it did not complete the\nwhole rebuild. Do not treat this pause as cancellation or acceptance.\n\nRead `AGENTS.md`, `docs/README.md`, the current Commonplace Linear skill at\n`.agents/skills/linear/SKILL.md` and its applicable references, the strict Effect\nskill, and the relevant package/architecture instructions before editing. Use\n`docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md`, its sibling `.tasks.json`, and\n`docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md` as the current scope, dependency,\nacceptance and execution owners. Read live Linear issues, linked design and\ncomments, PR state and hosted checks before resuming. Retain native dependency\nrelations and distinguish implemented, tested, reviewed, merged and deployed.\n\nQ1–Q13 are settled. Cooper's current implementation request supersedes the old\nwhole-design Q14 hold. Do not ask for whole-design permission again. Verify\ntruly unresolved material choices. No merge, deployment, publication or provider\napply is authorised. Final provider-plan approval is a separate boundary.\n\n## Checkout and review stack\n\nFetch remote branches and inspect local changes before switching. The latest\nhandoff branch is `codex/dev-73-skill-test-boundaries`; use its remote HEAD,\nincluding this committed prompt. Review the stack instead of starting again\nfrom main or cherry-picking only its final commit. All listed PRs were drafts,\nunmerged and undeployed at handoff; refresh their live state.\n\n| PR | Branch | Implementation revision |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [88](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/88) | `codex/dev-72-clean-slate-foundation` | `771a506a071277f1f975672c4edaa9e32bf629b0` |\n| [89](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/89) | `codex/dev-73-stable-effect-qualification` | `59b0a36ff1bc6f95501734ee65d789a4f5a37fcc` |\n| [90](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/90) | `codex/dev-73-canonical-skills` | `b726afb556fcafdb929b41417a8b0cf4a4aec92c` |\n| [91](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/91) | `codex/dev-73-atom-and-enforcement` | `8549b92` |\n| [92](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/92) | `codex/dev-73-strict-domain` | `e7b9f0a5a1da09fbc22825ce5916f0ba1d2aac7a` |\n/* eslint-disable */\n// Generated by Wrangler by running `wrangler types --config=wrangler.jsonc --strict-vars=false src/worker-runtime.generated.d.ts` (hash: 563fd0424018dabb7b789dbe1be02752)\n// Runtime types generated with workerd@1.20261001.1 2026-10-04 nodejs_compat\ninterfa