ort state, retaining tax rules/results and explicit 2025-26/PAYG limits. Use the Q10-Q12 choices: an explicit Calculate button; edits mark the old answer stale and cancel old work; a main answer with expandable existing breakdown, assumptions, supported year and sources; a calculator-first homepage with clear developer and agent routes.\",\n        \"Give the SDK an explicit caller-owned lifetime at its plain Promise boundary and an Effect interface; remove the package-global runtime and generic client escapes.\",\n        \"Complete named RPC and public HTTP/OpenAPI operations, bounded body/work/concurrency/rate policy and checked expected failures. Limits and the same safe application owner apply to every transport and caller.\",\n        \"Update package examples, generated snapshots, export/consumer fixtures, supported-scope public copy and Changesets with the new interface.\",\n        \"Tighten retained core/rule/calculator code to the accepted immutable/declarative policy, including one owning Schema and its whole-record checks, fallible constrained constructors, Option for semantic absence with historical codecs preserved, checked configuration, persistent collections, closed named services and flat piping. Do not re-decode checked internal values or use JSON cache keys. Preserve all valid known results; remove only unjustified helper wrappers and keep semantic operation owners.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"apps/web calculator routes/feature containers/leaves and apps/api application operations\",\n        \"packages/calculators/**, packages/core/**, packages/rules/au/*/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/** and packages/sdk/typescript/** owning contracts/exports/tests/examples\",\n        \"Owning package/app READMEs, docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md, frontend.md, effect-services.md and appropriate .changeset/*.md\",\n        \"Local calculator/RPC/HTTP/OpenAPI/SDK consumer and privacy receipts\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/calculators test\",\n        \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\",\n        \"bun run sdk:check-packed-artifact\",\n        \"bun run sdk:validate-downstream\",\n        \"bun run api:smoke\",\n        \"bun run test\",\n        \"bun run changeset:status\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Exercise each supported calculator with representative valid and invalid values, all states, keyboard/focus and accessible result announcements.\",\n        \"Check latest-input-wins, cancelled calculations, navigation/unmount cleanup, no saved figures and no figures in URL/history/share metadata.\",\n        \"Prove explicit Calculate, stale-answer indication and cancellation on edits, accessible expandable breakdown/assumptions/sources and supported-year visibility, without exporting input or trace values to telemetry.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"Every existing calculator is usable and returns the retained result for the same valid inputs.\",\n        \"Unsupported years and expected failures have checked visible outcomes; UI copy does not imply wider tax support.\",\n        \"Packed consumers use only public exports and dispose the new caller-owned client; fresh interfaces are versioned deliberately.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-client-lifetime.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-stale-calculator-answer.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-take-home-explanation.json\",\n`bun run --filter=web dev` remains the standalone Website fixture. It needs a\nmatching native API binding; the separate Bun HTTP process cannot supply that\nbinding. The saved native suite also starts the real CLI pair with an isolated\nempty profile directory, reads its actual addresses, checks browser validation\nbefore live edits, restores both sources exactly, and verifies calculations\nwith and without JavaScript plus closed app ports after shutdown. Do not run\nit beside another development process in this checkout: both watch the same\nsources. Full exported telemetry and complete package/transport qualification remain active work.\n\n## Related owners\n\n- [Frontend architecture](../../docs/architecture/frontend.md)\n- [RPC package](../../packages/api/rpc/README.md)\n- [API app](../api/README.md)\n- [Native apps graph](../../packages/infrastructure/README.md)\n- [Active execution plan](../../docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md)\n\nRetained 2025–26 results are unchanged. The Medicare decision, complete package/transport\nqualification and safe exported telemetry remain separate unfinished tasks.\nT003's local connection, failure/cancellation and disabled-platform acceptance\nis recorded in the [acceptance review](../../docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-connection-acceptance-review.json).\n\nThe settings server function accepts GET without query data or client Context.\nThe shared explicit route base is configured in Vite and checked at Worker\nimport { declareNativeAppsStack, NativeAppsHostMode } from \"@taxkit/infrastructure/apps-stack\";\nimport * as Alchemy from \"alchemy\";\nimport * as Cloudflare from \"alchemy/Cloudflare\";\nimport { Config, ConfigProvider, Effect } from \"effect\";\n\n// This root owns disposable local app development only. It cannot select the\n// cloud app stack, Doppler configuration or Cloudflare state store.\nexport default Alchemy.Stack(\n  \"TaxKitAppsLocal\",\n  {\n    providers: Cloudflare.providers(),\n    state: Alchemy.localState(),\n  },\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const context = yield* Alchemy.AlchemyContext;\n    const stage = yield* Alchemy.Stage;\n    const dev = yield* Alchemy.ALCHEMY_DEV;\n    const mode = yield* Alchemy.ProviderMode.defaultProviderMode;\n    if (\n      !context.dev ||\n      !dev ||\n      mode !== \"local\" ||\n      (stage !== \"dev_native_apps\" && stage !== \"dev_native_apps_proof\")\n    ) {\n      return yield* Effect.fail(\n        new Config.ConfigError(\n          new ConfigProvider.SourceError({\n            message:\n              \"Native local apps require alchemy dev at stage dev_native_apps\",\n          })\n        )\n      );\n    }\n    const config = yield* ConfigProvider.ConfigProvider;\n    return yield* declareNativeAppsStack.pipe(\n      Effect.provideService(NativeAppsHostMode, \"local-emulator\"),\n      Effect.provideService(\n        ConfigProvider.ConfigProvider,\n        ConfigProvider.orElse(\n          // This root can only run in local emulation. This isolated local\n          // namespace is neither a cloud reservation nor a Production value.\n          ConfigProvider.fromUnknown({ CALCULATOR_RATE_NAMESPACE: \"10075\" }),\n          config\n        )\n      )\n    );\n  })\n);\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"web test:native-pair: \nweb test:native-pair:  RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/apps/web\nweb test:native-pair: \n      \"id\": \"CSF-T004\",\n      \"title\": \"Finish calculator pages and the fresh package interface\",\n      \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-001\",\n        \"CSF-004\",\n        \"CSF-005\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T003\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Every existing calculator is usable and returns the retained result for the same valid inputs.\",\n      \"scope\": [