{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:15:10.757Z","ordinal":39658,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac491ec899887d083be28c244816828","status":"completed","call_id":"call_K69Vve1Hy2fo0NKIrUXswvCG","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg -n -A 18 '\\\"id\\\": \\\"CSF-T009\\\"' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json; cat packages/docs-content/content/api/errors.mdx; cat .changeset/shared-request-operation-protections.md; sed -n '1,85p' tools/sdk-packed-artifact/public-interface.typecheck.ts 2>/dev/null; rg --files tools packages/sdk | rg 'packed.*(type|proof)|consumer.*type' | head -n 15\",\"max_output_tokens\":3400}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git diff --stat; git diff --check\",\"max_output_tokens\":1500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","create_time":1791267292.449781}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:15:10.839Z","ordinal":39659,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b86bd92d-2aac-4dd2-907b-8840a5eb0530","process_id":"84687","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -A 18 '\"id\": \"CSF-T009\"' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json; cat packages/docs-content/content/api/errors.mdx; cat .changeset/shared-request-operation-protections.md; sed -n '1,85p' tools/sdk-packed-artifact/public-interface.typecheck.ts 2>/dev/null; rg --files tools packages/sdk | rg 'packed.*(type|proof)|consumer.*type' | head -n 15"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -A 18 '\"id\": \"CSF-T009\"' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json; cat packages/docs-content/content/api/errors.mdx; cat .changeset/shared-request-operation-protections.md; sed -n '1,85p' tools/sdk-packed-artifact/public-interface.typecheck.ts 2>/dev/null; rg --files tools packages/sdk | rg 'packed.*(type|proof)|consumer.*type' | head -n 15"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"741:      \"id\": \"CSF-T009\",\n742-      \"title\": \"Implement shared Axiom logs, traces, metrics and dashboards\",\n743-      \"status\": \"pending\",\n744-      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n745-      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n746-      \"requirementIds\": [\n747-        \"CSF-009\"\n748-      ],\n749-      \"dependsOn\": [\n750-        \"CSF-T003\",\n751-        \"CSF-T004\",\n752-        \"CSF-T006\"\n753-      ],\n754-      \"goal\": \"Exactly the three existing datasets are used; no retained foreign resource or retention setting is changed.\",\n755-      \"scope\": [\n756-        \"Reference Site's three retained dataset outputs from CooperCorbettSiteCloudflare/prod, never declare/adopt/change them; provision only TaxKit-owned retained ingest token, destination and dashboards under a reviewed plan.\",\n757-        \"Use one canonical TaxKit identity/query owner and explicit native Worker mapping; separate logs/traces revision/request fields from bounded metric labels. Implement the SPEC's minimum request/calculation logs, named service spans, request/calculation counters and millisecond histograms with the stated boundaries; never label root-span/flush duration visitor response time.\",\n758-        \"Keep one qualified native trace owner and event-scoped native Effect log/metric exporters with correct endpoints/Protobuf/header, bounded host completion and safe warning projections.\",\n759-        \"Prove a closed safe field policy across application and automatic traces. Qualify URL-field suppression or the candidate safe-native-span fallback on the exact version, including inbound/outbound spans, Axiom and retained Cloudflare storage. If privacy cannot be met, keep that path disabled, record CSF-009 as unmet and resolve a reviewed design change; do not claim safe native spans survived or silently add a competing exporter.\"\n---\ntitle: \"API errors\"\ndescription: \"Handle expected calculator service failures returned by the HTTP API.\"\nstatus: \"draft\"\n---\n\n# API errors\n\nThe HTTP API wraps expected calculator service failures in\n`CalculatorApiErrorEnvelope`. The `error` field is the canonical\n`CalculatorServiceError` union from the calculator package.\n\n## Error model\n\n```json\n{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"_tag\": \"CalculatorInputDecodeError\",\n    \"calculatorId\": \"au.pay.take-home\",\n    \"message\": \"Invalid facts for au.pay.take-home\",\n    \"issues\": [\n      {\n        \"_tag\": \"CalculatorInputIssue\",\n        \"message\": \"Expected GrossPay\",\n        \"path\": [\"grossPay\"]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nExpected failures stay in the service error channel. The current public union\nincludes calculator input decode failures, unsupported calculator errors,\nunsupported calculator context errors and calculation errors. Those request\nfailures use HTTP 400. A busy calculation server returns HTTP 503 with\n`CalculatorCapacityExceeded`. An operation that exceeds five seconds returns\nHTTP 504 with `CalculatorOperationTimedOut`. Both include a fixed `code`,\n`message` and `retry: \"try-again-manually\"`. Display the message and let the\ncaller choose when to retry; do not automatically repeat calculations.\n\nThe server shares eight active calculation places across HTTP and RPC. Each\ncalculation in a batch takes a place. This budget does not claim that a\nJavaScript timer can forcibly stop synchronous CPU work. Current per-client\nrate limiting remains under implementation; these work limits do not establish\nthat separate policy.\n\n## Handle an error response\n\n```ts\ntype ApiErrorEnvelope = {\n  error: {\n    _tag: string;\n    message: string;\n    issues?: ReadonlyArray<{ path: ReadonlyArray<string>; message: string }>;\n  };\n};\n\nconst response = await fetch(\n  \"http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate\",\n  {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" },\n    body: JSON.stringify({\n      facts: {\n        taxableIncome: { _tag: \"Money\", cents: 9000000, currency: \"AUD\" },\n      },\n      jurisdiction: \"AU\",\n      taxYear: \"2025-26\",\n    }),\n  }\n);\n\nif (!response.ok) {\n  const body = (await response.json()) as ApiErrorEnvelope;\n  console.error(body.error._tag, body.error.message);\n  for (const issue of body.error.issues ?? []) {\n    console.error(issue.path.join(\".\"), issue.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nExpected output for this shape is a `CalculatorInputDecodeError` because annual\nincome facts are not valid facts for `au.pay.take-home`.\n\n## Add help\n\nAppend `?help=errors` when you want descriptor-backed help for invalid input:\n\n```txt\nPOST /api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate?help=errors\n```\n\nThe help data comes from canonical fact descriptors. Do not maintain a\nseparate application copy of calculator fields.\n\n## Related pages\n\n- [Handle validation errors](../guides/handle-validation-errors.mdx)\n- [Show calculator help to users](../guides/show-calculator-help-to-users.mdx)\n- [Schemas](../sdk/schemas.mdx)\n---\n\"@taxkit/calculators\": major\n\"@taxkit/api-http\": major\n\"@taxkit/api-rpc\": major\n\"@taxkit/sdk\": major\n---\n\nApply the server's five-second operation budget to all metadata methods without\nusing calculation places. Export the canonical metadata timeout error union.\nMove shared streamed request admission into the HTTP package, mount it in the\nstandalone server and return fixed checked JSON 413/408 guidance or safe HTML\nform guidance. Declare HTTP metadata 504 and calculation 408/413 responses.\nRetain the RPC body export alias, existing RPC revision and tax results.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"741:      \"id\": \"CSF-T009\",\n742-      \"title\": \"Implement shared Axiom logs, traces, metrics and dashboards\",\n743-      \"status\": \"pending\",\n744-      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n745-      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n746-      \"requirementIds\": [\n747-        \"CSF-009\"\n748-      ],\n749-      \"dependsOn\": [\n750-        \"CSF-T003\",\n751-        \"CSF-T004\",\n752-        \"CSF-T006\"\n753-      ],\n754-      \"goal\": \"Exactly the three existing datasets are used; no retained foreign resource or retention setting is changed.\",\n755-      \"scope\": [\n756-        \"Reference Site's three retained dataset outputs from CooperCorbettSiteCloudflare/prod, never declare/adopt/change them; provision only TaxKit-owned retained ingest token, destination and dashboards under a reviewed plan.\",\n757-        \"Use one canonical TaxKit identity/query owner and explicit native Worker mapping; separate logs/traces revision/request fields from bounded metric labels. Implement the SPEC's minimum request/calculation logs, named service spans, request/calculation counters and millisecond histograms with the stated boundaries; never label root-span/flush duration visitor response time.\",\n758-        \"Keep one qualified native trace owner and event-scoped native Effect log/metric exporters with correct endpoints/Protobuf/header, bounded host completion and safe warning projections.\",\n759-        \"Prove a closed safe field policy across application and automatic traces. Qualify URL-field suppression or the candidate safe-native-span fallback on the exact version, including inbound/outbound spans, Axiom and retained Cloudflare storage. If privacy cannot be met, keep that path disabled, record CSF-009 as unmet and resolve a reviewed design change; do not claim safe native spans survived or silently add a competing exporter.\"\n---\ntitle: \"API errors\"\ndescription: \"Handle expected calculator service failures returned by the HTTP API.\"\nstatus: \"draft\"\n---\n\n# API errors\n\nThe HTTP API wraps expected calculator service failures in\n`CalculatorApiErrorEnvelope`. The `error` field is the canonical\n`CalculatorServiceError` union from the calculator package.\n\n## Error model\n\n```json\n{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"_tag\": \"CalculatorInputDecodeError\",\n    \"calculatorId\": \"au.pay.take-home\",\n    \"message\": \"Invalid facts for au.pay.take-home\",\n    \"issues\": [\n      {\n        \"_tag\": \"CalculatorInputIssue\",\n        \"message\": \"Expected GrossPay\",\n        \"path\": [\"grossPay\"]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nExpected failures stay in the service error channel. The current public union\nincludes calculator input decode failures, unsupported calculator errors,\nunsupported calculator context errors and calculation errors. Those request\nfailures use HTTP 400. A busy calculation server returns HTTP 503 with\n`CalculatorCapacityExceeded`. An operation that exceeds five seconds returns\nHTTP 504 with `CalculatorOperationTimedOut`. Both include a fixed `code`,\n`message` and `retry: \"try-again-manually\"`. Display the message and let the\ncaller choose when to retry; do not automatically repeat calculations.\n\nThe server shares eight active calculation places across HTTP and RPC. Each\ncalculation in a batch takes a place. This budget does not claim that a\nJavaScript timer can forcibly stop synchronous CPU work. Current per-client\nrate limiting remains under implementation; these work limits do not establish\nthat separate policy.\n\n## Handle an error response\n\n```ts\ntype ApiErrorEnvelope = {\n  error: {\n    _tag: string;\n    message: string;\n    issues?: ReadonlyArray<{ path: ReadonlyArray<string>; message: string }>;\n  };\n};\n\nconst response = await fetch(\n  \"http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate\",\n  {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" },\n    body: JSON.stringify({\n      facts: {\n        taxableIncome: { _tag: \"Money\", cents: 9000000, currency: \"AUD\" },\n      },\n      jurisdiction: \"AU\",\n      taxYear: \"2025-26\",\n    }),\n  }\n);\n\nif (!response.ok) {\n  const body = (await response.json()) as ApiErrorEnvelope;\n  console.error(body.error._tag, body.error.message);\n  for (const issue of body.error.issues ?? []) {\n    console.error(issue.path.join(\".\"), issue.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nExpected output for this shape is a `CalculatorInputDecodeError` because annual\nincome facts are not valid facts for `au.pay.take-home`.\n\n## Add help\n\nAppend `?help=errors` when you want descriptor-backed help for invalid input:\n\n```txt\nPOST /api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate?help=errors\n```\n\nThe help data comes from canonical fact descriptors. Do not maintain a\nseparate application copy of calculator fields.\n\n## Related pages\n\n- [Handle validation errors](../guides/handle-validation-errors.mdx)\n- [Show calculator help to users](../guides/show-calculator-help-to-users.mdx)\n- [Schemas](../sdk/schemas.mdx)\n---\n\"@taxkit/calculators\": major\n\"@taxkit/api-http\": major\n\"@taxkit/api-rpc\": major\n\"@taxkit/sdk\": major\n---\n\nApply the server's five-second operation budget to all metadata methods without\nusing calculation places. Export the canonical metadata timeout error union.\nMove shared streamed request admission into the HTTP package, mount it in the\nstandalone server and return fixed checked JSON 413/408 guidance or safe HTML\nform guidance. Declare HTTP metadata 504 and calculation 408/413 responses.\nRetain the RPC body export alias, existing RPC revision and tax results.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7333},"formatted_output":"741:      \"id\": \"CSF-T009\",\n742-      \"title\": \"Implement shared Axiom logs, traces, metrics and dashboards\",\n743-      \"status\": \"pending\",\n744-      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n745-      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n746-      \"requirementIds\": [\n747-        \"CSF-009\"\n748-      ],\n749-      \"dependsOn\": [\n750-        \"CSF-T003\",\n751-        \"CSF-T004\",\n752-        \"CSF-T006\"\n753-      ],\n754-      \"goal\": \"Exactly the three existing datasets are used; no retained foreign resource or retention setting is changed.\",\n755-      \"scope\": [\n756-        \"Reference Site's three retained dataset outputs from CooperCorbettSiteCloudflare/prod, never declare/adopt/change them; provision only TaxKit-owned retained ingest token, destination and dashboards under a reviewed plan.\",\n757-        \"Use one canonical TaxKit identity/query owner and explicit native Worker mapping; separate logs/traces revision/request fields from bounded metric labels. Implement the SPEC's minimum request/calculation logs, named service spans, request/calculation counters and millisecond histograms with the stated boundaries; never label root-span/flush duration visitor response time.\",\n758-        \"Keep one qualified native trace owner and event-scoped native Effect log/metric exporters with correct endpoints/Protobuf/header, bounded host completion and safe warning projections.\",\n759-        \"Prove a closed safe field policy across application and automatic traces. Qualify URL-field suppression or the candidate safe-native-span fallback on the exact version, including inbound/outbound spans, Axiom and retained Cloudflare storage. If privacy cannot be met, keep that path disabled, record CSF-009 as unmet and resolve a reviewed design change; do not claim safe native spans survived or silently add a competing exporter.\"\n---\ntitle: \"API errors\"\ndescription: \"Handle expected calculator service failures returned by the HTTP API.\"\nstatus: \"draft\"\n---\n\n# API errors\n\nThe HTTP API wraps expected calculator service failures in\n`CalculatorApiErrorEnvelope`. The `error` field is the canonical\n`CalculatorServiceError` union from the calculator package.\n\n## Error model\n\n```json\n{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"_tag\": \"CalculatorInputDecodeError\",\n    \"calculatorId\": \"au.pay.take-home\",\n    \"message\": \"Invalid facts for au.pay.take-home\",\n    \"issues\": [\n      {\n        \"_tag\": \"CalculatorInputIssue\",\n        \"message\": \"Expected GrossPay\",\n        \"path\": [\"grossPay\"]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nExpected failures stay in the service error channel. The current public union\nincludes calculator input decode failures, unsupported calculator errors,\nunsupported calculator context errors and calculation errors. Those request\nfailures use HTTP 400. A busy calculation server returns HTTP 503 with\n`CalculatorCapacityExceeded`. An operation that exceeds five seconds returns\nHTTP 504 with `CalculatorOperationTimedOut`. Both include a fixed `code`,\n`message` and `retry: \"try-again-manually\"`. Display the message and let the\ncaller choose when to retry; do not automatically repeat calculations.\n\nThe server shares eight active calculation places across HTTP and RPC. Each\ncalculation in a batch takes a place. This budget does not claim that a\nJavaScript timer can forcibly stop synchronous CPU work. Current per-client\nrate limiting remains under implementation; these work limits do not establish\nthat separate policy.\n\n## Handle an error response\n\n```ts\ntype ApiErrorEnvelope = {\n  error: {\n    _tag: string;\n    message: string;\n    issues?: ReadonlyArray<{ path: ReadonlyArray<string>; message: string }>;\n  };\n};\n\nconst response = await fetch(\n  \"http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate\",\n  {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" },\n    body: JSON.stringify({\n      facts: {\n        taxableIncome: { _tag: \"Money\", cents: 9000000, currency: \"AUD\" },\n      },\n      jurisdiction: \"AU\",\n      taxYear: \"2025-26\",\n    }),\n  }\n);\n\nif (!response.ok) {\n  const body = (await response.json()) as ApiErrorEnvelope;\n  console.error(body.error._tag, body.error.message);\n  for (const issue of body.error.issues ?? []) {\n    console.error(issue.path.join(\".\"), issue.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nExpected output for this shape is a `CalculatorInputDecodeError` because annual\nincome facts are not valid facts for `au.pay.take-home`.\n\n## Add help\n\nAppend `?help=errors` when you want descriptor-backed help for invalid input:\n\n```txt\nPOST /api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate?help=errors\n```\n\nThe help data comes from canonical fact descriptors. Do not maintain a\nseparate application copy of calculator fields.\n\n## Related pages\n\n- [Handle validation errors](../guides/handle-validation-errors.mdx)\n- [Show calculator help to users](../guides/show-calculator-help-to-users.mdx)\n- [Schemas](../sdk/schemas.mdx)\n---\n\"@taxkit/calculators\": major\n\"@taxkit/api-http\": major\n\"@taxkit/api-rpc\": major\n\"@taxkit/sdk\": major\n---\n\nApply the server's five-second operation budget to all metadata methods without\nusing calculation places. Export the canonical metadata timeout error union.\nMove shared streamed request admission into the HTTP package, mount it in the\nstandalone server and return fixed checked JSON 413/408 guidance or safe HTML\nform guidance. Declare HTTP metadata 504 and calculation 408/413 responses.\nRetain the RPC body export alias, existing RPC revision and tax results.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791267310838,"completed_at_ms":1791267310838}}
