            | 16 +++-\n apps/api/README.md                                 | 32 +++++++-\n apps/api/src/worker.application.ts                 | 91 ++++++++++++++++++++--\n apps/api/src/worker.ts                             | 24 +++++-\n apps/api/test/worker.boundary.test.ts              | 15 +++-\n apps/web/README.md                                 | 32 +++++++-\n apps/web/scripts/native-pair-build.runtime.ts      | 70 +++++++----------\n apps/web/src/lib/calculation-failure.ts            |  3 +-\n .../src/lib/calculator.boundary.browser.test.tsx   |  4 +-\n apps/web/src/lib/config.boundary.test.ts           |  2 +-\n apps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts                  | 15 ++--\n apps/web/src/lib/live.server.layer.ts              | 60 ++++++++++++--\n apps/web/src/server.ts                             |  6 ++\n apps/web/test/native-cancellation.boundary.test.ts |  5 ++\n .../test/native-local-development.boundary.test.ts |  2 +-\n apps/web/test/native-pair.boundary.test.ts         |  6 ++\n apps/web/test/native-rpc-failures.boundary.test.ts |  6 ++\n apps/web/vitest.native.config.ts                   |  1 +\n docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md                   | 35 ++++++++-\n docs/architecture/effect-services.md               | 28 +++++++\n docs/architecture/frontend.md                      | 28 +++++++\n docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md   | 62 +++++++++++++++\n docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md       | 24 +++++-\n packages/api/http/README.md                        | 30 ++++++-\n packages/api/http/src/groups/calculators.ts        | 17 ++++\n packages/api/http/src/handlers/calculators.ts      |  8 ++\n packages/api/rpc/README.md                         | 36 ++++++++-\n packages/api/rpc/package.json                      |  5 ++\n packages/api/rpc/src/client-response.boundary.ts   |  4 +-\n packages/api/rpc/src/errors.ts                     | 19 ++---\n packages/api/rpc/src/handlers.ts                   |  2 +\n packages/api/rpc/src/schemas.ts                    |  2 +-\n packages/api/rpc/test/handlers.test.ts             |  4 +-\n packages/calculators/README.md                     | 41 +++++++++-\n packages/calculators/package.json                  | 27 +++++++\n packages/calculators/src/index.ts                  |  2 +\n packages/calculators/src/schemas.ts                | 24 ++++++\n packages/infrastructure/README.md                  | 25 +++++-\n packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.test.ts     | 20 ++++-\n packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.ts          | 14 +++-\n 40 files changed, 737 insertions(+), 110 deletions(-)\n"},"started_at_ms":1791267310988,"completed_at_ms":1791267310988}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:15:11.039Z","ordinal":39662,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10fda-0dbf-75e2-80e0-05dab0499930","call_id":"call_K69Vve1Hy2fo0NKIrUXswvCG","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"c33a24\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007333,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1354,\"output\":\"741:      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CSF-T009\\\",\\n742-      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Implement shared Axiom logs, traces, metrics and dashboards\\\",\\n743-      \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\",\\n744-      \\\"type\\\": \\\"vertical-slice\\\",\\n745-      \\\"acceptedFindingIds\\\": [],\\n746-      \\\"requirementIds\\\": [\\n747-        \\\"CSF-009\\\"\\n748-      ],\\n749-      \\\"dependsOn\\\": [\\n750-        \\\"CSF-T003\\\",\\n751-        \\\"CSF-T004\\\",\\n752-        \\\"CSF-T006\\\"\\n753-      ],\\n754-      \\\"goal\\\": \\\"Exactly the three existing datasets are used; no retained foreign resource or retention setting is changed.\\\",\\n755-      \\\"scope\\\": [\\n756-        \\\"Reference Site's three retained dataset outputs from CooperCorbettSiteCloudflare/prod, never declare/adopt/change them; provision only TaxKit-owned retained ingest token, destination and dashboards under a reviewed plan.\\\",\\n757-        \\\"Use one canonical TaxKit identity/query owner and explicit native Worker mapping; separate logs/traces revision/request fields from bounded metric labels. Implement the SPEC's minimum request/calculation logs, named service spans, request/calculation counters and millisecond histograms with the stated boundaries; never label root-span/flush duration visitor response time.\\\",\\n758-        \\\"Keep one qualified native trace owner and event-scoped native Effect log/metric exporters with correct endpoints/Protobuf/header, bounded host completion and safe warning projections.\\\",\\n759-        \\\"Prove a closed safe field policy across application and automatic traces. Qualify URL-field suppression or the candidate safe-native-span fallback on the exact version, including inbound/outbound spans, Axiom and retained Cloudflare storage. If privacy cannot be met, keep that path disabled, record CSF-009 as unmet and resolve a reviewed design change; do not claim safe native spans survived or silently add a competing exporter.\\\"\\n---\\ntitle: \\\"API errors\\\"\\ndescription: \\\"Handle expected calculator service failures returned by the HTTP API.\\\"\\nstatus: \\\"draft\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# API errors\\n\\nThe HTTP API wraps expected calculator service failures in\\n`CalculatorApiErrorEnvelope`. The `error` field is the canonical\\n`CalculatorServiceError` union from the calculator package.\\n\\n## Error model\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"error\\\": {\\n    \\\"_tag\\\": \\\"CalculatorInputDecodeError\\\",\\n    \\\"calculatorId\\\": \\\"au.pay.take-home\\\",\\n    \\\"message\\\": \\\"Invalid facts for au.pay.take-home\\\",\\n    \\\"issues\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"_tag\\\": \\\"CalculatorInputIssue\\\",\\n        \\\"message\\\": \\\"Expected GrossPay\\\",\\n        \\\"path\\\": [\\\"grossPay\\\"]\\n      }\\n    ]\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nExpected failures stay in the service error channel. The current public union\\nincludes calculator input decode failures, unsupported calculator errors,\\nunsupported calculator context errors and calculation errors. Those request\\nfailures use HTTP 400. A busy calculation server returns HTTP 503 with\\n`CalculatorCapacityExceeded`. An operation that exceeds five seconds returns\\nHTTP 504 with `CalculatorOperationTimedOut`. Both include a fixed `code`,\\n`message` and `retry: \\\"try-again-manually\\\"`. Display the message and let the\\ncaller choose when to retry; do not automatically repeat calculations.\\n\\nThe server shares eight active calculation places across HTTP and RPC. Each\\ncalculation in a batch takes a place. This budget does not claim that a\\nJavaScript timer can forcibly stop synchronous CPU work. Current per-client\\nrate limiting remains under implementation; these work limits do not establish\\nthat separate policy.\\n\\n## Handle an error response\\n\\n```ts\\ntype ApiErrorEnvelope = {\\n  error: {\\n    _tag: string;\\n    message: string;\\n    issues?: ReadonlyArray<{ path: ReadonlyArray<string>; message: string }>;\\n  };\\n};\\n\\nconst response = await fetch(\\n  \\\"http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate\\\",\\n  {\\n    method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n    headers: { \\\"content-type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({\\n      facts: {\\n        taxableIncome: { _tag: \\\"Money\\\", cents: 9000000, currency: \\\"AUD\\\" },\\n      },\\n      jurisdiction: \\\"AU\\\",\\n      taxYear: \\\"2025-26\\\",\\n    }),\\n  }\\n);\\n\\nif (!response.ok) {\\n  const body = (await response.json()) as ApiErrorEnvelope;\\n  console.error(body.error._tag, body.error.message);\\n  for (const issue of body.error.issues ?? []) {\\n    console.error(issue.path.join(\\\".\\\"), issue.message);\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nExpected output for this shape is a `CalculatorInputDecodeError` because annual\\nincome facts are not valid facts for `au.pay.take-home`.\\n\\n## Add help\\n\\nAppend `?help=errors` when you want descriptor-backed help for invalid input:\\n\\n```txt\\nPOST /api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate?help=errors\\n```\\n\\nThe help data comes from canonical fact descriptors. Do not maintain a\\nseparate application copy of calculator fields.\\n\\n## Related pages\\n\\n- [Handle validation errors](../guides/handle-validation-errors.mdx)\\n- [Show calculator help to users](../guides/show-calculator-help-to-users.mdx)\\n- [Schemas](../sdk/schemas.mdx)\\n---\\n\\\"@taxkit/calculators\\\": major\\n\\\"@taxkit/api-http\\\": major\\n\\\"@taxkit/api-rpc\\\": major\\n\\\"@taxkit/sdk\\\": major\\n---\\n\\nApply the server's five-second operation budget to all metadata methods without\\nusing calculation places. Export the canonical metadata timeout error union.\\nMove shared streamed request admission into the HTTP package, mount it in the\\nstandalone server and return fixed checked JSON 413/408 guidance or safe HTML\\nform guidance. Declare HTTP metadata 504 and calculation 408/413 responses.\\nRetain the RPC body export alias, existing RPC revision and tax results.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"8f01d5\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007666,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":650,\"output\":\" alchemy.apps.local.run.ts                          | 16 +++-\\n apps/api/README.md                                 | 32 +++++++-\\n apps/api/src/worker.application.ts                 | 91 ++++++++++++++++++++--\\n apps/api/src/worker.ts                             | 24 +++++-\\n apps/api/test/worker.boundary.test.ts              | 15 +++-\\n apps/web/README.md                                 | 32 +++++++-\\n apps/web/scripts/native-pair-build.runtime.ts      | 70 +++++++----------\\n apps/web/src/lib/calculation-failure.ts            |  3 +-\\n .../src/lib/calculator.boundary.browser.test.tsx   |  4 +-\\n apps/web/src/lib/config.boundary.test.ts           |  2 +-\\n apps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts                  | 15 ++--\\n apps/web/src/lib/live.server.layer.ts              | 60 ++++++++++++--\\n apps/web/src/server.ts                             |  6 ++\\n apps/web/test/native-cancellation.boundary.test.ts |  5 ++\\n .../test/native-local-development.boundary.test.ts |  2 +-\\n apps/web/test/native-pair.boundary.test.ts         |  6 ++\\n apps/web/test/native-rpc-failures.boundary.test.ts |  6 ++\\n apps/web/vitest.native.config.ts                   |  1 +\\n docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md                   | 35 ++++++++-\\n docs/architecture/effect-services.md               | 28 +++++++\\n docs/architecture/frontend.md                      | 28 +++++++\\n docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md   | 62 +++++++++++++++\\n docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md       | 24 +++++-\\n packages/api/http/README.md                        | 30 ++++++-\\n packages/api/http/src/groups/calculators.ts        | 17 ++++\\n packages/api/http/src/handlers/calculators.ts      |  8 ++\\n packages/api/rpc/README.md                         | 36 ++++++++-\\n packages/api/rpc/package.json                      |  5 ++\\n packages/api/rpc/src/client-response.boundary.ts   |  4 +-\\n packages/api/rpc/src/errors.ts                     | 19 ++---\\n packages/api/rpc/src/handlers.ts                   |  2 +\\n packages/api/rpc/src/schemas.ts                    |  2 +-\\n packages/api/rpc/test/handlers.test.ts             |  4 +-\\n packages/calculators/README.md                     | 41 +++++++++-\\n packages/calculators/package.json                  | 27 +++++++\\n packages/calculators/src/index.ts                  |  2 +\\n packages/calculators/src/schemas.ts                | 24 ++++++\\n packages/infrastructure/README.md                  | 25 +++++-\\n packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.test.ts     | 20 ++++-\\n packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.ts          | 14 +++-\\n 40 files changed, 737 insertions(+), 110 deletions(-)\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","create_time":1791267311.039833}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:15:11.040Z","ordinal":39663,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":751900060,"cached_input_tokens":736485632,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3188160,"reasoning_output_tokens":1509783,"total_tokens":755088220},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":174192,"cached_input_tokens":170624,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":657,"reasoning_output_tokens":461,"total_tokens":174849},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":76.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1791592581},"secondary":null,"credits":{"has_credits":true,"unlimited":false,"balance":"63000"},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":"pro","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:15:27.789Z","ordinal":39664,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac491f1533887d09ce7c869915d89eb","summary_text":[],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1791267313349,"completed_at_ms":1791267327789}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:15:27.797Z","ordinal":39665,"type":"response_item","payload":{"id":"rs_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac491f1533887d09ce7c869915d89eb","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:16:07.659Z","ordinal":39666,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac491ffaac087d0a29126b4f382ec5e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_yxwOCYZ6nGtUKTQ4taZdpfeU","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nowners={\\n'packages/api/http/README.md':'''The [calculator-owned rate contract](../../calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) adds canonical rate/unavailable errors to calculation responses. The native API maps them to HTTP 429 with `Retry-After: 60` and fixed 503 guidance, using the existing error envelope. Metadata consumes no rate unit. Owning group Schemas drive generated clients and the OpenAPI snapshot; the standalone Bun host keeps its existing policy.\\\\n''',\\n'packages/api/rpc/README.md':'''Revision `4` preserves canonical `CalculatorRateLimited` and `CalculatorAdmissionUnavailable` alongside existing expected errors. Older clients receive the checked revision mismatch. The native API and Website share the [calculator-owned rate contract](../../calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission); each batch calculation takes one unit and metadata takes none. `./rate-identity` is an explicit workspace-only host export; it is excluded from the published RPC capability surface. The rate identity is separate from RPC request JSON and is never an analytics identifier.\\\\n''',\\n'apps/api/README.md':'''The native API builds `PublicCalculatorServiceRateLimited` once underneath its bounded service. HTTP/RPC and the binding-only `calculatorRequest` operation share the [calculator-owned rate contract](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission). Public requests need a checked original Cloudflare connection address; forwarded Worker calls and arbitrary forwarded headers cannot select a key. The Website private call supplies its checked key separately from JSON; no HTTP route admits that argument. The closed reply is buffered inside the native event scope, bounded to 2 MiB and ten seconds.\\\\n\\\\n`ApiCalculatorAdmissionLive` uses the installed native RateLimit Layer, decodes each provider reply and returns fixed unavailable guidance for provider failures or invalid replies. It requires `CALCULATOR_RATE_NAMESPACE` as a positive decimal string. The operator must select an account-wide unique stage value before a cloud plan/apply; no provider value is invented. The [infrastructure owner](../../packages/infrastructure/README.md#native-calculation-limiter-configuration) owns graph and local-root selection. Hosted mode defaults to `edge`. The guarded local root selects `local-emulator`; a shared local allowance additionally requires an HTTP loopback API origin.\\\\n\\\\nCloudflare's [rate limiter](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/bindings/rate-limit/) is approximate and local to a location, not an exact global quota. Real edge identity, namespace uniqueness and uploaded provider settings need separate authorised readback. Direct engine/local SDK and standalone Bun execution keep their existing contracts.\\\\n''',\\n'apps/web/README.md':'''The API and Website use the [calculator-owned rate contract](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission). The Website checks its original Cloudflare connection address and supplies it separately from request JSON to the binding-only `calculatorRequest` operation. The installed Alchemy native RPC adapter owns private-call reply handling. Both browser and restored HTML forms display fixed rate/unavailable guidance and never retry automatically.\\\\n\\\\nThe private request omits an explicit AbortSignal because the pinned native RPC cannot serialise it. Client cancellation stops local waiting; API work and reply budgets remain in force. This does not prove remote cancellation. The guarded disposable root selects `local-emulator` and one loopback allowance; hosted composition defaults to `edge`. [Infrastructure configuration](../../packages/infrastructure/README.md#native-calculation-limiter-configuration) owns this distinction.\\\\n''',\\n'docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md':'''The [calculator rate owner](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) defines canonical errors and a redacted IP key. The [native API](../../apps/api/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) composes admission once below bounded work, so HTTP/RPC/private Website calls share an allowance and each batch member takes one unit. Metadata remains independent. HTTP uses 429 with `Retry-After: 60` or fixed 503 guidance; RPC revision 4 preserves the same errors. The standalone Bun host and local engine/SDK keep their existing behaviour. Packed declarations must expose the expanded checked error union without adding private host identity capabilities to the published RPC exports.\\\\n''',\\n'docs/architecture/effect-services.md':'''`CalculatorAdmission` is a closed named service; its [owning contract](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) and redacted key Schema live with calculators. The request Context reference carries checked identity separately from facts. `PublicCalculatorServiceRateLimited` provides calculation-only admission; the native API composes it once below bounded work. Its provider Layer, installed live Layer and mock test Layer remain separate. Native provider replies are decoded immediately and failures become fixed errors without provider causes or addresses.\\\\n''',\\n'docs/architecture/frontend.md':'''The [Website owner](../../apps/web/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) captures checked original connection identity and uses the API's binding-only named operation for HTML forms. Browser calculations use public RPC. Both reach the same [calculator-owned allowance](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission), including separate batch members. Containers show fixed safe guidance with manual retry. This adds no calculation engine, stored figures, analytics identity or URL data to the Website. Private-call local cancellation and remote work limits remain distinct.\\\\n''',\\n}\\nfor name,body in owners.items():\\n p=Path(name);s=p.read_text();a=s.rindex('\\\\n\\\\n## Native calculation rate admission');p.write_text(s[:a]+'\\\\n\\\\n## Native calculation rate admission\\\\n\\\\n'+body)\\np=Path('packages/docs-content/content/api/errors.mdx');s=p.read_text().replace('rate limiting remains under implementation; these work limits do not establish\\\\nthat separate policy.','rate admission in the native API adds 60 calculations per minute per checked\\\\nconnection address across HTTP, RPC and Website forms. Every batch calculation\\\\ncounts separately; metadata reads do not count. A rejected calculation returns\\\\nHTTP 429 with `CalculatorRateLimited` and `Retry-After: 60`. Missing/invalid\\\\nconnection identity or a failed limiter returns HTTP 503 with\\\\n`CalculatorAdmissionUnavailable`. Both contain fixed safe guidance and manual\\\\nretry fields. These native limits are approximate and local to a Cloudflare\\\\nlocation, rather than an exact worldwide quota. The standalone Bun server\\\\nkeeps its existing work policy.');p.write_text(s)\\np=Path('.changeset/native-calculation-rate-admission.md');p.write_text('''---\\\\n\\\"@taxkit/calculators\\\": major\\\\n\\\"@taxkit/api-http\\\": major\\\\n\\\"@taxkit/api-rpc\\\": major\\\\n\\\"@taxkit/sdk\\\": major\\\\n\\\"@taxkit/docs-content\\\": patch\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nAdd canonical checked rate-limit and admission-unavailable calculation errors.\\\\nThe native API shares 60 calculations per minute per checked connection address\\\\nacross HTTP, RPC and private Website calls, including each batch member. HTTP\\\\nuses 429 with Retry-After 60 or fixed 503 guidance; RPC revision 4 preserves the\\\\nsame errors. Metadata, direct engine/local SDK and standalone Bun work retain\\\\ntheir existing policy. Declare required native namespace configuration and\\\\nexplicit bounded local emulation. Update generated/public error contracts.\\\\nNo automatic calculation retry, provider apply, versioning or publication.\\\\n''')\\np=Path('docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md');s=p.read_text();s+='''\\\\n\\\\n## Metrics deferral — 6 October 2026\\\\n\\\\nCooper asked to leave metrics work for now because the approach is likely to\\\\nchange, and to proceed with the other work. CSF-T009/DEV-80 remains pending; its\\\\nmetrics/exporter/dataset/dashboard choices must be revisited before that task\\\\nstarts. This continuation does not implement or accept that prior metrics\\\\napproach. Existing disabled collection and fixed safe failure containment stay\\\\nin place while calculator/API and other authorised work proceed.\\\\n''';p.write_text(s)\\np=Path('docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md');s=p.read_text();s+='''\\\\n\\\\nCooper's 6 October steering defers metrics/telemetry approach work for now and\\\\nauthorises proceeding with the other tasks. Leave CSF-T009/DEV-80 pending and\\\\nrevisit its approach before implementation. Do not add exporters, datasets,\\\\ndashboards or metric collection in this rate slice; preserve disabled platform\\\\ncollection and fixed safe error containment. This is a task-specific deferral,\\\\nnot a pause or completion of the overall clean-slate continuation.\\\\n''';p.write_text(s)\\nPY\",\"max_output_tokens\":1000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 /private/tmp/dev75-request-run-checks.py '[[\\\"calc-build\\\",[\\\"bun\\\",\\\"run\\\",\\\"--filter=@taxkit/calculators\\\",\\\"build\\\"]],[\\\"http-openapi\\\",[\\\"bun\\\",\\\"run\\\",\\\"--filter=@taxkit/api-http\\\",\\\"update-openapi-snapshot\\\"]],[\\\"http-types\\\",[\\\"bun\\\",\\\"run\\\",\\\"--filter=@taxkit/api-http\\\",\\\"check-types\\\"]]]' dev75-rate-v34\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":700}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","create_time":1791267311.62669}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:16:07.704Z","ordinal":39667,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","session_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","root_turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","response_id":"resp_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac491ef6a6487d0801ba257cfd6fa18","usage":{"input_tokens":176979,"cached_input_tokens":173952,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2451,"reasoning_output_tokens":397,"total_tokens":179430},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":20408375,"cached_input_tokens":19815552,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":89147,"reasoning_output_tokens":27761,"total_tokens":20497522},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":764611548,"cached_input_tokens":748851840,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3594151,"reasoning_output_tokens":1510180,"total_tokens":768205699}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:16:07.766Z","ordinal":39668,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-91193071-4a4f-48bf-b70a-d5e5e8118b6a","process_id":"81192","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nowners={\n'packages/api/http/README.md':'''The [calculator-owned rate contract](../../calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) adds canonical rate/unavailable errors to calculation responses. The native API maps them to HTTP 429 with `Retry-After: 60` and fixed 503 guidance, using the existing error envelope. Metadata consumes no rate unit. Owning group Schemas drive generated clients and the OpenAPI snapshot; the standalone Bun host keeps its existing policy.\\n''',\n'packages/api/rpc/README.md':'''Revision `4` preserves canonical `CalculatorRateLimited` and `CalculatorAdmissionUnavailable` alongside existing expected errors. Older clients receive the checked revision mismatch. The native API and Website share the [calculator-owned rate contract](../../calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission); each batch calculation takes one unit and metadata takes none. `./rate-identity` is an explicit workspace-only host export; it is excluded from the published RPC capability surface. The rate identity is separate from RPC request JSON and is never an analytics identifier.\\n''',\n'apps/api/README.md':'''The native API builds `PublicCalculatorServiceRateLimited` once underneath its bounded service. HTTP/RPC and the binding-only `calculatorRequest` operation share the [calculator-owned rate contract](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission). Public requests need a checked original Cloudflare connection address; forwarded Worker calls and arbitrary forwarded headers cannot select a key. The Website private call supplies its checked key separately from JSON; no HTTP route admits that argument. The closed reply is buffered inside the native event scope, bounded to 2 MiB and ten seconds.\\n\\n`ApiCalculatorAdmissionLive` uses the installed native RateLimit Layer, decodes each provider reply and returns fixed unavailable guidance for provider failures or invalid replies. It requires `CALCULATOR_RATE_NAMESPACE` as a positive decimal string. The operator must select an account-wide unique stage value before a cloud plan/apply; no provider value is invented. The [infrastructure owner](../../packages/infrastructure/README.md#native-calculation-limiter-configuration) owns graph and local-root selection. Hosted mode defaults to `edge`. The guarded local root selects `local-emulator`; a shared local allowance additionally requires an HTTP loopback API origin.\\n\\nCloudflare's [rate limiter](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/bindings/rate-limit/) is approximate and local to a location, not an exact global quota. Real edge identity, namespace uniqueness and uploaded provider settings need separate authorised readback. Direct engine/local SDK and standalone Bun execution keep their existing contracts.\\n''',\n'apps/web/README.md':'''The API and Website use the [calculator-owned rate contract](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission). The Website checks its original Cloudflare connection address and supplies it separately from request JSON to the binding-only `calculatorRequest` operation. The installed Alchemy native RPC adapter owns private-call reply handling. Both browser and restored HTML forms display fixed rate/unavailable guidance and never retry automatically.\\n\\nThe private request omits an explicit AbortSignal because the pinned native RPC cannot serialise it. Client cancellation stops local waiting; API work and reply budgets remain in force. This does not prove remote cancellation. The guarded disposable root selects `local-emulator` and one loopback allowance; hosted composition defaults to `edge`. [Infrastructure configuration](../../packages/infrastructure/README.md#native-calculation-limiter-configuration) owns this distinction.\\n''',\n'docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md':'''The [calculator rate owner](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) defines canonical errors and a redacted IP key. The [native API](../../apps/api/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) composes admission once below bounded work, so HTTP/RPC/private Website calls share an allowance and each batch member takes one unit. Metadata remains independent. HTTP uses 429 with `Retry-After: 60` or fixed 503 guidance; RPC revision 4 preserves the same errors. The standalone Bun host and local engine/SDK keep their existing behaviour. Packed declarations must expose the expanded checked error union without adding private host identity capabilities to the published RPC exports.\\n''',\n'docs/architecture/effect-services.md':'''`CalculatorAdmission` is a closed named service; its [owning contract](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) and redacted key Schema live with calculators. The request Context reference carries checked identity separately from facts. `PublicCalculatorServiceRateLimited` provides calculation-only admission; the native API composes it once below bounded work. Its provider Layer, installed live Layer and mock test Layer remain separate. Native provider replies are decoded immediately and failures become fixed errors without provider causes or addresses.\\n''',\n'docs/architecture/frontend.md':'''The [Website owner](../../apps/web/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) captures checked original connection identity and uses the API's binding-only named operation for HTML forms. Browser calculations use public RPC. Both reach the same [calculator-owned allowance](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission), including separate batch members. Containers show fixed safe guidance with manual retry. This adds no calculation engine, stored figures, analytics identity or URL data to the Website. Private-call local cancellation and remote work limits remain distinct.\\n''',\n}\nfor name,body in owners.items():\n p=Path(name);s=p.read_text();a=s.rindex('\\n\\n## Native calculation rate admission');p.write_text(s[:a]+'\\n\\n## Native calculation rate admission\\n\\n'+body)\np=Path('packages/docs-content/content/api/errors.mdx');s=p.read_text().replace('rate limiting remains under implementation; these work limits do not establish\\nthat separate policy.','rate admission in the native API adds 60 calculations per minute per checked\\nconnection address across HTTP, RPC and Website forms. Every batch calculation\\ncounts separately; metadata reads do not count. A rejected calculation returns\\nHTTP 429 with `CalculatorRateLimited` and `Retry-After: 60`. Missing/invalid\\nconnection identity or a failed limiter returns HTTP 503 with\\n`CalculatorAdmissionUnavailable`. Both contain fixed safe guidance and manual\\nretry fields. These native limits are approximate and local to a Cloudflare\\nlocation, rather than an exact worldwide quota. The standalone Bun server\\nkeeps its existing work policy.');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('.changeset/native-calculation-rate-admission.md');p.write_text('''---\\n\"@taxkit/calculators\": major\\n\"@taxkit/api-http\": major\\n\"@taxkit/api-rpc\": major\\n\"@taxkit/sdk\": major\\n\"@taxkit/docs-content\": patch\\n---\\n\\nAdd canonical checked rate-limit and admission-unavailable calculation errors.\\nThe native API shares 60 calculations per minute per checked connection address\\nacross HTTP, RPC and private Website calls, including each batch member. HTTP\\nuses 429 with Retry-After 60 or fixed 503 guidance; RPC revision 4 preserves the\\nsame errors. Metadata, direct engine/local SDK and standalone Bun work retain\\ntheir existing policy. Declare required native namespace configuration and\\nexplicit bounded local emulation. Update generated/public error contracts.\\nNo automatic calculation retry, provider apply, versioning or publication.\\n''')\np=Path('docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md');s=p.read_text();s+='''\\n\\n## Metrics deferral — 6 October 2026\\n\\nCooper asked to leave metrics work for now because the approach is likely to\\nchange, and to proceed with the other work. CSF-T009/DEV-80 remains pending; its\\nmetrics/exporter/dataset/dashboard choices must be revisited before that task\\nstarts. This continuation does not implement or accept that prior metrics\\napproach. Existing disabled collection and fixed safe failure containment stay\\nin place while calculator/API and other authorised work proceed.\\n''';p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md');s=p.read_text();s+='''\\n\\nCooper's 6 October steering defers metrics/telemetry approach work for now and\\nauthorises proceeding with the other tasks. Leave CSF-T009/DEV-80 pending and\\nrevisit its approach before implementation. Do not add exporters, datasets,\\ndashboards or metric collection in this rate slice; preserve disabled platform\\ncollection and fixed safe error containment. This is a task-specific deferral,\\nnot a pause or completion of the overall clean-slate continuation.\\n''';p.write_text(s)\nPY"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nowners={\n'packages/api/http/README.md':'''The [calculator-owned rate contract](../../calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) adds canonical rate/unavailable errors to calculation responses. The native API maps them to HTTP 429 with `Retry-After: 60` and fixed 503 guidance, using the existing error envelope. Metadata consumes no rate unit. Owning group Schemas drive generated clients and the OpenAPI snapshot; the standalone Bun host keeps its existing policy.\\n''',\n'packages/api/rpc/README.md':'''Revision `4` preserves canonical `CalculatorRateLimited` and `CalculatorAdmissionUnavailable` alongside existing expected errors. Older clients receive the checked revision mismatch. The native API and Website share the [calculator-owned rate contract](../../calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission); each batch calculation takes one unit and metadata takes none. `./rate-identity` is an explicit workspace-only host export; it is excluded from the published RPC capability surface. The rate identity is separate from RPC request JSON and is never an analytics identifier.\\n''',\n'apps/api/README.md':'''The native API builds `PublicCalculatorServiceRateLimited` once underneath its bounded service. HTTP/RPC and the binding-only `calculatorRequest` operation share the [calculator-owned rate contract](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission). Public requests need a checked original Cloudflare connection address; forwarded Worker calls and arbitrary forwarded headers cannot select a key. The Website private call supplies its checked key separately from JSON; no HTTP route admits that argument. The closed reply is buffered inside the native event scope, bounded to 2 MiB and ten seconds.\\n\\n`ApiCalculatorAdmissionLive` uses the installed native RateLimit Layer, decodes each provider reply and returns fixed unavailable guidance for provider failures or invalid replies. It requires `CALCULATOR_RATE_NAMESPACE` as a positive decimal string. The operator must select an account-wide unique stage value before a cloud plan/apply; no provider value is invented. The [infrastructure owner](../../packages/infrastructure/README.md#native-calculation-limiter-configuration) owns graph and local-root selection. Hosted mode defaults to `edge`. The guarded local root selects `local-emulator`; a shared local allowance additionally requires an HTTP loopback API origin.\\n\\nCloudflare's [rate limiter](https: