{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T07:21:16.517Z","ordinal":40045,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2dd61ba1-da06-48fe-899d-21ca872d9cda","process_id":"41924","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '498,563p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json; sed -n '1,150p' .agents/skills/docs-maintainer/references/repository-profile.md; rg -n 'duration|outcomes|status|artifact|lastSuccessful' tmp/release-readiness/report.json | head"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '498,563p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json","name":"clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json","path":"docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,150p' .agents/skills/docs-maintainer/references/repository-profile.md","name":"repository-profile.md","path":".agents/skills/docs-maintainer/references/repository-profile.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'duration|outcomes|status|artifact|lastSuccessful' tmp/release-readiness/report.json","query":"duration|outcomes|status|artifact|lastSuccessful","path":"report.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"      \"id\": \"CSF-T005\",\n      \"title\": \"Replace public docs and all discovery representations\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-006\",\n        \"CSF-010\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T003\",\n        \"CSF-T004\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Review the retained authored pages and navigation for finished content and source fidelity, recording exact publication acceptance and excluding unfinished drafts from public search.\",\n        \"Implement one accepted content/page catalogue. Website owns HTML and browser-safe generated presentation exports; dynamic page/navigation/source/search/Markdown/image services belong to the backend and checked client contract. Generated static sitemap/robots/agent indexes/Markdown/OG assets need no extra API.\",\n        \"Generate useful deterministic 1200x630 page OG images from checked public page metadata with the selected current Takumi/font graph; never incorporate calculation values.\",\n        \"Retire apps/docs and replaced rendering/build paths once equivalent local journeys and retained source/artifact identities are proved; update current owners and preserve addressability of history/old useful URLs.\",\n        \"Replace hard-coded apps/docs browser/cache/quality paths in tools/quality-workflow/** and .github/workflows/quality.yml; update the docs browser command in packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and current owners in docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json.\",\n        \"Apply Q13: processed Markdown exposes only accepted public pages/reference content. Personal report downloads are outside this release; calculation answers remain temporary and visible on screen or through the agreed agent tools. Any public-content cache uses an owned readonly structured key with installed Equal/Hash semantics, not JSON; prove equivalent reconstructed keys, distinct address fields and last-reader cancellation cleanup where a shared cache is needed.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"packages/docs-content/** authored/status/navigation/generated owners and any justified retained docs-fumadocs bridge\",\n        \"apps/web HTML/docs presentation, generated static discovery/image assets and old-route redirect map\",\n        \"apps/api dynamic page/navigation/search/processed-Markdown/image services and packages/api/http checked contracts/clients; owning content package preserves prose, links, tables and examples\",\n        \"tools/documentation/owner-policy.json exact public acceptance records and generated edges\",\n        \"Public/app/package READMEs, docs/architecture/frontend.md, content-and-posts.md, package-ownership.md and applicable runbook/command pointers\",\n        \"tools/quality-workflow/**, .github/workflows/quality.yml, package.json/Turbo command wiring, packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run docs:validate\",\n        \"bun run check:docs\",\n        \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n        \"bun run build\",\n        \"bun run check-types\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Verify public docs/navigation, search, Markdown negotiation/explicit links, crawler-readable rendering, canonicals and share previews on actual local routes.\",\n        \"Check draft exclusion, no raw JSX/imports in processed Markdown, valid image output/size/cache, mobile/keyboard behaviour and old useful URL redirects.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n        \"The Website imports only browser-safe compiled presentation/contract exports; dynamic content machine routes and authored source/live Layers belong to the backend.\",\n        \"Quality/cache/release/profile owners admit the replacement app and no longer depend on a removed apps/docs path; new commands exist and are proved before obsolete commands are removed.\",\n        \"Finished pages are explicitly accepted, unfinished pages do not enter public discovery, and valid public content retains source attribution.\",\n        \"The replacement covers the retired app's useful journeys and historical evidence remains addressable.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T006\",\n# TaxKit documentation profile\n\nRead this profile after `AGENTS.md` and `docs/README.md`. Paths and commands\nbelow are repository-local; resolve the checkout with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`.\n\n## Owner map\n\n| Change class                                        | Earliest owner and required pointers                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Maintainer lifecycle, truth layers, archive routing | `docs/README.md`; architecture, standards, audit and active intent only when affected                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| Calculator rules, facts and schemas                 | owning `packages/calculators` or `packages/rules/**` source/README; relevant `docs/architecture/**`, SDK/API/public docs only when consumers change                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| SDK exports and examples                            | `packages/sdk/typescript` source/export map and README; packed-consumer/downstream proof; `docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| HTTP/OpenAPI                                        | `packages/api/http/src/**` schemas and `src/openapi.ts`; generated snapshot `packages/api/http/__snapshots__/openapi.json` through `test:openapi`; `packages/api/http/README.md`, `apps/api/README.md`, and API/SDK architecture only when their contracts change                                                               |\n| Public MDX/navigation/lifecycle                     | `packages/docs-content/content/**`, `packages/docs-content/navigation.json`, and `tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`; `published` requires one exact `public.statusDecision.acceptanceRecords` binding to a strict addressable record, with the durable lifecycle decision routed from `docs/documentation-audit/hgi-207/public-mdx-lifecycle.json` |\n| Public docs runtime/generated Fumadocs              | `apps/docs/README.md`, `packages/docs-content/source.config.ts`, `packages/docs-content/.source`, and `packages/docs-fumadocs`; regenerate/check through the owning commands and never hand-edit generated output                                                                                                               |\n| Package/app roots                                   | owning package/app README, package ownership architecture, root routes only when discoverability changes                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| Commands, CI, versioning and release readiness      | `package.json`, workflow/command owner, `docs/standards/versioning.md`, `docs/runbooks/README.md`, testing-quality architecture and proof owner                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| Runbooks, authority, proof and history              | exactly five target-owned procedures routed by `docs/runbooks/README.md`; `docs/operations/authority-model.md`; `tools/documentation/runbook-contract.json`; sanitized `docs/evidence/releases/**`, `docs/evidence/deployments/**`, or dated `docs/documentation-audit/**`; preserve provenance and non-claims                             |\n| PRD and implementation                              | target SPEC, sibling tasks and active plan; local `prd-writer`, `prd-review`, `prd-implementer` invoke this skill                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n\nPublic `published` needs an exact accepted record and one-to-one binding in\n`tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`; its `targetPath` must equal the public\npath. Navigation remains independently draft unless it receives its own exact\nrecord and binding.\nGenerated source is authoritative over checked output. Repository evidence is\nnot provider, registry, deployment, public-site or consumer proof.\n\n## Commands and boundaries\n\n- Baseline documentation/path/skill checks: `bun run test:skills`, `bun run\ncheck:docs`, `bun run check:runbooks`, `bun run check:repository-paths`.\n- Harness foundation checks: `bun run check:harness-governance:types`, `bun run\n  test:harness-governance`, and `bun run check:harness-governance`. The runtime\n  gate reads only repository-local profile, audit, receipt, skill, link, and\n  critical-journey owners.\n- Full local closeout: `bun run verification` and `git diff --check`.\n- Public content/runtime: `bun run docs:validate`, `bun run docs:build`,\n  `bun run --filter=docs test:browser` when applicable.\n- SDK package boundary: `bun run --filter=@taxkit/sdk check-packed-artifact`\n  and `bun run --filter=@taxkit/sdk validate:downstream` when applicable.\n- Release evidence: `bun run release:check` is local proof only; versioning,\n  publication and deployment remain separately authorized operations.\n- Runbook contract: `bun run check:runbooks` is inspect-only and writes the\n  bounded ignored `tmp/runbook-validation-report.json`; it never runs a\n  documented procedure or establishes external state.\n\nFor each check, state its observable postcondition and what it does not prove.\nKeep background freshness reports as candidates until an attached implementation\nauthority, responsible reviewer and separately named publisher accept them.\n\n## Clean-slate compatibility and implementation\n\nThe local root manifest and lockfile select stable Effect 4.0.0 and TypeScript\n7.0.2. Canonical skill templates may retain their upstream rc.117 qualification;\nthat reference snapshot does not downgrade TaxKit or prove an app/provider\nmigration. Check installed exports and the active clean-slate plan before use.\n\nThe complete local skill collection is pinned by\n`tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json` to Commonplace development-workflows\n0.6.1. It includes `linear`, `strict-effect-ts` and `alchemy-iac`, with relative\nClaude links. Use the Linear skill for tracked task status/evidence. The active\n`docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md` distinguishes skill adoption, strict enforcement and Atom integration from\nlater application work. Use its task receipts for current acceptance; the\nupstream skill receipt alone does not prove runtime behaviour.\nrg: tmp/release-readiness/report.json: IO error for operation on tmp/re