{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T07:24:44.781Z","ordinal":40175,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac4a23b657887d0abb37134a8488d22","status":"completed","call_id":"call_i7HR8L0wDEu94oNmAEDTgAQ9","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '355,460p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md; cat packages/docs-content/package.json; sed -n '1,190p' packages/docs-content/src/schemas.ts; cat packages/docs-content/navigation.json | head -90; rg --files apps/web/src/routes | head -25\",\"max_output_tokens\":5000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","create_time":1791271475.041664}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T07:24:44.858Z","ordinal":40176,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1ed10132-7725-479e-b320-1df917b25325","process_id":"89252","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '355,460p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md; cat packages/docs-content/package.json; sed -n '1,190p' packages/docs-content/src/schemas.ts; cat packages/docs-content/navigation.json | head -90; rg --files apps/web/src/routes | head -25"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '355,460p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md","name":"clean-slate-foundation.md","path":"docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat packages/docs-content/package.json","name":"package.json","path":"packages/docs-content/package.json"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,190p' packages/docs-content/src/schemas.ts","name":"schemas.ts","path":"packages/docs-content/src/schemas.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat packages/docs-content/navigation.json","name":"navigation.json","path":"packages/docs-content/navigation.json"},{"type":"list_files","cmd":"rg --files apps/web/src/routes","path":"routes"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"  bounded arrays or persistent Effect collections. Do not expose a mutable\n  array, native Map/Set/WeakMap/WeakSet, Date, SDK object or mutable reference as\n  a domain value.\n  Do not use casts or shallow freezing as a substitute for this contract.\n- Express transformations with pure Effect collection mapping/folding;\n  express workflows with named Effects and combinators. No `for`, `for...in`,\n  `for...of`, `while`, `do...while` or native array traversal, including native\n  `forEach`, in owned code. Pure array work uses Effect Array functions directly;\n  use scoped, bounded Effect traversal/repetition where work really repeats.\n- Prefer a pipe for a clear linear data flow. Use flat `Effect.gen` with\n  immutable bindings when dependencies or several sequential steps make that\n  clearer. Neither syntax permits raw work, mutation, hidden branching or\n  helper chains that obscure the operation.\n- Expected failures stay in tagged error channels and are handled exhaustively\n  with Effect/Match and Option/Result's matching APIs. No `switch`, manual\n  `_tag` comparisons, thrown expected errors, `try`/`catch`, manual Promise\n  control flow, manual unknown probing or nullable domain state.\n- Pure deterministic calculations and rendering remain total plain functions.\n  Do not wrap constants or safe leaf transformations in ceremonial Effects,\n  or construct a service/Layer for every helper.\n\nNecessary changing state belongs to the narrowest explicit owner: React for\nlocal synchronous input/display state; Effect Atom for browser work; or scoped\nRef/Queue/Cache/Semaphore/transaction facilities inside a named Layer where\ntheir semantics are needed. Values held in those owners remain immutable;\nupdates are pure and atomic, and no underlying mutable reference escapes.\nThere is no claim that React, Effect, the host or a vendor SDK has no internal\nstate. Prove route/request/instance lifetime, concurrent updates, interruption\nand disposal rather than hiding state in module globals. Calculation facts and\nreports get no persistence or cache; accepted public content may have an\nexplicit bounded cache policy.\n\nThe current skill permits measured private native data structures and genuine\nhost requirements, and no longer treats a total leaf as permission for local\nmutation. TaxKit's stronger requirement admits only a host-imposed primitive\nin a named outer adapter with an exact construct, containment, owner, test and\nremoval condition. Grant only the\nconstruct that the host needs; a Promise-returning adapter exception does not\npermit nearby mutation, loops, SDK leakage or a nested runtime. Generated,\nvendor and reference templates have explicit provenance and exclusions; runnable owned policy code\nand tests remain covered. A performance preference alone cannot silently relax\nCooper's immutable/declarative requirement.\n\nExtract an operation only when it owns stable policy, external work or a\nresource lifetime, or has a real independent reuse/substitution point. Each\nextraction needs its semantic owner and simpler call graph. Keep one-use\ndecoding, mapping, error projection and matching inline. Ban dumping-ground\n`helpers`, `utils`, `common` and `shared` modules; naming a wrapper as a service\ndoes not give it semantic weight. Review the actual call graph in every slice.\n\nAdopt the current 0.6.1 portable strict Effect policy at its repository-owned\ncanonical skill asset. Merge into `oxlint.config.ts` and retain useful existing TaxKit,\nMDX and workspace checks. Enable `strict-effect/no-unchecked-index`,\n`no-native-at`, `runtime-file-convention`, `tagged-error-name`,\n`error-constructor-new`, `no-promise-workflow`, `no-unsafe-option-unwrap`,\n`no-unchecked-json`, `no-runtime-outside-boundary`, `no-native-work` and\n`no-imperative-collections` under that plugin. Keep assertions/any, raw fetch/JSON/environment, ambient\ntime/random/timers, console telemetry and native mutable collections restricted\nacross owned source, tests, tools, infrastructure and configuration. Exact host\nadapters get only their necessary exception; generated/vendor exclusions are\nexplicit. Pure local rendering and deterministic computations remain direct.\nCover owned `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`, `.mjs` and `.cjs` execution paths, not\nonly the scaffold's TypeScript override. Convert retained JavaScript policy\ntools to checked TypeScript where needed; do not leave them outside enforcement\nbecause their extension differs. Validate executable MDX expressions/imports\nthrough the existing content-policy owner; fenced documentation examples are\nrepresentation content, not hidden executable source.\n\nThe earlier 0.5.1 plugin lacked local mutation and loop checks. Its installed\n0.6.0 successor now supplies `no-imperative-collections`: use that canonical\nrule instead of creating duplicate mutable-binding/reassignment/loop rules.\nIt rejects loops, `let`/`var`, assignments, updates, deletion, native array\ntraversal/mutators/constructors, transient Effect collection modes, `switch`\nand manual `_tag` decisions. Imported Effect functional collection operations\nand native Alchemy Output transformations remain valid. Ordinary pure work\nneeds no Effect wrapper merely to use those functional operations.\n\nThe rule is syntax/import-based. Add a TaxKit correction only for an evidenced\ngap, with the owner and actual tool capability established first. Retain and\nqualify native Map/Set/WeakMap/WeakSet, mutable built-in/class/contract values,\nObject/Reflect writes, local/destructured aliases and runtime reference checks\nthrough the relevant existing rules, readonly types and focused additions.\nComputed member access is already rejected by `no-unchecked-index`; do not\npresent it as an admitted combined-baseline escape.\n`Ref.set` and native mutable `Map.set` are different operations; a method-name\nsearch alone does not establish their identity. Each correction must reject\nits bad fixture without rejecting a valid persistent collection, Effect-managed\nstate update or qualified Alchemy Output operation.\n\nActual-command fixtures must cover every owned path group, including moved\napps, nested packages, JavaScript policy tools, tests and configuration. Assert\nthe admitted file count, exit code and expected rule. Exact `allowedAssignments`\nand `allowedMethods` options name a file and the single target/receiver/method;\nno parent path, glob or whole-file exception. Prove nearby mutations remain\nrejected and that removing/disabling a required rule or broadening an exception\nfails the verifier. Readonly types and the selected Effect diagnostics cover\nthe type side; structural review covers helper purpose, Schema ownership and\ncall-graph simplicity. Do not present lint as proof of all semantic requirements.\n\nPreserve and qualify the stronger existing TaxKit lexical checks when merging\nthe portable plugin. Runtime operations used as references/callbacks, such as\npassing `Effect.runPromise` to a pipe, must be rejected outside the exact host\nowner as well as direct calls. Prove renamed imports, namespace aliases,\nre-exports, shadowed names and callback references; a CallExpression-only check\nis insufficient. Primitive host adapters cannot become a generic `run`\nescape for arbitrary callers.\n{\n  \"name\": \"@taxkit/docs-content\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.3\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \"./errors\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/errors.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/errors.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/errors.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./live\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./generated-source\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/generated-source.layer.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/generated-source.layer.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/generated-source.layer.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./server\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/server.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/server.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/server.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./client\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/client.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/client.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/client.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./schemas\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/schemas.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/schemas.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/schemas.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./service\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/service.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/service.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/service.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./test\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./validate\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/validate.runtime.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/validate.runtime.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/validate.runtime.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./source.config\": \"./source.config.ts\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"bun run generate\",\n    \"check-examples\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.examples.json --noEmit\",\n    \"check-types\": \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/docs-fumadocs build && tsc --noEmit && bun run check-examples\",\n    \"generate\": \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/docs-fumadocs build && fumadocs-mdx\",\n    \"test\": \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/docs-fumadocs build && vitest run --passWithNoTests\",\n    \"validate\": \"bun run ./src/validate.runtime.ts\",\n    \"clean\": \"rm -rf .source .turbo *.tsbuildinfo\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@effect/platform-bun\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@effect/platform-node\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@taxkit/docs-fumadocs\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"effect\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"fumadocs-core\": \"16.16.0\",\n    \"fumadocs-mdx\": \"15.4.6\",\n    \"yaml\": \"2.9.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@effect/vitest\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@taxkit/api-http\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/calculators\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/core\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/rules-au-pay\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/sdk\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@types/bun\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"typescript\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vite\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vitest\": \"catalog:\"\n  }\n}\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\";\n\nexport const DocsNonEmptyText = Schema.Trimmed.check(Schema.isMinLength(1));\nexport type DocsNonEmptyText = typeof DocsNonEmptyText.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPagePath = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\n  Schema.brand(\"taxkit/DocsPagePath\")\n);\nexport type DocsPagePath = typeof DocsPagePath.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPageSlug = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\n  Schema.brand(\"taxkit/DocsPageSlug\")\n);\nexport type DocsPageSlug = typeof DocsPageSlug.Type;\n\nexport const DocsSourcePath = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\n  Schema.brand(\"taxkit/DocsSourcePath\")\n);\nexport type DocsSourcePath = typeof DocsSourcePath.Type;\n\nexport const DocsContentStatus = Schema.Literals([\"draft\", \"published\"]);\nexport type DocsContentStatus = typeof DocsContentStatus.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPageFrontmatter = Schema.Struct({\n  description: DocsNonEmptyText,\n  status: DocsContentStatus,\n  title: DocsNonEmptyText,\n});\nexport type DocsPageFrontmatter = typeof DocsPageFrontmatter.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPageType = Schema.Literals([\n  \"api reference overview\",\n  \"changelog or release note\",\n  \"concept\",\n  \"contribution guide\",\n  \"decision page\",\n  \"guide\",\n  \"quickstart\",\n  \"reference\",\n  \"section index\",\n  \"troubleshooting\",\n]);\nexport type DocsPageType = typeof DocsPageType.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPrimaryReader = Schema.Literals([\n  \"API consumer\",\n  \"Application integrator\",\n  \"Correctness reviewer\",\n  \"Documentation contributor\",\n  \"New contributor\",\n  \"SDK evaluator\",\n  \"Type-safety focused developer\",\n]);\nexport type DocsPrimaryReader = typeof DocsPrimaryReader.Type;\n\nexport const DocsNavigationLeaf = Schema.Struct({\n  pageType: DocsPageType,\n  path: DocsPagePath,\n  primaryReader: DocsPrimaryReader,\n  source: DocsSourcePath,\n  title: DocsNonEmptyText,\n});\nexport type DocsNavigationLeaf = typeof DocsNavigationLeaf.Type;\n\nexport const DocsNavigationItem = Schema.Struct({\n  ...DocsNavigationLeaf.fields,\n  pages: Schema.optional(Schema.Array(DocsNavigationLeaf)),\n});\nexport type DocsNavigationItem = typeof DocsNavigationItem.Type;\n\nexport const DocsNavigation = Schema.Struct({\n  $schema: Schema.optional(Schema.String),\n  contentRoot: Schema.Literal(\"packages/docs-content/content\"),\n  primaryNavigation: Schema.Array(DocsNavigationItem),\n  status: DocsContentStatus,\n});\nexport type DocsNavigation = typeof DocsNavigation.Type;\n\nexport const DocsMeta = Schema.Struct({\n  collapsible: Schema.optional(Schema.Boolean),\n  defaultOpen: Schema.optional(Schema.Boolean),\n  description: Schema.optional(DocsNonEmptyText),\n  icon: Schema.optional(Schema.String),\n  pages: Schema.optional(Schema.mutable(Schema.Array(Schema.String))),\n  root: Schema.optional(Schema.Boolean),\n  title: Schema.optional(DocsNonEmptyText),\n});\nexport type DocsMeta = typeof DocsMeta.Type;\n\nexport const DocsMdxComponentName = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\n  Schema.check(\n    Schema.isPattern(/^[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*(?:\\.[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*)*$/u)\n  ),\n  Schema.brand(\"taxkit/DocsMdxComponentName\")\n);\nexport type DocsMdxComponentName = typeof DocsMdxComponentName.Type;\n\nexport const DocsContentPage = Schema.Struct({\n  frontmatter: DocsPageFrontmatter,\n  markdown: Schema.String,\n  path: DocsPagePath,\n  slugs: Schema.Array(DocsPageSlug),\n  source: DocsSourcePath,\n});\nexport type DocsContentPage = typeof DocsContentPage.Type;\n\nexport class DocsValidationIssue extends Schema.TaggedClass<DocsValidationIssue>()(\n  \"DocsValidationIssue\",\n  {\n    message: DocsNonEmptyText,\n    path: Schema.Array(Schema.String),\n  }\n) {}\n\nexport const DocsValidationResult = Schema.Struct({\n  issues: Schema.Array(DocsValidationIssue),\n});\nexport type DocsValidationResult = typeof DocsValidationResult.Type;\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"./navigation.schema.json\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"contentRoot\": \"packages/docs-content/content\",\n  \"primaryNavigation\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Start\",\n      \"path\": \"/start\",\n      \"source\": \"content/start/index.mdx\",\n      \"pageType\": \"section index\",\n      \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\",\n      \"pages\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Overview\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/overview\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/overview.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"section index\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Quickstart\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/quickstart\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/quickstart.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"quickstart\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Install the SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/install-the-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/install-the-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Run your first calculation\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/run-your-first-calculation\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/run-your-first-calculation.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Choose SDK or HTTP API\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/choose-sdk-or-api\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/choose-sdk-or-api.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"decision page\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Application integrator\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"SDK\",\n      \"path\": \"/sdk\",\n      \"source\": \"content/sdk/index.mdx\",\n      \"pageType\": \"section index\",\n      \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\",\n      \"pages\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"TypeScript SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/typescript-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/typescript-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"concept\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Plain SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/plain-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/plain-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Application integrator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Safe SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/safe-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/safe-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Application integrator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Effect SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/effect-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/effect-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Application integrator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Schemas\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/schemas\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/schemas.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"reference\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Type-safety focused developer\"\napps/web/src/routes/agents.tsx\napps/web/src/routes/calculators.$calculatorId.tsx\napps/web/src/routes/__root.tsx\napps/web/src/routes/index.tsx\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"  bounded arrays or persistent Effect collections. Do not expose a mutable\n  array, native Map/Set/WeakMap/WeakSet, Date, SDK object or mutable reference as\n  a domain value.\n  Do not use casts or shallow freezing as a substitute for this contract.\n- Express transformations with pure Effect collection mapping/folding;\n  express workflows with named Effects and combinators. No `for`, `for...in`,\n  `for...of`, `while`, `do...while` or native array traversal, including native\n  `forEach`, in owned code. Pure array work uses Effect Array functions directly;\n  use scoped, bounded Effect traversal/repetition where work really repeats.\n- Prefer a pipe for a clear linear data flow. Use flat `Effect.gen` with\n  immutable bindings when dependencies or several sequential steps make that\n  clearer. Neither syntax permits raw work, mutation, hidden branching or\n  helper chains that obscure the operation.\n- Expected failures stay in tagged error channels and are handled exhaustively\n  with Effect/Match and Option/Result's matching APIs. No `switch`, manual\n  `_tag` comparisons, thrown expected errors, `try`/`catch`, manual Promise\n  control flow, manual unknown probing or nullable domain state.\n- Pure deterministic calculations and rendering remain total plain functions.\n  Do not wrap constants or safe leaf transformations in ceremonial Effects,\n  or construct a service/Layer for every helper.\n\nNecessary changing state belongs to the narrowest explicit owner: React for\nlocal synchronous input/display state; Effect Atom for browser work; or scoped\nRef/Queue/Cache/Semaphore/transaction facilities inside a named Layer where\ntheir semantics are needed. Values held in those owners remain immutable;\nupdates are pure and atomic, and no underlying mutable reference escapes.\nThere is no claim that React, Effect, the host or a vendor SDK has no internal\nstate. Prove route/request/instance lifetime, concurrent updates, interruption\nand disposal rather than hiding state in module globals. Calculation facts and\nreports get no persistence or cache; accepted public content may have an\nexplicit bounded cache policy.\n\nThe current skill permits measured private native data structures and genuine\nhost requirements, and no longer treats a total leaf as permission for local\nmutation. TaxKit's stronger requirement admits only a host-imposed primitive\nin a named outer adapter with an exact construct, containment, owner, test and\nremoval condition. Grant only the\nconstruct that the host needs; a Promise-returning adapter exception does not\npermit nearby mutation, loops, SDK leakage or a nested runtime. Generated,\nvendor and reference templates have explicit provenance and exclusions; runnable owned policy code\nand tests remain covered. A performance preference alone cannot silently relax\nCooper's immutable/declarative requirement.\n\nExtract an operation only when it owns stable policy, external work or a\nresource lifetime, or has a real independent reuse/substitution point. Each\nextraction needs its semantic owner and simpler call graph. Keep one-use\ndecoding, mapping, error projection and matching inline. Ban dumping-ground\n`helpers`, `utils`, `common` and `shared` modules; naming a wrapper as a service\ndoes not give it semantic weight. Review the actual call graph in every slice.\n\nAdopt the current 0.6.1 portable strict Effect policy at its repository-owned\ncanonical skill asset. Merge into `oxlint.config.ts` and retain useful existing TaxKit,\nMDX and workspace checks. Enable `strict-effect/no-unchecked-index`,\n`no-native-at`, `runtime-file-convention`, `tagged-error-name`,\n`error-constructor-new`, `no-promise-workflow`, `no-unsafe-option-unwrap`,\n`no-unchecked-json`, `no-runtime-outside-boundary`, `no-native-work` and\n`no-imperative-collections` under that plugin. Keep assertions/any, raw fetch/JSON/environment, ambient\ntime/random/timers, console telemetry and native mutable collections restricted\nacross owned source, tests, tools, infrastructure and configuration. Exact host\nadapters get only their necessary exception; generated/vendor exclusions are\nexplicit. Pure local rendering and deterministic computations remain direct.\nCover owned `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`, `.mjs` and `.cjs` execution paths, not\nonly the scaffold's TypeScript override. Convert retained JavaScript policy\ntools to checked TypeScript where needed; do not leave them outside enforcement\nbecause their extension differs. Validate executable MDX expressions/imports\nthrough the existing content-policy owner; fenced documentation examples are\nrepresentation content, not hidden executable source.\n\nThe earlier 0.5.1 plugin lacked local mutation and loop checks. Its installed\n0.6.0 successor now supplies `no-imperative-collections`: use that canonical\nrule instead of creating duplicate mutable-binding/reassignment/loop rules.\nIt rejects loops, `let`/`var`, assignments, updates, deletion, native array\ntraversal/mutators/constructors, transient Effect collection modes, `switch`\nand manual `_tag` decisions. Imported Effect functional collection operations\nand native Alchemy Output transformations remain valid. Ordinary pure work\nneeds no Effect wrapper merely to use those functional operations.\n\nThe rule is syntax/import-based. Add a TaxKit correction only for an evidenced\ngap, with the owner and actual tool capability established first. Retain and\nqualify native Map/Set/WeakMap/WeakSet, mutable built-in/class/contract values,\nObject/Reflect writes, local/destructured aliases and runtime reference checks\nthrough the relevant existing rules, readonly types and focused additions.\nComputed member access is already rejected by `no-unchecked-index`; do not\npresent it as an admitted combined-baseline escape.\n`Ref.set` and native mutable `Map.set` are different operations; a method-name\nsearch alone does not establish their identity. Each correction must reject\nits bad fixture without rejecting a valid persistent collection, Effect-managed\nstate update or qualified Alchemy Output operation.\n\nActual-command fixtures must cover every owned path group, including moved\napps, nested packages, JavaScript policy tools, tests and configuration. Assert\nthe admitted file count, exit code and expected rule. Exact `allowedAssignments`\nand `allowedMethods` options name a file and the single target/receiver/method;\nno parent path, glob or whole-file exception. Prove nearby mutations remain\nrejected and that removing/disabling a required rule or broadening an exception\nfails the verifier. Readonly types and the selected Effect diagnostics cover\nthe type side; structural review covers helper purpose, Schema ownership and\ncall-graph simplicity. Do not present lint as proof of all semantic requirements.\n\nPreserve and qualify the stronger existing TaxKit lexical checks when merging\nthe portable plugin. Runtime operations used as references/callbacks, such as\npassing `Effect.runPromise` to a pipe, must be rejected outside the exact host\nowner as well as direct calls. Prove renamed imports, namespace aliases,\nre-exports, shadowed names and callback references; a CallExpression-only check\nis insufficient. Primitive host adapters cannot become a generic `run`\nescape for arbitrary callers.\n{\n  \"name\": \"@taxkit/docs-content\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.3\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \"./errors\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/errors.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/errors.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/errors.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./live\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./generated-source\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/generated-source.layer.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/generated-source.layer.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/generated-source.layer.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./server\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/server.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/server.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/server.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./client\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/client.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/client.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/client.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./schemas\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/schemas.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/schemas.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/schemas.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./service\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/service.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/service.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/service.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./test\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./validate\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/validate.runtime.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/validate.runtime.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/validate.runtime.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./source.config\": \"./source.config.ts\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"bun run generate\",\n    \"check-examples\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.examples.json --noEmit\",\n    \"check-types\": \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/docs-fumadocs build && tsc --noEmit && bun run check-examples\",\n    \"generate\": \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/docs-fumadocs build && fumadocs-mdx\",\n    \"test\": \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/docs-fumadocs build && vitest run --passWithNoTests\",\n    \"validate\": \"bun run ./src/validate.runtime.ts\",\n    \"clean\": \"rm -rf .source .turbo *.tsbuildinfo\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@effect/platform-bun\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@effect/platform-node\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@taxkit/docs-fumadocs\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"effect\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"fumadocs-core\": \"16.16.0\",\n    \"fumadocs-mdx\": \"15.4.6\",\n    \"yaml\": \"2.9.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@effect/vitest\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@taxkit/api-http\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/calculators\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/core\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/rules-au-pay\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/sdk\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@types/bun\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"typescript\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vite\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vitest\": \"catalog:\"\n  }\n}\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\";\n\nexport const DocsNonEmptyText = Schema.Trimmed.check(Schema.isMinLength(1));\nexport type DocsNonEmptyText = typeof DocsNonEmptyText.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPagePath = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\n  Schema.brand(\"taxkit/DocsPagePath\")\n);\nexport type DocsPagePath = typeof DocsPagePath.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPageSlug = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\n  Schema.brand(\"taxkit/DocsPageSlug\")\n);\nexport type DocsPageSlug = typeof DocsPageSlug.Type;\n\nexport const DocsSourcePath = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\n  Schema.brand(\"taxkit/DocsSourcePath\")\n);\nexport type DocsSourcePath = typeof DocsSourcePath.Type;\n\nexport const DocsContentStatus = Schema.Literals([\"draft\", \"published\"]);\nexport type DocsContentStatus = typeof DocsContentStatus.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPageFrontmatter = Schema.Struct({\n  description: DocsNonEmptyText,\n  status: DocsContentStatus,\n  title: DocsNonEmptyText,\n});\nexport type DocsPageFrontmatter = typeof DocsPageFrontmatter.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPageType = Schema.Literals([\n  \"api reference overview\",\n  \"changelog or release note\",\n  \"concept\",\n  \"contribution guide\",\n  \"decision page\",\n  \"guide\",\n  \"quickstart\",\n  \"reference\",\n  \"section index\",\n  \"troubleshooting\",\n]);\nexport type DocsPageType = typeof DocsPageType.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPrimaryReader = Schema.Literals([\n  \"API consumer\",\n  \"Application integrator\",\n  \"Correctness reviewer\",\n  \"Documentation contributor\",\n  \"New contributor\",\n  \"SDK evaluator\",\n  \"Type-safety focused developer\",\n]);\nexport type DocsPrimaryReader = typeof DocsPrimaryReader.Type;\n\nexport const DocsNavigationLeaf = Schema.Struct({\n  pageType: DocsPageType,\n  path: DocsPagePath,\n  primaryReader: DocsPrimaryReader,\n  source: DocsSourcePath,\n  title: DocsNonEmptyText,\n});\nexport type DocsNavigationLeaf = typeof DocsNavigationLeaf.Type;\n\nexport const DocsNavigationItem = Schema.Struct({\n  ...DocsNavigationLeaf.fields,\n  pages: Schema.optional(Schema.Array(DocsNavigationLeaf)),\n});\nexport type DocsNavigationItem = typeof DocsNavigationItem.Type;\n\nexport const DocsNavigation = Schema.Struct({\n  $schema: Schema.optional(Schema.String),\n  contentRoot: Schema.Literal(\"packages/docs-content/content\"),\n  primaryNavigation: Schema.Array(DocsNavigationItem),\n  status: DocsContentStatus,\n});\nexport type DocsNavigation = typeof DocsNavigation.Type;\n\nexport const DocsMeta = Schema.Struct({\n  collapsible: Schema.optional(Schema.Boolean),\n  defaultOpen: Schema.optional(Schema.Boolean),\n  description: Schema.optional(DocsNonEmptyText),\n  icon: Schema.optional(Schema.String),\n  pages: Schema.optional(Schema.mutable(Schema.Array(Schema.String))),\n  root: Schema.optional(Schema.Boolean),\n  title: Schema.optional(DocsNonEmptyText),\n});\nexport type DocsMeta = typeof DocsMeta.Type;\n\nexport const DocsMdxComponentName = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\n  Schema.check(\n    Schema.isPattern(/^[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*(?:\\.[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*)*$/u)\n  ),\n  Schema.brand(\"taxkit/DocsMdxComponentName\")\n);\nexport type DocsMdxComponentName = typeof DocsMdxComponentName.Type;\n\nexport const DocsContentPage = Schema.Struct({\n  frontmatter: DocsPageFrontmatter,\n  markdown: Schema.String,\n  path: DocsPagePath,\n  slugs: Schema.Array(DocsPageSlug),\n  source: DocsSourcePath,\n});\nexport type DocsContentPage = typeof DocsContentPage.Type;\n\nexport class DocsValidationIssue extends Schema.TaggedClass<DocsValidationIssue>()(\n  \"DocsValidationIssue\",\n  {\n    message: DocsNonEmptyText,\n    path: Schema.Array(Schema.String),\n  }\n) {}\n\nexport const DocsValidationResult = Schema.Struct({\n  issues: Schema.Array(DocsValidationIssue),\n});\nexport type DocsValidationResult = typeof DocsValidationResult.Type;\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"./navigation.schema.json\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"contentRoot\": \"packages/docs-content/content\",\n  \"primaryNavigation\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Start\",\n      \"path\": \"/start\",\n      \"source\": \"content/start/index.mdx\",\n      \"pageType\": \"section index\",\n      \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\",\n      \"pages\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Overview\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/overview\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/overview.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"section index\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Quickstart\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/quickstart\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/quickstart.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"quickstart\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Install the SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/install-the-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/install-the-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Run your first calculation\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/run-your-first-calculation\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/run-your-first-calculation.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Choose SDK or HTTP API\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/choose-sdk-or-api\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/choose-sdk-or-api.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"decision page\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Application integrator\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"SDK\",\n      \"path\": \"/sdk\",\n      \"source\": \"content/sdk/index.mdx\",\n      \"pageType\": \"section index\",\n      \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\",\n      \"pages\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"TypeScript SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/typescript-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/typescript-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"concept\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Plain SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/plain-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/plain-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Application integrator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Safe SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/safe-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/safe-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Application integrator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Effect SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/effect-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/effect-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Application integrator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Schemas\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/schemas\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/schemas.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"reference\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Type-safety focused developer\"\napps/web/src/routes/agents.tsx\napps/web/src/routes/calculators.$calculatorId.tsx\napps/web/src/routes/__root.tsx\napps/web/src/routes/index.tsx\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6584},"formatted_output":"  bounded arrays or persistent Effect collections. Do not expose a mutable\n  array, native Map/Set/WeakMap/WeakSet, Date, SDK object or mutable reference as\n  a domain value.\n  Do not use casts or shallow freezing as a substitute for this contract.\n- Express transformations with pure Effect collection mapping/folding;\n  express workflows with named Effects and combinators. No `for`, `for...in`,\n  `for...of`, `while`, `do...while` or native array traversal, including native\n  `forEach`, in owned code. Pure array work uses Effect Array functions directly;\n  use scoped, bounded Effect traversal/repetition where work really repeats.\n- Prefer a pipe for a clear linear data flow. Use flat `Effect.gen` with\n  immutable bindings when dependencies or several sequential steps make that\n  clearer. Neither syntax permits raw work, mutation, hidden branching or\n  helper chains that obscure the operation.\n- Expected failures stay in tagged error channels and are handled exhaustively\n  with Effect/Match and Option/Result's matching APIs. No `switch`, manual\n  `_tag` comparisons, thrown expected errors, `try`/`catch`, manual Promise\n  control flow, manual unknown probing or nullable domain state.\n- Pure deterministic calculations and rendering remain total plain functions.\n  Do not wrap constants or safe leaf transformations in ceremonial Effects,\n  or construct a service/Layer for every helper.\n\nNecessary changing state belongs to the narrowest explicit owner: React for\nlocal synchronous input/display state; Effect Atom for browser work; or scoped\nRef/Queue/Cache/Semaphore/transaction facilities inside a named Layer where\ntheir semantics are needed. Values held in those owners remain immutable;\nupdates are pure and atomic, and no underlying mutable reference escapes.\nThere is no claim that React, Effect, the host or a vendor SDK has no internal\nstate. Prove route/request/instance lifetime, concurrent updates, interruption\nand disposal rather than hiding state in module globals. Calculation facts and\nreports get no persistence or cache; accepted public content may have an\nexplicit bounded cache policy.\n\nThe current skill permits measured private native data structures and genuine\nhost requirements, and no longer treats a total leaf as permission for local\nmutation. TaxKit's stronger requirement admits only a host-imposed primitive\nin a named outer adapter with an exact construct, containment, owner, test and\nremoval condition. Grant only the\nconstruct that the host needs; a Promise-returning adapter exception does not\npermit nearby mutation, loops, SDK leakage or a nested runtime. Generated,\nvendor and reference templates have explicit provenance and exclusions; runnable owned policy code\nand tests remain covered. A performance preference alone cannot silently relax\nCooper's immutable/declarative requirement.\n\nExtract an operation only when it owns stable policy, external work or a\nresource lifetime, or has a real independent reuse/substitution point. Each\nextraction needs its semantic owner and simpler call graph. Keep one-use\ndecoding, mapping, error projection and matching inline. Ban dumping-ground\n`helpers`, `utils`, `common` and `shared` modules; naming a wrapper as a service\ndoes not give it semantic weight. Review the actual call graph in every slice.\n\nAdopt the current 0.6.1 portable strict Effect policy at its repository-owned\ncanonical skill asset. Merge into `oxlint.config.ts` and retain useful existing TaxKit,\nMDX and workspace checks. Enable `strict-effect/no-unchecked-index`,\n`no-native-at`, `runtime-file-convention`, `tagged-error-name`,\n`error-constructor-new`, `no-promise-workflow`, `no-unsafe-option-unwrap`,\n`no-unchecked-json`, `no-runtime-outside-boundary`, `no-native-work` and\n`no-imperative-collections` under that plugin. Keep assertions/any, raw fetch/JSON/environment, ambient\ntime/random/timers, console telemetry and native mutable collections restricted\nacross owned source, tests, tools, infrastructure and configuration. Exact host\nadapters get only their necessary exception; generated/vendor exclusions are\nexplicit. Pure local rendering and deterministic computations remain direct.\nCover owned `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`, `.mjs` and `.cjs` execution paths, not\nonly the scaffold's TypeScript override. Convert retained JavaScript policy\ntools to checked TypeScript where needed; do not leave them outside enforcement\nbecause their extension differs. Validate executable MDX expressions/imports\nthrough the existing content-policy owner; fenced documentation examples are\nrepresentation content, not hidden executable source.\n\nThe earlier 0.5.1 plugin lacked local mutation and loop checks. Its installed\n0.6.0 successor now supplies `no-imperative-collections`: use that canonical\nrule instead of creating duplicate mutable-binding/reassignment/loop rules.\nIt rejects loops, `let`/`var`, assignments, updates, deletion, native array\ntraversal/mutators/constructors, transient Effect collection modes, `switch`\nand manual `_tag` decisions. Imported Effect functional collection operations\nand native Alchemy Output transformations remain valid. Ordinary pure work\nneeds no Effect wrapper merely to use those functional operations.\n\nThe rule is syntax/import-based. Add a TaxKit correction only for an evidenced\ngap, with the owner and actual tool capability established first. Retain and\nqualify native Map/Set/WeakMap/WeakSet, mutable built-in/class/contract values,\nObject/Reflect writes, local/destructured aliases and runtime reference checks\nthrough the relevant existing rules, readonly types and focused additions.\nComputed member access is already rejected by `no-unchecked-index`; do not\npresent it as an admitted combined-baseline escape.\n`Ref.set` and native mutable `Map.set` are different operations; a method-name\nsearch alone does not establish their identity. Each correction must reject\nits bad fixture without rejecting a valid persistent collection, Effect-managed\nstate update or qualified Alchemy Output operation.\n\nActual-command fixtures must cover every owned path group, including moved\napps, nested packages, JavaScript policy tools, tests and configuration. Assert\nthe admitted file count, exit code and expected rule. Exact `allowedAssignments`\nand `allowedMethods` options name a file and the single target/receiver/method;\nno parent path, glob or whole-file exception. Prove nearby mutations remain\nrejected and that removing/disabling a required rule or broadening an exception\nfails the verifier. Readonly types and the selected Effect diagnostics cover\nthe type side; structural review covers helper purpose, Schema ownership and\ncall-graph simplicity. Do not present lint as proof of all semantic requirements.\n\nPreserve and qualify the stronger existing TaxKit lexical checks when merging\nthe portable plugin. Runtime operations used as references/callbacks, such as\npassing `Effect.runPromise` to a pipe, must be rejected outside the exact host\nowner as well as direct calls. Prove renamed imports, namespace aliases,\nre-exports, shadowed names and callback references; a CallExpression-only check\nis insufficient. Primitive host adapters cannot become a generic `run`\nescape for arbitrary callers.\n{\n  \"name\": \"@taxkit/docs-content\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.3\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \"./errors\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/errors.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/errors.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/errors.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./live\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./generated-source\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/generated-source.layer.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/generated-source.layer.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/generated-source.layer.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./server\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/server.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/server.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/server.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./client\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/client.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/client.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/client.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./schemas\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/schemas.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/schemas.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/schemas.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./service\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/service.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/service.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/service.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./test\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./validate\": {\n      \"types\": \"./src/validate.runtime.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/validate.runtime.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/validate.runtime.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./source.config\": \"./source.config.ts\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"bun run generate\",\n    \"check-examples\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.examples.json --noEmit\",\n    \"check-types\": \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/docs-fumadocs build && tsc --noEmit && bun run check-examples\",\n    \"generate\": \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/docs-fumadocs build && fumadocs-mdx\",\n    \"test\": \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/docs-fumadocs build && vitest run --passWithNoTests\",\n    \"validate\": \"bun run ./src/validate.runtime.ts\",\n    \"clean\": \"rm -rf .source .turbo *.tsbuildinfo\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@effect/platform-bun\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@effect/platform-node\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@taxkit/docs-fumadocs\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"effect\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"fumadocs-core\": \"16.16.0\",\n    \"fumadocs-mdx\": \"15.4.6\",\n    \"yaml\": \"2.9.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@effect/vitest\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@taxkit/api-http\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/calculators\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/core\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/rules-au-pay\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/sdk\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@types/bun\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"typescript\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vite\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vitest\": \"catalog:\"\n  }\n}\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\";\n\nexport const DocsNonEmptyText = Schema.Trimmed.check(Schema.isMinLength(1));\nexport type DocsNonEmptyText = typeof DocsNonEmptyText.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPagePath = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\n  Schema.brand(\"taxkit/DocsPagePath\")\n);\nexport type DocsPagePath = typeof DocsPagePath.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPageSlug = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\n  Schema.brand(\"taxkit/DocsPageSlug\")\n);\nexport type DocsPageSlug = typeof DocsPageSlug.Type;\n\nexport const DocsSourcePath = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\n  Schema.brand(\"taxkit/DocsSourcePath\")\n);\nexport type DocsSourcePath = typeof DocsSourcePath.Type;\n\nexport const DocsContentStatus = Schema.Literals([\"draft\", \"published\"]);\nexport type DocsContentStatus = typeof DocsContentStatus.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPageFrontmatter = Schema.Struct({\n  description: DocsNonEmptyText,\n  status: DocsContentStatus,\n  title: DocsNonEmptyText,\n});\nexport type DocsPageFrontmatter = typeof DocsPageFrontmatter.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPageType = Schema.Literals([\n  \"api reference overview\",\n  \"changelog or release note\",\n  \"concept\",\n  \"contribution guide\",\n  \"decision page\",\n  \"guide\",\n  \"quickstart\",\n  \"reference\",\n  \"section index\",\n  \"troubleshooting\",\n]);\nexport type DocsPageType = typeof DocsPageType.Type;\n\nexport const DocsPrimaryReader = Schema.Literals([\n  \"API consumer\",\n  \"Application integrator\",\n  \"Correctness reviewer\",\n  \"Documentation contributor\",\n  \"New contributor\",\n  \"SDK evaluator\",\n  \"Type-safety focused developer\",\n]);\nexport type DocsPrimaryReader = typeof DocsPrimaryReader.Type;\n\nexport const DocsNavigationLeaf = Schema.Struct({\n  pageType: DocsPageType,\n  path: DocsPagePath,\n  primaryReader: DocsPrimaryReader,\n  source: DocsSourcePath,\n  title: DocsNonEmptyText,\n});\nexport type DocsNavigationLeaf = typeof DocsNavigationLeaf.Type;\n\nexport const DocsNavigationItem = Schema.Struct({\n  ...DocsNavigationLeaf.fields,\n  pages: Schema.optional(Schema.Array(DocsNavigationLeaf)),\n});\nexport type DocsNavigationItem = typeof DocsNavigationItem.Type;\n\nexport const DocsNavigation = Schema.Struct({\n  $schema: Schema.optional(Schema.String),\n  contentRoot: Schema.Literal(\"packages/docs-content/content\"),\n  primaryNavigation: Schema.Array(DocsNavigationItem),\n  status: DocsContentStatus,\n});\nexport type DocsNavigation = typeof DocsNavigation.Type;\n\nexport const DocsMeta = Schema.Struct({\n  collapsible: Schema.optional(Schema.Boolean),\n  defaultOpen: Schema.optional(Schema.Boolean),\n  description: Schema.optional(DocsNonEmptyText),\n  icon: Schema.optional(Schema.String),\n  pages: Schema.optional(Schema.mutable(Schema.Array(Schema.String))),\n  root: Schema.optional(Schema.Boolean),\n  title: Schema.optional(DocsNonEmptyText),\n});\nexport type DocsMeta = typeof DocsMeta.Type;\n\nexport const DocsMdxComponentName = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\n  Schema.check(\n    Schema.isPattern(/^[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*(?:\\.[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*)*$/u)\n  ),\n  Schema.brand(\"taxkit/DocsMdxComponentName\")\n);\nexport type DocsMdxComponentName = typeof DocsMdxComponentName.Type;\n\nexport const DocsContentPage = Schema.Struct({\n  frontmatter: DocsPageFrontmatter,\n  markdown: Schema.String,\n  path: DocsPagePath,\n  slugs: Schema.Array(DocsPageSlug),\n  source: DocsSourcePath,\n});\nexport type DocsContentPage = typeof DocsContentPage.Type;\n\nexport class DocsValidationIssue extends Schema.TaggedClass<DocsValidationIssue>()(\n  \"DocsValidationIssue\",\n  {\n    message: DocsNonEmptyText,\n    path: Schema.Array(Schema.String),\n  }\n) {}\n\nexport const DocsValidationResult = Schema.Struct({\n  issues: Schema.Array(DocsValidationIssue),\n});\nexport type DocsValidationResult = typeof DocsValidationResult.Type;\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"./navigation.schema.json\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"contentRoot\": \"packages/docs-content/content\",\n  \"primaryNavigation\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Start\",\n      \"path\": \"/start\",\n      \"source\": \"content/start/index.mdx\",\n      \"pageType\": \"section index\",\n      \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\",\n      \"pages\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Overview\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/overview\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/overview.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"section index\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Quickstart\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/quickstart\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/quickstart.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"quickstart\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Install the SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/install-the-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/install-the-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Run your first calculation\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/run-your-first-calculation\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/run-your-first-calculation.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Choose SDK or HTTP API\",\n          \"path\": \"/start/choose-sdk-or-api\",\n          \"source\": \"content/start/choose-sdk-or-api.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"decision page\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Application integrator\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"SDK\",\n      \"path\": \"/sdk\",\n      \"source\": \"content/sdk/index.mdx\",\n      \"pageType\": \"section index\",\n      \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\",\n      \"pages\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"TypeScript SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/typescript-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/typescript-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"concept\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"SDK evaluator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Plain SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/plain-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/plain-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Application integrator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Safe SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/safe-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/safe-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Application integrator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Effect SDK\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/effect-sdk\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/effect-sdk.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"guide\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Application integrator\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Schemas\",\n          \"path\": \"/sdk/schemas\",\n          \"source\": \"content/sdk/schemas.mdx\",\n          \"pageType\": \"reference\",\n          \"primaryReader\": \"Type-safety focused developer\"\napps/web/src/routes/agents.tsx\napps/web/src/routes/calculators.$calculatorId.tsx\napps/web/src/routes/__root.tsx\napps/web/src/routes/index.tsx\n"},"started_at_ms":1791271484858,"completed_at_ms":1791271484858}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T07:24:44.904Z","ordinal":40177,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","session_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","root_turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","response_id":"resp_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac4a232e07487d0b934a8096337d1cf","usage":{"input_tokens":120525,"cached_input_tokens":117760,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":244,"reasoning_output_tokens":149,"total_tokens":120769},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":29195864,"cached_input_tokens":28353664,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":122584,"reasoning_output_tokens":37978,"total_tokens":29318448},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":773399037,"cached_input_tokens":757389952,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3627588,"reasoning_output_tokens":1520397,"total_tokens":777026625}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T07:24:44.909Z","ordinal":40178,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a11019-bded-76d2-8643-49ce75073bd7","call_id":"call_i7HR8L0wDEu94oNmAEDTgAQ9","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"cf7aa0\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000006584,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":4107,\"output\":\"  bounded arrays or persistent Effect collections. Do not expose a mutable\\n  array, native Map/Set/WeakMap/WeakSet, Date, SDK object or mutable reference as\\n  a domain value.\\n  Do not use casts or shallow freezing as a substitute for this contract.\\n- Express transformations with pure Effect collection mapping/folding;\\n  express workflows with named Effects and combinators. No `for`, `for...in`,\\n  `for...of`, `while`, `do...while` or native array traversal, including native\\n  `forEach`, in owned code. Pure array work uses Effect Array functions directly;\\n  use scoped, bounded Effect traversal/repetition where work really repeats.\\n- Prefer a pipe for a clear linear data flow. Use flat `Effect.gen` with\\n  immutable bindings when dependencies or several sequential steps make that\\n  clearer. Neither syntax permits raw work, mutation, hidden branching or\\n  helper chains that obscure the operation.\\n- Expected failures stay in tagged error channels and are handled exhaustively\\n  with Effect/Match and Option/Result's matching APIs. No `switch`, manual\\n  `_tag` comparisons, thrown expected errors, `try`/`catch`, manual Promise\\n  control flow, manual unknown probing or nullable domain state.\\n- Pure deterministic calculations and rendering remain total plain functions.\\n  Do not wrap constants or safe leaf transformations in ceremonial Effects,\\n  or construct a service/Layer for every helper.\\n\\nNecessary changing state belongs to the narrowest explicit owner: React for\\nlocal synchronous input/display state; Effect Atom for browser work; or scoped\\nRef/Queue/Cache/Semaphore/transaction facilities inside a named Layer where\\ntheir semantics are needed. Values held in those owners remain immutable;\\nupdates are pure and atomic, and no underlying mutable reference escapes.\\nThere is no claim that React, Effect, the host or a vendor SDK has no internal\\nstate. Prove route/request/instance lifetime, concurrent updates, interruption\\nand disposal rather than hiding state in module globals. Calculation facts and\\nreports get no persistence or cache; accepted public content may have an\\nexplicit bounded cache policy.\\n\\nThe current skill permits measured private native data structures and genuine\\nhost requirements, and no longer treats a total leaf as permission for local\\nmutation. TaxKit's stronger requirement admits only a host-imposed primitive\\nin a named outer adapter with an exact construct, containment, owner, test and\\nremoval condition. Grant only the\\nconstruct that the host needs; a Promise-returning adapter exception does not\\npermit nearby mutation, loops, SDK leakage or a nested runtime. Generated,\\nvendor and reference templates have explicit provenance and exclusions; runnable owned policy code\\nand tests remain covered. A performance preference alone cannot silently relax\\nCooper's immutable/declarative requirement.\\n\\nExtract an operation only when it owns stable policy, external work or a\\nresource lifetime, or has a real independent reuse/substitution point. Each\\nextraction needs its semantic owner and simpler call graph. Keep one-use\\ndecoding, mapping, error projection and matching inline. Ban dumping-ground\\n`helpers`, `utils`, `common` and `shared` modules; naming a wrapper as a service\\ndoes not give it semantic weight. Review the actual call graph in every slice.\\n\\nAdopt the current 0.6.1 portable strict Effect policy at its repository-owned\\ncanonical skill asset. Merge into `oxlint.config.ts` and retain useful existing TaxKit,\\nMDX and workspace checks. Enable `strict-effect/no-unchecked-index`,\\n`no-native-at`, `runtime-file-convention`, `tagged-error-name`,\\n`error-constructor-new`, `no-promise-workflow`, `no-unsafe-option-unwrap`,\\n`no-unchecked-json`, `no-runtime-outside-boundary`, `no-native-work` and\\n`no-imperative-collections` under that plugin. Keep assertions/any, raw fetch/JSON/environment, ambient\\ntime/random/timers, console telemetry and native mutable collections restricted\\nacross owned source, tests, tools, infrastructure and configuration. Exact host\\nadapters get only their necessary exception; generated/vendor exclusions are\\nexplicit. Pure local rendering and deterministic computations remain direct.\\nCover owned `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`, `.mjs` and `.cjs` execution paths, not\\nonly the scaffold's TypeScript override. Convert retained JavaScript policy\\ntools to checked TypeScript where needed; do not leave them outside enforcement\\nbecause their extension differs. Validate executable MDX expressions/imports\\nthrough the existing content-policy owner; fenced documentation examples are\\nrepresentation content, not hidden executable source.\\n\\nThe earlier 0.5.1 plugin lacked local mutation and loop checks. Its installed\\n0.6.0 successor now supplies `no-imperative-collections`: use that canonical\\nrule instead of creating duplicate mutable-binding/reassignment/loop rules.\\nIt rejects loops, `let`/`var`, assignments, updates, deletion, native array\\ntraversal/mutators/constructors, transient Effect collection modes, `switch`\\nand manual `_tag` decisions. Imported Effect functional collection operations\\nand native Alchemy Output transformations remain valid. Ordinary pure work\\nneeds no Effect wrapper merely to use those functional operations.\\n\\nThe rule is syntax/import-based. Add a TaxKit correction only for an evidenced\\ngap, with the owner and actual tool capability established first. Retain and\\nqualify native Map/Set/WeakMap/WeakSet, mutable built-in/class/contract values,\\nObject/Reflect writes, local/destructured aliases and runtime reference checks\\nthrough the relevant existing rules, readonly types and focused additions.\\nComputed member access is already rejected by `no-unchecked-index`; do not\\npresent it as an admitted combined-baseline escape.\\n`Ref.set` and native mutable `Map.set` are different operations; a method-name\\nsearch alone does not establish their identity. Each correction must reject\\nits bad fixture without rejecting a valid persistent collection, Effect-managed\\nstate update or qualified Alchemy Output operation.\\n\\nActual-command fixtures must cover every owned path group, including moved\\napps, nested packages, JavaScript policy tools, tests and configuration. Assert\\nthe admitted file count, exit code and expected rule. Exact `allowedAssignments`\\nand `allowedMethods` options name a file and the single target/receiver/method;\\nno parent path, glob or whole-file exception. Prove nearby mutations remain\\nrejected and that removing/disabling a required rule or broadening an exception\\nfails the verifier. Readonly types and the selected Effect diagnostics cover\\nthe type side; structural review covers helper purpose, Schema ownership and\\ncall-graph simplicity. Do not present lint as proof of all semantic requirements.\\n\\nPreserve and qualify the stronger existing TaxKit lexical checks when merging\\nthe portable plugin. Runtime operations used as references/callbacks, such as\\npassing `Effect.runPromise` to a pipe, must be rejected outside the exact host\\nowner as well as direct calls. Prove renamed imports, namespace aliases,\\nre-exports, shadowed names and callback references; a CallExpression-only check\\nis insufficient. Primitive host adapters cannot become a generic `run`\\nescape for arbitrary callers.\\n{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"@taxkit/docs-content\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.3\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n  \\\"exports\\\": {\\n    \\\"./errors\\\": {\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./src/errors.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/errors.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./src/errors.ts\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./live\\\": {\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./src/live.layer.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/live.layer.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./src/live.layer.ts\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./generated-source\\\": {\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./src/generated-source.layer.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/generated-source.layer.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./src/generated-source.layer.ts\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./server\\\": {\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./src/server.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/server.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./src/server.ts\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./client\\\": {\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./src/client.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/client.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./src/client.ts\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./schemas\\\": {\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./src/schemas.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/schemas.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./src/schemas.ts\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./service\\\": {\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./src/service.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/service.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./src/service.ts\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./test\\\": {\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./src/test.layer.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/test.layer.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./src/test.layer.ts\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./validate\\\": {\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./src/validate.runtime.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/validate.runtime.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./src/validate.runtime.ts\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./source.config\\\": \\\"./source.config.ts\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"bun run generate\\\",\\n    \\\"check-examples\\\": \\\"tsc -p tsconfig.examples.json --noEmit\\\",\\n    \\\"check-types\\\": \\\"bun run --filter=@taxkit/docs-fumadocs build && tsc --noEmit && bun run check-examples\\\",\\n    \\\"generate\\\": \\\"bun run --filter=@taxkit/docs-fumadocs build && fumadocs-mdx\\\",\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"bun run --filter=@taxkit/docs-fumadocs build && vitest run --passWithNoTests\\\",\\n    \\\"validate\\\": \\\"bun run ./src/validate.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"clean\\\": \\\"rm -rf .source .turbo *.tsbuildinfo\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@effect/platform-bun\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@effect/platform-node\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/docs-fumadocs\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"effect\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"fumadocs-core\\\": \\\"16.16.0\\\",\\n    \\\"fumadocs-mdx\\\": \\\"15.4.6\\\",\\n    \\\"yaml\\\": \\\"2.9.1\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"devDependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@effect/vitest\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/api-http\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/calculators\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/core\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/rules-au-pay\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/sdk\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@types/bun\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"typescript\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"vite\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"vitest\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\nimport { Schema } from \\\"effect\\\";\\n\\nexport const DocsNonEmptyText = Schema.Trimmed.check(Schema.isMinLength(1));\\nexport type DocsNonEmptyText = typeof DocsNonEmptyText.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsPagePath = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\\n  Schema.brand(\\\"taxkit/DocsPagePath\\\")\\n);\\nexport type DocsPagePath = typeof DocsPagePath.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsPageSlug = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\\n  Schema.brand(\\\"taxkit/DocsPageSlug\\\")\\n);\\nexport type DocsPageSlug = typeof DocsPageSlug.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsSourcePath = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\\n  Schema.brand(\\\"taxkit/DocsSourcePath\\\")\\n);\\nexport type DocsSourcePath = typeof DocsSourcePath.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsContentStatus = Schema.Literals([\\\"draft\\\", \\\"published\\\"]);\\nexport type DocsContentStatus = typeof DocsContentStatus.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsPageFrontmatter = Schema.Struct({\\n  description: DocsNonEmptyText,\\n  status: DocsContentStatus,\\n  title: DocsNonEmptyText,\\n});\\nexport type DocsPageFrontmatter = typeof DocsPageFrontmatter.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsPageType = Schema.Literals([\\n  \\\"api reference overview\\\",\\n  \\\"changelog or release note\\\",\\n  \\\"concept\\\",\\n  \\\"contribution guide\\\",\\n  \\\"decision page\\\",\\n  \\\"guide\\\",\\n  \\\"quickstart\\\",\\n  \\\"reference\\\",\\n  \\\"section index\\\",\\n  \\\"troubleshooting\\\",\\n]);\\nexport type DocsPageType = typeof DocsPageType.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsPrimaryReader = Schema.Literals([\\n  \\\"API consumer\\\",\\n  \\\"Application integrator\\\",\\n  \\\"Correctness reviewer\\\",\\n  \\\"Documentation contributor\\\",\\n  \\\"New contributor\\\",\\n  \\\"SDK evaluator\\\",\\n  \\\"Type-safety focused developer\\\",\\n]);\\nexport type DocsPrimaryReader = typeof DocsPrimaryReader.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsNavigationLeaf = Schema.Struct({\\n  pageType: DocsPageType,\\n  path: DocsPagePath,\\n  primaryReader: DocsPrimaryReader,\\n  source: DocsSourcePath,\\n  title: DocsNonEmptyText,\\n});\\nexport type DocsNavigationLeaf = typeof DocsNavigationLeaf.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsNavigationItem = Schema.Struct({\\n  ...DocsNavigationLeaf.fields,\\n  pages: Schema.optional(Schema.Array(DocsNavigationLeaf)),\\n});\\nexport type DocsNavigationItem = typeof DocsNavigationItem.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsNavigation = Schema.Struct({\\n  $schema: Schema.optional(Schema.String),\\n  contentRoot: Schema.Literal(\\\"packages/docs-content/content\\\"),\\n  primaryNavigation: Schema.Array(DocsNavigationItem),\\n  status: DocsContentStatus,\\n});\\nexport type DocsNavigation = typeof DocsNavigation.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsMeta = Schema.Struct({\\n  collapsible: Schema.optional(Schema.Boolean),\\n  defaultOpen: Schema.optional(Schema.Boolean),\\n  description: Schema.optional(DocsNonEmptyText),\\n  icon: Schema.optional(Schema.String),\\n  pages: Schema.optional(Schema.mutable(Schema.Array(Schema.String))),\\n  root: Schema.optional(Schema.Boolean),\\n  title: Schema.optional(DocsNonEmptyText),\\n});\\nexport type DocsMeta = typeof DocsMeta.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsMdxComponentName = DocsNonEmptyText.pipe(\\n  Schema.check(\\n    Schema.isPattern(/^[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*(?:\\\\.[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*)*$/u)\\n  ),\\n  Schema.brand(\\\"taxkit/DocsMdxComponentName\\\")\\n);\\nexport type DocsMdxComponentName = typeof DocsMdxComponentName.Type;\\n\\nexport const DocsContentPage = Schema.Struct({\\n  frontmatter: DocsPageFrontmatter,\\n  markdown: Schema.String,\\n  path: DocsPagePath,\\n  slugs: Schema.Array(DocsPageSlug),\\n  source: DocsSourcePath,\\n});\\nexport type DocsContentPage = typeof DocsContentPage.Type;\\n\\nexport class DocsValidationIssue extends Schema.TaggedClass<DocsValidationIssue>()(\\n  \\\"DocsValidationIssue\\\",\\n  {\\n    message: DocsNonEmptyText,\\n    path: Schema.Array(Schema.String),\\n  }\\n) {}\\n\\nexport const DocsValidationResult = Schema.Struct({\\n  issues: Schema.Array(DocsValidationIssue),\\n});\\nexport type DocsValidationResult = typeof DocsValidationResult.Type;\\n{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"./navigation.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"draft\\\",\\n  \\\"contentRoot\\\": \\\"packages/docs-content/content\\\",\\n  \\\"primaryNavigation\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Start\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/start\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"content/start/index.mdx\\\",\\n      \\\"pageType\\\": \\\"section index\\\",\\n      \\\"primaryReader\\\": \\\"SDK evaluator\\\",\\n      \\\"pages\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Overview\\\",\\n          \\\"path\\\": \\\"/start/overview\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"content/start/overview.mdx\\\",\\n          \\\"pageType\\\": \\\"section index\\\",\\n          \\\"primaryReader\\\": \\\"SDK evaluator\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Quickstart\\\",\\n          \\\"path\\\": \\\"/start/quickstart\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"content/start/quickstart.mdx\\\",\\n          \\\"pageType\\\": \\\"quickstart\\\",\\n          \\\"primaryReader\\\": \\\"SDK evaluator\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Install the SDK\\\",\\n          \\\"path\\\": \\\"/start/install-the-sdk\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"content/start/install-the-sdk.mdx\\\",\\n          \\\"pageType\\\": \\\"guide\\\",\\n          \\\"primaryReader\\\": \\\"SDK evaluator\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Run your first calculation\\\",\\n          \\\"path\\\": \\\"/start/run-your-first-calculation\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"content/start/run-your-first-calculation.mdx\\\",\\n          \\\"pageType\\\": \\\"guide\\\",\\n          \\\"primaryReader\\\": \\\"SDK evaluator\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Choose SDK or HTTP API\\\",\\n          \\\"path\\\": \\\"/start/choose-sdk-or-api\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"content/start/choose-sdk-or-api.mdx\\\",\\n          \\\"pageType\\\": \\\"decision page\\\",\\n          \\\"primaryReader\\\": \\\"Application integrator\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"SDK\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/sdk\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"content/sdk/index.mdx\\\",\\n      \\\"pageType\\\": \\\"section index\\\",\\n      \\\"primaryReader\\\": \\\"SDK evaluator\\\",\\n      \\\"pages\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"TypeScript SDK\\\",\\n          \\\"path\\\": \\\"/sdk/typescript-sdk\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"content/sdk/typescript-sdk.mdx\\\",\\n          \\\"pageType\\\": \\\"concept\\\",\\n          \\\"primaryReader\\\