on,\\n  onNavigate,\\n  onToggle,\\n  open,\\n}: Readonly<{\\n  currentPath: DocsContentPage[\\\"path\\\"];\\n  interactive: boolean;\\n  navigation: DocsNavigationValue;\\n  onNavigate: () => void;\\n  onToggle: () => void;\\n  open: boolean;\\n}>) => (\\n  <>\\n    <header className=\\\"docs-mobile-header\\\">\\n      <Link className=\\\"docs-nav__home\\\" to=\\\"/\\\">\\n        TaxKit Docs\\n      </Link>\\n      <button\\n        aria-controls=\\\"docs-navigation\\\"\\n        aria-expanded={open}\\n        className=\\\"docs-nav-toggle\\\"\\n        onClick={onToggle}\\n        type=\\\"button\\\"\\n      >\\n        {open ? \\\"Close navigation\\\" : \\\"Open navigation\\\"}\\n      </button>\\n    </header>\\n    <nav\\n      aria-label=\\\"Documentation\\\"\\n      className=\\\"docs-nav\\\"\\n      data-open={open}\\n      data-tk-navigation-interactive={interactive ? \\\"true\\\" : \\\"false\\\"}\\n---\\ntitle: \\\"Overview\\\"\\ndescription: \\\"Learn where to start with the TaxKit SDK and HTTP API.\\\"\\nstatus: \\\"draft\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Overview\\n\\nUse TaxKit when you need source-backed tax calculations from TypeScript or\\nover HTTP. Start with the TypeScript SDK when your application can import\\nTaxKit packages. Use the HTTP API when the caller is a browser, another\\nlanguage or a service boundary that should not run the SDK in-process.\\n\\n## Choose your first path\\n\\n| You need to                                          | Start with                                        |\\n| ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Run one calculation from TypeScript                  | [Quickstart](./quickstart.mdx)                    |\\n| Add TaxKit to a server application                   | [Plain SDK](../sdk/plain-sdk.mdx)                 |\\n| Return typed success or failure values               | [Safe SDK](../sdk/safe-sdk.mdx)                   |\\n| Compose TaxKit inside an Effect application          | [Effect SDK](../sdk/effect-sdk.mdx)               |\\n| Call TaxKit from a browser or non-TypeScript service | [Choose SDK or HTTP API](./choose-sdk-or-api.mdx) |\\n\\n## How the public surfaces fit\\n\\n```ts\\nProduction: public integration surfaces\\n\\nTypeScript application\\n  -> @taxkit/sdk plain facade\\n    -> calculator service\\n\\nEffect application or in-process transport\\n  -> @taxkit/sdk/effect\\n    -> calculator service\\n\\nBrowser or non-TypeScript caller\\n  -> HTTP API\\n    -> @taxkit/sdk/effect\\n      -> calculator service\\n```\\n\\nThe SDK and API use the same calculator-owned schemas and branded values. This\\nkeeps request validation, calculator reports and expected errors aligned across\\nsurfaces.\\n\\n## Current release status\\n\\nThe TypeScript SDK package is still private until release approval. The docs\\nshow the intended public package shape and the current workspace exports.\\n\\n## Next steps\\n\\n- Run your first calculation with the [quickstart](./quickstart.mdx).\\n- Compare integration surfaces in [Choose SDK or HTTP API](./choose-sdk-or-api.mdx).\\n- Read the [TypeScript SDK](../sdk/typescript-sdk.mdx) page for the SDK surface.\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f","create_time":1791272742.636539}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
