,\"id\":8}); Total lines: 85\nL0: cite0†Fumadocs L1: \nL2: cite0†Fumadocs L3: \nL4: Search\nL5: \nL6: `⌘``K`\nL7: \nL8: Fumadocs MDX\nL9: \nL10: The official content source\nL11: \nL12: Guide\nL13: \nL14: cite1†Getting Started cite2†Performance L15: \nL16: cite3†Accessing Collections L17: \nL18: cite4†Macro API L19: \nL20: Integrations\nL21: \nL22: cite5†Next.js cite6†Vite L23: \nL24: cite7†Runtime Loader L25: \nL26: cite8†Bun cite9†Node.js L27: \nL28: Configuration\nL29: \nL30: cite10†Collections cite11†Global Options cite12†MDX Presets L31: \nL32: Features\nL33: \nL34: cite13†Include cite14†Last Modified Time cite15†Lazy Loading cite16†Generate Types cite17†Workspace L35: \nL36: Bun\nL37: \nL38: cite7†Runtime Loader L39: \nL40: # Bun\nL41: \nL42: Access content in Bun.\nL43: \nL44: Copy Markdown Open\nL45: ## cite18†Setup L46: \nL47: Register the plugin in preload script:\nL48: \nL49: bunfig.toml\nL50: \nL51: scripts/preload.ts\nL52: \nL53:     `preload = [\"./scripts/preload.ts\"]`\nL54: \nL55: It will add support for loading MDX/meta files on runtime.\nL56: \nL57: Now running any script with Bun, you can access your content files directly.\nL58: ### cite19†Re-generate `.source` folder L59: \nL60: Optionally, you can re-generate the `.source` folder.\nL61: \nL62: It is useful when the folder could be missing, or you are using Vite, which defaults to generating code with Vite-specific APIs.\nL63: \nL64: Next.js\nL65: \nL66: Vite\nL67: \nL68: preload.ts\nL69: \nL70:     `import { postInstall } from 'fumadocs-mdx/next';\nL71: \nL72:     await postInstall({ configPath: 'source.config.ts' });`\nL73: \nL74: How is this guide?\nL75: \nL76: Good Bad\nL77: \nL78: Last updated on\nL79: cite7†Runtime Loader Fumadocs MDX loader integration. cite9†Node.js Access content in Node.js runtime. L80: ### On this page\nL81: \nL82: cite18†Setup cite19†Re-generate `.source` folder L83: \nL84: Ask AI\n"}],"in